{"type":"text","timestamp":1778872694253,"sessionID":"ses_1d2ee29dbffeDS6MAKCPHUbUS7","part":{"id":"prt_e2d132e6e001wxM08lcuJGfybS","messageID":"msg_e2d12ee62001ns8SfvtId6Q7ZV","sessionID":"ses_1d2ee29dbffeDS6MAKCPHUbUS7","type":"text","text":"I found a distinct micro-opt that hasn’t been proposed yet: canonicalize unused `rs1/rs2` fields in ID, then use those true source-use bits for the load-use interlock. That directly addresses the `r4s0` failure mode without pulling in late store-data plumbing.","time":{"start":1778872692334,"end":1778872694253},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_02f8fa21a50b758c016a0771743994819ba931418c0cb18602","phase":"commentary"}}}}
