{"type":"text","timestamp":1778872786051,"sessionID":"ses_1d2ee29dbffeDS6MAKCPHUbUS7","part":{"id":"prt_e2d149c2a001U7Hlf921jFMa2V","messageID":"msg_e2d143a9a001OOPXYDaYw7ND9t","sessionID":"ses_1d2ee29dbffeDS6MAKCPHUbUS7","type":"text","text":"Writing the hypothesis file now. It targets decode-time source canonicalization plus a tighter load-use interlock, because that’s the cleanest untried micro-opt that follows the `r4s0` lesson instead of repeating the failed late-store-data path.","time":{"start":1778872785962,"end":1778872786050},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_031bea926aef19bc016a0771d1c9788198b81d23bc624befbe","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778872798782,"sessionID":"ses_1d2ee29dbffeDS6MAKCPHUbUS7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_LprmASocVxNKt1hSuzpOUdl3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r10s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r10s0\n+title: \"Canonical Decode Source Operands\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current load-use interlock keys off raw IF/ID bitfields, not the\n+  operands a legal instruction will actually consume. That means single-source\n+  or zero-source instructions can still alias an older load's `rd` through\n+  unused immediate bits and burn a bubble. The `r4s0` failure showed why a\n+  direct hazard rewrite was unsafe: `bench` currently carries those raw source\n+  fields into RVFI, so any safe relaxation has to start by canonicalizing the\n+  architectural source view.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Teach decode which source operands are architecturally live for each\n+  validated opcode/funct form, and canonicalize unused sources to `x0` before\n+  the regfile, hazard unit, and RVFI pipeline state ever see them. In\n+  practice, OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, and EBREAK would stop\n+  advertising bogus `rs2` or `rs1` aliases, while R-type, BRANCH, STORE, and\n+  other true consumers keep their existing source fields.\n+\n+  Then drive the existing load-use detector from those canonical source\n+  addresses instead of raw `instr[19:15]` / `instr[24:20]`. This stays off the\n+  fragile fetch-target and MEM-store paths, removes false dependency bubbles,\n+  and makes RVFI source reporting semantically accurate instead of \"whatever\n+  bits happened to live in the encoding.\"\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Add conservative `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` outputs that only clear unused sources inside validated opcode/funct matches, mirroring the existing illegal-default discipline.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Canonicalize regfile read addresses and latched `rs*_addr` fields from the decoder's source-use bits so unused operands become x0/0 before they feed EX or RVFI.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Feed `hazard_unit` from ID's canonical source addresses instead of raw IF/ID instruction bits, preserving the current interlock structure while removing false load-use aliases.\"\n+  - file: test/test_decoder.py\n+    description: \"Add unit coverage for per-op source-use classification, especially OP-IMM/LOAD/JALR/JAL/LUI/AUIPC/FENCE/EBREAK versus true two-source ops.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add an end-to-end alias case where a legal single-source instruction's immediate bits match an older load destination and verify no extra bubble plus canonical RVFI `rs*_addr` / `rs*_rdata` reporting.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r10s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r10s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r10s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r10s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r10s0\n+title: \"Canonical Decode Source Operands\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current load-use interlock keys off raw IF/ID bitfields, not the\n+  operands a legal instruction will actually consume. That means single-source\n+  or zero-source instructions can still alias an older load's `rd` through\n+  unused immediate bits and burn a bubble. The `r4s0` failure showed why a\n+  direct hazard rewrite was unsafe: `bench` currently carries those raw source\n+  fields into RVFI, so any safe relaxation has to start by canonicalizing the\n+  architectural source view.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Teach decode which source operands are architecturally live for each\n+  validated opcode/funct form, and canonicalize unused sources to `x0` before\n+  the regfile, hazard unit, and RVFI pipeline state ever see them. In\n+  practice, OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, and EBREAK would stop\n+  advertising bogus `rs2` or `rs1` aliases, while R-type, BRANCH, STORE, and\n+  other true consumers keep their existing source fields.\n+\n+  Then drive the existing load-use detector from those canonical source\n+  addresses instead of raw `instr[19:15]` / `instr[24:20]`. This stays off the\n+  fragile fetch-target and MEM-store paths, removes false dependency bubbles,\n+  and makes RVFI source reporting semantically accurate instead of \"whatever\n+  bits happened to live in the encoding.\"\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Add conservative `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` outputs that only clear unused sources inside validated opcode/funct matches, mirroring the existing illegal-default discipline.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Canonicalize regfile read addresses and latched `rs*_addr` fields from the decoder's source-use bits so unused operands become x0/0 before they feed EX or RVFI.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Feed `hazard_unit` from ID's canonical source addresses instead of raw IF/ID instruction bits, preserving the current interlock structure while removing false load-use aliases.\"\n+  - file: test/test_decoder.py\n+    description: \"Add unit coverage for per-op source-use classification, especially OP-IMM/LOAD/JALR/JAL/LUI/AUIPC/FENCE/EBREAK versus true two-source ops.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add an end-to-end alias case where a legal single-source instruction's immediate bits match an older load destination and verify no extra bubble plus canonical RVFI `rs*_addr` / `rs*_rdata` reporting.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r10s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r10s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r10s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r10s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r10s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r10s0\n+title: \"Canonical Decode Source Operands\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current load-use interlock keys off raw IF/ID bitfields, not the\n+  operands a legal instruction will actually consume. That means single-source\n+  or zero-source instructions can still alias an older load's `rd` through\n+  unused immediate bits and burn a bubble. The `r4s0` failure showed why a\n+  direct hazard rewrite was unsafe: `bench` currently carries those raw source\n+  fields into RVFI, so any safe relaxation has to start by canonicalizing the\n+  architectural source view.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Teach decode which source operands are architecturally live for each\n+  validated opcode/funct form, and canonicalize unused sources to `x0` before\n+  the regfile, hazard unit, and RVFI pipeline state ever see th