{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778874726147,"sessionID":"ses_1d2d0d46affeDQJGIeMWOEYdBs","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_NgPRFJCgK3TRCSXHPc7xjqe3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r11s0\n+title: \"Hazard-Only Live Source Filtering\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  `bench` still detects load-use hazards from raw IF/ID bitfields, so\n+  instructions that do not architecturally read `rs2` or `rs1` can alias an\n+  older load destination through immediate bits and take an unnecessary bubble.\n+  The prior broad hazard-relaxation attempts failed because they also changed\n+  architected source accounting or touched the late STORE-data path; the\n+  backend-only opportunity itself is still there.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Keep RVFI-visible `rs1_addr` / `rs2_addr` and the existing load->STORE-data\n+  policy unchanged, but make the interlock smarter about which IF/ID sources\n+  are actually live for hazard purposes. In `hazard_unit`, derive conservative\n+  `uses_rs1_hazard` / `uses_rs2_hazard` bits from the younger instruction's\n+  opcode/funct form and ignore only the source fields that are provably unused\n+  in EX for legal encodings such as OP-IMM, LOAD, JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, and\n+  EBREAK. Leave STORE `rs2`, BRANCH, R-type, and unknown/illegal encodings\n+  conservative.\n+\n+  This targets IPC with almost no new datapath or fetch-path work: it removes\n+  false load-use bubbles caused by immediate-field aliases while avoiding the\n+  correctness pitfalls that broke the earlier stage-accurate and\n+  canonicalized-source attempts.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Replace raw rs-field load-use checks with conservative hazard-only live-source qualification, while keeping STORE rs2 and unknown encodings conservative.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add false-alias load-use tests showing OP-IMM/JAL/LUI/AUIPC/FENCE/EBREAK no longer stall when only immediate bits match an older load rd.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r11s0\n+title: \"Hazard-Only Live Source Filtering\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  `bench` still detects load-use hazards from raw IF/ID bitfields, so\n+  instructions that do not architecturally read `rs2` or `rs1` can alias an\n+  older load destination through immediate bits and take an unnecessary bubble.\n+  The prior broad hazard-relaxation attempts failed because they also changed\n+  architected source accounting or touched the late STORE-data path; the\n+  backend-only opportunity itself is still there.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Keep RVFI-visible `rs1_addr` / `rs2_addr` and the existing load->STORE-data\n+  policy unchanged, but make the interlock smarter about which IF/ID sources\n+  are actually live for hazard purposes. In `hazard_unit`, derive conservative\n+  `uses_rs1_hazard` / `uses_rs2_hazard` bits from the younger instruction's\n+  opcode/funct form and ignore only the source fields that are provably unused\n+  in EX for legal encodings such as OP-IMM, LOAD, JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, and\n+  EBREAK. Leave STORE `rs2`, BRANCH, R-type, and unknown/illegal encodings\n+  conservative.\n+\n+  This targets IPC with almost no new datapath or fetch-path work: it removes\n+  false load-use bubbles caused by immediate-field aliases while avoiding the\n+  correctness pitfalls that broke the earlier stage-accurate and\n+  canonicalized-source attempts.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Replace raw rs-field load-use checks with conservative hazard-only live-source qualification, while keeping STORE rs2 and unknown encodings conservative.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add false-alias load-use tests showing OP-IMM/JAL/LUI/AUIPC/FENCE/EBREAK no longer stall when only immediate bits match an older load rd.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r11s0\n+title: \"Hazard-Only Live Source Filtering\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  `bench` still detects load-use hazards from raw IF/ID bitfields, so\n+  instructions that do not architecturally read `rs2` or `rs1` can alias an\n+  older load destination through immediate bits a