{"type":"text","timestamp":1778876285999,"sessionID":"ses_1d2b93872ffeQM7BArOoRSWwDF","part":{"id":"prt_e2d4a0368001Csu89bwJ5Rittl","messageID":"msg_e2d49c58b001pDJgA4yC5aER9X","sessionID":"ses_1d2b93872ffeQM7BArOoRSWwDF","type":"text","text":"Writing the requested hypothesis file now under `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/` with the single chosen `micro_opt` proposal.","time":{"start":1778876285800,"end":1778876285998},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_08868cc12587380b016a077f7daee4819ba2de8bab5001956c","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778876303322,"sessionID":"ses_1d2b93872ffeQM7BArOoRSWwDF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_0OjZzKUp1sSNxqJCu7Yau04F","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r12s0\n+title: \"Compact MEM/WB Payload and Registered Rd Data\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current `bench` champion already found the big wins that stay off the\n+  fragile fetch path: cold divide offload and a one-deep deferred store slot.\n+  The remaining always-hot backend cone still carries avoidable late-stage\n+  baggage, though. `mem_wb_t` stores both `alu_result` and `read_data` even\n+  though only one can ever become architectural `rd_wdata`, and the full\n+  `ctrl_t` bundle is dragged all the way into WB even though only a tiny subset\n+  is still live there.\n+\n+  On a Tang Nano 20K, that extra register width, control fanout, and the\n+  MEM/WB-to-WB select mux all sit on a path that also feeds regfile writeback,\n+  same-cycle regfile bypass, EX forwarding, and RVFI `rd_wdata`. This looks\n+  like the cleanest remaining Fmax-focused `micro_opt` that does not revisit\n+  the broken hazard-source space or the already-regressive fetch-side ideas.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Retire the MEM/WB stage around the architectural result that downstream logic\n+  actually consumes. In `mem_stage`, precompute the final `rd_wdata` once and\n+  register that canonical value directly in `mem_wb_t` instead of carrying both\n+  `alu_result` and `read_data` into WB for a late mux. At the same time, trim\n+  late-stage control so MEM/WB only holds the bits that are still semantically\n+  live there, rather than the full decode-era `ctrl_t`.\n+\n+  Concretely, this means removing redundant `mem_to_reg` plumbing after MEM,\n+  compacting the MEM/WB payload around `rd`, `rd_wdata`, `reg_write`,\n+  `is_illegal`, and the existing RVFI-visible fields, and making `wb_stage`\n+  largely a pass-through. That should cut flop/routing load and remove one mux\n+  level from the MEM/WB forwarding path without changing CPI, hazard policy,\n+  store-slot ordering, or any RVFI-visible behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Replace the late-stage `alu_result`/`read_data` duality with a single registered `rd_wdata` field in `mem_wb_t`, and split or trim control so WB only carries bits still live after MEM.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Remove the redundant `mem_to_reg` output so load writeback selection is no longer encoded as a pipeline-wide control bit when `mem_read` already identifies the only load-producing class.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Stop propagating `mem_to_reg` through decoded control and keep only the control information that is still required by downstream stages.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute the final architectural `rd_wdata` in MEM, pack the compact MEM/WB payload, and preserve stall-hold forwarding semantics using the registered canonical writeback value.\"\n+  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Collapse WB into a direct drive of the already-registered `rd_wdata`, `rd`, and `reg_write` fields instead of a fresh load-vs-ALU mux.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Rewire regfile writeback, MEM/WB-to-EX forwarding, and RVFI `rd_wdata` to consume the compact MEM/WB result directly while preserving the top-level nret=1 contract.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r12s0\n+title: \"Compact MEM/WB Payload and Registered Rd Data\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current `bench` champion already found the big wins that stay off the\n+  fragile fetch path: cold divide offload and a one-deep deferred store slot.\n+  The remaining always-hot backend cone still carries avoidable late-stage\n+  baggage, though. `mem_wb_t` stores both `alu_result` and `read_data` even\n+  though only one can ever become architectural `rd_wdata`, and the full\n+  `ctrl_t` bundle is dragged all the way into WB even though only a tiny subset\n+  is still live there.\n+\n+  On a Tang Nano 20K, that extra register width, control fanout, and the\n+  MEM/WB-to-WB select mux all sit on a path that also feeds regfile writeback,\n+  same-cycle regfile bypass, EX forwarding, and RVFI `rd_wdata`. This looks\n+  like the cleanest remaining Fmax-focused `micro_opt` that does not revisit\n+  the broken hazard-source space or the already-regressive fetch-side ideas.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Retire the MEM/WB stage around the architectural result that downstream logic\n+  actually consumes. In `mem_stage`, precompute the final `rd_wdata` once and\n+  register that canonical value directly in `mem_wb_t` instead of carrying both\n+  `alu_result` and `read_data` into WB for a late mux. At the same time, trim\n+  late-stage control so MEM/WB only holds the bits that are still semantically\n+  live there, rather than the full decode-era `ctrl_t`.\n+\n+  Concretely, this means removing redundant `mem_to_reg` plumbing after MEM,\n+  compacting the MEM/WB payload around `rd`, `rd_wdata`, `reg_write`,\n+  `is_illegal`, and the existing RVFI-visible fields, and making `wb_stage`\n+  largely a pass-through. That should cut flop/routing load and remove one mux\n+  level from the MEM/WB forwarding path without changing CPI, hazard policy,\n+  store-slot ordering, or any RVFI-visible behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Replace the late-stage `alu_result`/`read_data` duality with a single registered `rd_wdata` field in `mem_wb_t`, and split or trim control so WB only carries bits still live after MEM.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Remove the redundant `mem_to_reg` output so load writeback selection is no longer encoded as a pipeline-wide control bit when `mem_read` already identifies the only load-producing class.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Stop propagating `mem_to_reg` through decoded control and keep only the control information that is still required by downstream stages.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute the final architectural `rd_wdata` in MEM, pack the compact MEM/WB payload, and preserve stall-hold forwarding semantics using the registered canonical writeback value.\"\n+  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Collapse WB into a direct drive of the already-registered `rd_wdata`, `rd`, and `reg_write` fields instead of a fresh load-vs-ALU mux.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Rewire regfile writeback, MEM/WB-to-EX forwarding, and RVFI `rd_wdata` to consume the compact MEM/WB result directly while preserving the top-level nret=1 contract.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/ben