classes and replacing one flat ALU result `case` with separate `hot_result`/`m_result` muxes plus an `op[4]` final select regressed, suggesting bench's real EX critical path is elsewhere and extra class-select structure can cost more Fmax than it saves.\\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (improvement, +10.45%): Backend-only buffering of aligned normal-RAM stores is a good lever on this RTL because CoreMark issues enough stack/list/matrix/state stores that turning `io_dmemReady=0` on STOREs from a whole-pipeline freeze into a one-deep deferred write raises IPC, as long as younger memory ops and end-visible markers stay fenced behind the pending slot... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n6: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778879434811,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d28632e1ffeyB5vXCsqgnd27t\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d7a10370017TsZ2Hpo7aAAb8\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"d54c9ca8f121e9c62caccb9e8496efab7dea4a76\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d79d08f0011zdZsZf9Phzum1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d28632e1ffeyB5vXCsqgnd27t\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":43498,\"input\":4328,\"output\":254,\"reasoning\":516,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":38400}},\"cost\":0}}\n7: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778879435964,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d28632e1ffeyB5vXCsqgnd27t\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d7a14ba001cHDBE9FkzYU4ui\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d7a10ad001ZZq5EX3ZZBoPDd\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d28632e1ffeyB5vXCsqgnd27t\",\"snapshot\":\"d54c9ca8f121e9c62caccb9e8496efab7dea4a76\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n8: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778879475595,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d28632e1ffeyB5vXCsqgnd27t\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d7aa501001u8dXmg56via3fZ\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d7a10ad001ZZq5EX3ZZBoPDd\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d28632e1ffeyB5vXCsqgnd27t\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The unexplored high-leverage angle looks like the register file itself: its resettable 32x32 flop array likely blocks RAM inference and adds routing on a design where fetch-side and MEM-side