{"type":"text","timestamp":1778836790438,"sessionID":"ses_1d511137cffe4v017SuI15LgTU","part":{"id":"prt_e2aef4eec001yDJRj6VQMa0tDd","messageID":"msg_e2aef1860001WoeQB3MWN7RwIU","sessionID":"ses_1d511137cffe4v017SuI15LgTU","type":"text","text":"Current divider-offload win leaves two obvious local bottlenecks: unnecessary hazard bubbles and some hot-path control/forwarding cones. I'm checking whether the existing load-use detector is conservatively stalling on instructions that do not actually read `rs2`, because that's a clean IPC-side `micro_opt` with low Fmax risk.","time":{"start":1778836786924,"end":1778836790436},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0494a7a2c93f91f0016a06e532d524819aa51f38098d06bf7c","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778836790507,"sessionID":"ses_1d511137cffe4v017SuI15LgTU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_N5qaIJPbIvv4u5KZrXmOFvVA","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"CoreMark|load-use|stall|bubble|hazard|immediate","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores","include":"*.md"},"output":"Found 13 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md:\n  Line 1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.23%): Pulling DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the one-cycle EX ALU and handling them with a stall-on-use iterative unit can buy large Fmax gains because CoreMark's hot loop is dominated by MUL, load/store, and branch traffic, so rare divide stalls cost less than keeping a 32-bit divider on the common critical path.\n\n  Line 2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, -14.32%): On this core's combinational IF/ID path, adding ID-stage BTFNT and always-taken JAL prediction pulled decode, immediate-target add, and next-PC select onto the fetch critical path, and the resulting Fmax loss outweighed any CoreMark loop-branch bubble savings.\n\n\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/vexriscv/UPSTREAM.md:\n  Line 9: ## Cited CoreMark/MHz\n\n  Line 13: Compiler context: `riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc -O3 -fno-inline` (dhrystone; CoreMark figure from \"VexRiscv full no cache\" and \"VexRiscv full\" config rows in upstream README)\n\n\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/picorv32/UPSTREAM.md:\n  Line 9: ## Cited CoreMark/MHz\n\n  Line 18: composite reference fitness is `Fmax (locally measured) × CoreMark/MHz\n\n\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/neorv32/UPSTREAM.md:\n  Line 9: ## Cited CoreMark/MHz\n\n  Line 18: composite reference fitness is `Fmax (locally measured) × CoreMark/MHz\n\n  Line 23: Nolting 2020–present. **VHDL.** Yosys requires `ghdl-yosys-plugin` for VHDL synthesis. If that's not installed in the bench's `.toolchain/`, NEORV32 falls back to citation-only. Upstream README cites 0.9523 CoreMarks/MHz for an RTOS-capable `rv32imc_Zicsr_Zicntr` configuration on an Altera Cyclone IV E EP4CE22F17C6 FPGA running at up to 130 MHz. The RTL vendored here is the full `rtl/core/` tree (56 VHDL files).\n\n\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/ibex/UPSTREAM.md:\n  Line 9: ## Cited CoreMark/MHz\n\n  Line 13: Compiler context: CoreMark run on Ibex Simple System platform; see `examples/sw/benchmarks/README.md` in upstream for exact flags. Default benchmark build uses standard RISC-V GCC toolchain targeting `rv32imc`.\n\n  Line 18: composite reference fitness is `Fmax (locally measured) × CoreMark/MHz\n\n  Line 23: lowRISC. OpenTitan-deployed. Configurable (small / maxperf, with/without PMP, single-cycle / multi-cycle multiplier). Yosys+nextpnr-himbaechel may not synthesize all SystemVerilog features used (interfaces, generate, classes); fallback to citation-only is documented in §7 of the paper. Three CoreMark/MHz figures from upstream README depending on config: 0.904 (small), 2.47 (mid), 3.13 (maxperf). The `citation_only` field in `core.yaml` records the small-config figure (0.904) as the conservative baseline.\n","metadata":{"matches":13,"truncated":false},"title":"CoreMark|load-use|stall|bubble|hazard|immediate","time":{"start":1778836790456,"end":1778836790506}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0494a7a2c93f91f0016a06e53655c0819a9a22bc761ad585b1"}},"id":"prt_e2aef5cb70020liqOODUJj5l77","sessionID":"ses_1d511137cffe4v017SuI15LgTU","messageID":"msg_e2aef1860001WoeQB3MWN7RwIU"}}
