{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778836828457,"sessionID":"ses_1d511137cffe4v017SuI15LgTU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_4nnqewIsdUoJOKUuVUCeWItQ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"jq -c 'select(.id==\"hyp-20260428-001-r3s0\" or .id==\"hyp-20260428-046-r18s0\" or .id==\"hyp-20260428-047-r18s1\") | {id,title,category,outcome,delta_pct,fitness,fmax_mhz,cycles,ipc_coremark,implementation_notes}' log.jsonl","timeout":120000,"workdir":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/v1/experiments","description":"Extract selected v1 experiment outcomes"},"output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260428-001-r3s0\",\"title\":\"Operand-Aware Load-Use Interlock\",\"category\":\"micro_opt\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"fitness\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"cycles\":null,\"ipc_coremark\":null,\"implementation_notes\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260428-046-r18s0\",\"title\":\"Source-Qualified Load-Use Interlock\",\"category\":\"micro_opt\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":-30.99,\"fitness\":365.3,\"fmax_mhz\":126.37,\"cycles\":3459314,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000003,\"implementation_notes\":\"# Source-Qualified Load-Use Interlock\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- Added `rtl/source_use_decode.sv`, a compact shared predecode for architectural source usage.\\n- Updated `rtl/hazard_unit.sv` so load-use stalls require:\\n  - a valid ID/EX load producer,\\n  - a valid IF/ID consumer,\\n  - a nonzero matching load destination,\\n  - and a match only against source operands the IF/ID instruction actually reads.\\n- Updated `rtl/core.sv` to wire IF/ID and ID/EX valid bits plus the IF/ID instruction into the hazard unit.\\n- Added a MEM-stage RVFI source-data repair path from the current WB value. This keeps the core's existing raw RVFI source-address convention intact for cosim while ensuring a false raw source match behind a load still reports the current architectural source data.\\n- Qualified EX/MEM forwarding so loads are not forwarded from EX/MEM. True load consumers still wait for the existing load-use bubble and receive data from MEM/WB; this prevents false consumers from recording a load address as raw RVFI source data.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- I added a small `source_use_decode` module instead of open-coding the opcode mask directly inside `hazard_unit`.\\n- I kept raw RVFI source addresses because the existing cosim reference compares them directly for every instruction. Instead of masking unused sources to x0/0, `mem_stage` repairs raw source data from the immediately older WB instruction when needed. This affects RVFI metadata only; it does not feed EX operands or add a load-data bypass for execution.\\n- EX/MEM forwarding for loads is now explicitly disabled. The old forwarding select was harmless only because the conservative load-use interlock kept true consumers away from that path; after source qualification, false consumers can reach EX while a load is in MEM, so forwarding the load address would corrupt raw RVFI source metadata.\\n\\n## Concerns\\n\\n- No known functional concerns after lint, formal, and cosim.\\n- The added source-use decode is combinational in the existing hazard path. The MEM-stage RVFI repair adds small compare/mux logic on source metadata; FPGA timing will determine the actual Fmax impact.\\n\\n## Local verification\\n\\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv rtl/*.sv`: pass.\\n- Direct `bash formal/run_all.sh`: blocked before solver startup because `formal/riscv-formal` is a symlink to a protected checkout outside the writable sandbox, and the script's staging cleanup failed with `Operation not permitted`.\\n- Equivalent formal run from `/tmp/codex-formal-hyp-20260428-046-r18s0`, using the same `run_all.sh`, `checks.cfg`, `wrapper.sv`, current `rtl/*.sv`, and riscv-formal framework files: pass, `105 passed, 0 failed`.\\n- `make cosim`: pass, `elfs_tested: 2`.\\n- Intermediate formal attempts failed `reg_ch0` on false raw source dependencies. The first counterexample showed stale raw source data behind a load; the second showed an AUIPC recording a misaligned load's address through EX/MEM forwarding. The WB-to-MEM metadata repair plus load-qualified EX/MEM forwarding fixed those failures while preserving raw RVFI source addresses.\\n\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260428-047-r18s1\",\"title\":\"Decode-Exact Load-Use Interlock\",\"category\":\"structural\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"fitness\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"cycles\":null,\"ipc_coremark\":null,\"implementation_notes\":null}\n","metadata":{"output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260428-001-r3s0\",\"title\":\"Operand-Aware Load-Use Interlock\",\"category\":\"micro_opt\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"fitness\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"cycles\":null,\"ipc_coremark\":null,\"implementation_notes\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260428-046-r18s0\",\"title\":\"Source-Qualified Load-Use Interlock\",\"category\":\"micro_opt\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":-30.99,\"fitness\":365.3,\"fmax_mhz\":126.37,\"cycles\":3459314,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000003,\"implementation_notes\":\"# Source-Qualified Load-Use Interlock\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- Added `rtl/source_use_decode.sv`, a compact shared predecode for architectural source usage.\\n- Updated `rtl/hazard_unit.sv` so load-use stalls require:\\n  - a valid ID/EX load producer,\\n  - a valid IF/ID consumer,\\n  - a nonzero matching load destination,\\n  - and a match only against source operands the IF/ID instruction actually reads.\\n- Updated `rtl/core.sv` to wire IF/ID and ID/EX valid bits plus the IF/ID instruction into the hazard unit.\\n- Added a MEM-stage RVFI source-data repair path from the current WB value. This keeps the core's existing raw RVFI source-address convention intact for cosim while ensuring a false raw source match behind a load still reports the current architectural source data.\\n- Qualified EX/MEM forwarding so loads are not forwarded from EX/MEM. True load consumers still wait for the existing load-use bubble and receive data from MEM/WB; this prevents false consumers from recording a load address as raw RVFI source data.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- I added a small `source_use_decode` module instead of open-coding the opcode mask directly inside `hazard_unit`.\\n- I kept raw RVFI source addresses because the existing cosim reference compares them directly for every instruction. Instead of masking unused sources to x0/0, `mem_stage` repairs raw source data from the immediately older WB instruction when needed. This affects RVFI metadata only; it does not feed EX operands or add a load-data bypass for execution.\\n- EX/MEM forwarding for loads is now explicitly disabled. The old forwarding select was harmless only because the conservative load-use interlock kept true consumers away from that path; after source qualification, false consumers can reach EX while a load is in MEM, so forwarding the load address would corrupt raw RVFI source metadata.\\n\\n## Concerns\\n\\n- No known functional concerns after lint, formal, and cosim.\\n- The added source-use decode is combinational in the existing hazard path. The MEM-stage RVFI repair adds small compare/mux logic on source metadata; FPGA timing will determine the actual Fmax impact.\\n\\n## Local verification\\n\\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv rtl/*.sv`: pass.\\n- Direct `bash formal/run_all.sh`: blocked before solver startup because `formal/riscv-formal` is a symlink to a protected checkout outside the writable sandbox, and the script's staging cleanup failed with `Operation not permitted`.\\n- Equivalent formal run from `/tmp/codex-formal-hyp-20260428-046-r18s0`, using the same `run_all.sh`, `checks.cfg`, `wrapper.sv`, current `rtl/*.sv`, and riscv-formal framework files: pass, `105 passed, 0 failed`.\\n- `make cosim`: pass, `elfs_tested: 2`.\\n- Intermediate formal attempts failed `reg_ch0` on false raw source dependencies. The first counterexample showed stale raw source data behind a load; the second showed an AUIPC recording a misaligned load's address through EX/MEM forwarding. The WB-to-MEM metadata repair plus load-qualified EX/MEM forwarding fixed those failures while preserving raw RVFI source addresses.\\n\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260428-047-r18s1\",\"title\":\"Decode-Exact Load-Use Interlock\",\"category\":\"structural\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"fitness\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"cycles\":null,\"ipc_coremark\":null,\"implementation_notes\":null}\n","exit":0,"description":"Extract selected v1 experiment outcomes","truncated":false},"title":"Extract selected v1 experiment outcomes","time":{"start":1778836828450,"end":1778836828455}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0d8abf678a9c7ffc016a06e55b8c08819a986945507b96ac00"}},"id":"prt_e2aefedfb001mmgbHN7oIpLxrc","sessionID":"ses_1d511137cffe4v017SuI15LgTU","messageID":"msg_e2aefbd3e001j2t0x9sWSeX2tq"}}
