{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778836885057,"sessionID":"ses_1d511137cffe4v017SuI15LgTU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_QvCWnBLr0bgG7qfl5WTFPBTy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"jq -r 'select(.id==\"hyp-20260428-043-r17s0\") | .implementation_notes' log.jsonl","timeout":120000,"workdir":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/v1/experiments","description":"Show v1 ALU split implementation notes"},"output":"# Implementation Notes\n\n## Changes made\n\n- Re-encoded the RV32M ALU constants in `rtl/core_pkg.sv` so all M-extension\n  operations have `alu_op[4] = 1`.\n- Assigned the M-extension constants contiguously as `5'b10000` through\n  `5'b10111`, matching RV32M `funct3` order:\n  `MUL`, `MULH`, `MULHSU`, `MULHU`, `DIV`, `DIVU`, `REM`, `REMU`.\n- Refactored `rtl/alu.sv` from one broad result `case` into two local result\n  muxes:\n  - `simple_out` covers ADD/SUB, logic, compare, shifts, and LUI.\n  - `m_out` covers multiply results plus the existing zero result for\n    DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, whose real result still comes from `div_unit.sv`.\n- The final ALU result is selected only by `op[4] ? m_out : simple_out`.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- No architectural or pipeline behavior was changed.\n- No bundle widths, RVFI fields, decoder legality defaults, divider protocol,\n  forwarding behavior, retirement order, top-level IO, or test/eval files were\n  changed.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` could not run directly in this sandbox because\n  `formal/riscv-formal` is a symlink to a shared tree outside the writable\n  worktree, and the script's staging cleanup hit `Operation not permitted`.\n  I ran the unmodified script from a temporary writable copy of the project\n  instead.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- None known. The change is intentionally limited to ALU op encoding and ALU\n  result mux shape.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh`: blocked in-place by sandbox permissions before any\n  proof ran.\n- Equivalent local formal self-check from temporary writable staging copy:\n  pass, `Formal: 105 passed, 0 failed`.\n\n","metadata":{"output":"# Implementation Notes\n\n## Changes made\n\n- Re-encoded the RV32M ALU constants in `rtl/core_pkg.sv` so all M-extension\n  operations have `alu_op[4] = 1`.\n- Assigned the M-extension constants contiguously as `5'b10000` through\n  `5'b10111`, matching RV32M `funct3` order:\n  `MUL`, `MULH`, `MULHSU`, `MULHU`, `DIV`, `DIVU`, `REM`, `REMU`.\n- Refactored `rtl/alu.sv` from one broad result `case` into two local result\n  muxes:\n  - `simple_out` covers ADD/SUB, logic, compare, shifts, and LUI.\n  - `m_out` covers multiply results plus the existing zero result for\n    DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, whose real result still comes from `div_unit.sv`.\n- The final ALU result is selected only by `op[4] ? m_out : simple_out`.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- No architectural or pipeline behavior was changed.\n- No bundle widths, RVFI fields, decoder legality defaults, divider protocol,\n  forwarding behavior, retirement order, top-level IO, or test/eval files were\n  changed.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` could not run directly in this sandbox because\n  `formal/riscv-formal` is a symlink to a shared tree outside the writable\n  worktree, and the script's staging cleanup hit `Operation not permitted`.\n  I ran the unmodified script from a temporary writable copy of the project\n  instead.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- None known. The change is intentionally limited to ALU op encoding and ALU\n  result mux shape.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh`: blocked in-place by sandbox permissions before any\n  proof ran.\n- Equivalent local formal self-check from temporary writable staging copy:\n  pass, `Formal: 105 passed, 0 failed`.\n\n","exit":0,"description":"Show v1 ALU split implementation notes","trunc