{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778836910347,"sessionID":"ses_1d511137cffe4v017SuI15LgTU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_YVkjrvsv8eD6MaZ5Cu61fyLa","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r2s0\n+title: \"RTL-only hot/cold ALU opcode split\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current best bench result already removed DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU from the\n+  hot one-cycle EX path, but `rtl/alu.sv` still uses a dense ALU-op encoding\n+  and one broad result case covering common RV32I work, multiply results, and\n+  dummy divide-class outputs. That leaves the always-hot ADD/address/compare/\n+  shift path sharing decode and mux structure with cold M-extension cases.\n+\n+  A sibling-core experiment on `cores/v1` showed that this specific RTL-only\n+  reshaping can improve fitness, while more aggressive multiplier rewrites and\n+  source-qualified hazard logic either regressed or broke. That makes the ALU\n+  mux shape the best-supported remaining `micro_opt` angle for the frozen\n+  bench fixture.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Re-encode the ALU operation constants so bit 4 cleanly marks RV32M\n+  operations, with MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU/DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU grouped as a cold\n+  `op[4]=1` class while the common RV32I/simple operations stay in the hot\n+  `op[4]=0` class. Then refactor `rtl/alu.sv` into two local result muxes:\n+  a simple-result mux for ADD/SUB/logic/compare/shift/LUI and an M-result mux\n+  for multiply plus the existing placeholder divide outputs used when the real\n+  divider lives in `rtl/div_unit.sv`.\n+\n+  This keeps the pipeline, RVFI contract, divider protocol, and CoreMark\n+  cycle behavior unchanged while giving synthesis a shallower common EX result\n+  select on the instructions that dominate CoreMark. The expected gain is\n+  mainly Fmax, not IPC, which fits the post-divider state of `cores/bench`.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Re-encode ALU op localparams so RV32M ops occupy a cold `op[4]=1` class without changing architectural meaning.\"\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Split the broad ALU result case into separate hot RV32I and cold RV32M result muxes, selecting the final output with the new hot/cold opcode bit.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r2s0\n+title: \"RTL-only hot/cold ALU opcode split\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current best bench result already removed DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU from the\n+  hot one-cycle EX path, but `rtl/alu.sv` still uses a dense ALU-op encoding\n+  and one broad result case covering common RV32I work, multiply results, and\n+  dummy divide-class outputs. That leaves the always-hot ADD/address/compare/\n+  shift path sharing decode and mux structure with cold M-extension cases.\n+\n+  A sibling-core experiment on `cores/v1` showed that this specific RTL-only\n+  reshaping can improve fitness, while more aggressive multiplier rewrites and\n+  source-qualified hazard logic either regressed or broke. That makes the ALU\n+  mux shape the best-supported remaining `micro_opt` angle for the frozen\n+  bench fixture.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Re-encode the ALU operation constants so bit 4 cleanly marks RV32M\n+  operations, with MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU/DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU grouped as a cold\n+  `op[4]=1` class while the common RV32I/simple operations stay in the hot\n+  `op[4]=0` class. Then refactor `rtl/alu.sv` into two local result muxes:\n+  a simple-result mux for ADD/SUB/logic/compare/shift/LUI and an M-result mux\n+  for multiply plus the existing placeholder divide outputs used when the real\n+  divider lives in `rtl/div_unit.sv`.\n+\n+  This keeps the pipeline, RVFI contract, divider protocol, and CoreMark\n+  cycle behavior unchanged while giving synthesis a shallower common EX result\n+  select on the instructions that dominate CoreMark. The expected gain is\n+  mainly Fmax, not IPC, which fits the post-divider state of `cores/bench`.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Re-encode ALU op localparams so RV32M ops occupy a cold `op[4]=1` class without changing architectural meaning.\"\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Split the broad ALU result case into separate hot RV32I and cold RV32M result muxes, selecting the final output with the new hot/cold opcode bit.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20