{"type":"text","timestamp":1778838816117,"sessionID":"ses_1d4f68b8cffeG5Xlzhh3tTXwJ0","part":{"id":"prt_e2b0e4273001w0U27AEA5bZf8f","messageID":"msg_e2b0de306001YC1pLhRFDhPLq8","sessionID":"ses_1d4f68b8cffeG5Xlzhh3tTXwJ0","type":"text","text":"Writing `hyp-20260515-001-r3s0` as a backend-control-cone cleanup: trim redundant EX/MEM payload and replace wide store-slot compares with narrow registered bits/decodes.","time":{"start":1778838815347,"end":1778838816116},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_01451f3f35cce3e2016a06ed1f3d0c819bb75d51c2ef7d6f3c","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778838831005,"sessionID":"ses_1d4f68b8cffeG5Xlzhh3tTXwJ0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_ez773SNfsJ9hkqd3tmVs5l1A","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\n+title: \"Prune EX/MEM payload and narrow store-slot control\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current best `bench` result already found the two large levers that pay\n+  on this RTL: keep divide/remainder off the hot EX path, and hide some\n+  store-only dmem stalls with the one-deep retirement slot. The failed branch\n+  and replay experiments showed the opposite boundary: adding more fetch-side\n+  control logic costs too much Fmax on this core.\n+\n+  That leaves the MEM-side control cone as the best micro-opt target. The\n+  current store-slot path still carries redundant EX/MEM metadata and uses\n+  always-live wide compares (`instr == 32'h0010_0073`, `addr < 32'h0010_0000`)\n+  to drive global stall decisions.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Collapse backend metadata and replace wide store-slot control compares with\n+  narrower registered signals. In `ex_mem_t`, remove fields that do not add\n+  architectural information on this core: `write_data` duplicates the already\n+  forwarded `rs2_val`, and `branch_taken` / `branch_target` are registered but\n+  never consumed after EX. Replace the top-level EBREAK fence compare with a\n+  one-bit `is_ebreak` marker captured in EX/MEM, and rewrite the normal-RAM\n+  store-slot range check as an explicit high-bit-zero decode instead of a\n+  32-bit less-than comparator.\n+\n+  This keeps CoreMark IPC, RVFI order, and memory ordering unchanged while\n+  shrinking the EX/MEM register, the MEM-stage store-data/control muxing, and\n+  the stall network fed by the pending-store slot. It stays off the frontend\n+  critical path and should stack cleanly with the current divider-offload plus\n+  one-deep-store-slot design.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Trim `ex_mem_t` by removing redundant `write_data`, `branch_taken`, and `branch_target` fields, and add a 1-bit registered `is_ebreak` marker for the store-slot fence path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Stop populating unused branch metadata, keep `rs2_val` as the single post-forwarded store operand, and capture the EX/MEM `is_ebreak` flag without changing redirect or divide behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Build replicated store write data from `rs2_val` instead of a duplicate payload field, and replace the normal-RAM `< 0x0010_0000` check with an equivalent high-bit decode on the store-slot control path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Drive `ex_mem_end_fence` from the registered EX/MEM EBREAK marker instead of a live 32-bit instruction compare, keeping the existing hazard, RVFI, and bus interfaces unchanged.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\n+title: \"Prune EX/MEM payload and narrow store-slot control\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current best `bench` result already found the two large levers that pay\n+  on this RTL: keep divide/remainder off the hot EX path, and hide some\n+  store-only dmem stalls with the one-deep retirement slot. The failed branch\n+  and replay experiments showed the opposite boundary: adding more fetch-side\n+  control logic costs too much Fmax on this core.\n+\n+  That leaves the MEM-side control cone as the best micro-opt target. The\n+  current store-slot path still carries redundant EX/MEM metadata and uses\n+  always-live wide compares (`instr == 32'h0010_0073`, `addr < 32'h0010_0000`)\n+  to drive global stall decisions.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Collapse backend metadata and replace wide store-slot control compares with\n+  narrower registered signals. In `ex_mem_t`, remove fields that do not add\n+  architectural information on this core: `write_data` duplicates the already\n+  forwarded `rs2_val`, and `branch_taken` / `branch_target` are registered but\n+  never consumed after EX. Replace the top-level EBREAK fence compare with a\n+  one-bit `is_ebreak` marker captured in EX/MEM, and rewrite the normal-RAM\n+  store-slot range check as an explicit high-bit-zero decode instead of a\n+  32-bit less-than comparator.\n+\n+  This keeps CoreMark IPC, RVFI order, and memory ordering unchanged while\n+  shrinking the EX/MEM register, the MEM-stage store-data/control muxing, and\n+  the stall network fed by the pending-store slot. It stays off the frontend\n+  critical path and should stack cleanly with the current divider-offload plus\n+  one-deep-store-slot design.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Trim `ex_mem_t` by removing redundant `write_data`, `branch_taken`, and `branch_target` fields, and add a 1-bit registered `is_ebreak` marker for the store-slot fence path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Stop populating unused branch metadata, keep `rs2_val` as the single post-forwarded store operand, and capture the EX/MEM `is_ebreak` flag without changing redirect or divide behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Build replicated store write data from `rs2_val` instead of a duplicate payload field, and replace the normal-RAM `< 0x0010_0000` check with an equivalent high-bit decode on the store-slot control path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Drive `ex_mem_end_fence` from the registered EX/MEM EBREAK marker instead of a live 32-bit instruction compare, keeping the existing hazard, RVFI, and bus interfaces unchanged.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\n+title: \"Prune EX/MEM payload and narrow store-slot control\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current best `bench` result already found the two large levers that pay\n+  on this RTL: keep divide/remainder off the hot EX path, and hide some\n+  store-only dmem stalls with the one-deep retirement slot. The failed branch\n+  and replay experiments showed the opposite boundary: adding more fetch-side\n+  control logic costs too much Fmax on this core.\n+\n+  That leaves the MEM-side control cone as the best micro-opt target. The\n+  current store-slot path still carries redundant EX/MEM metadata and uses\n+  always-live wide compares (`instr == 32'h0010_0073`, `addr < 32'h0010_0000`)\n+  to drive global stall decisions.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Collapse backend metadata and replace wide store-slot control compares with\n+  narrower registered signals. In `ex_mem_t`, remove fields that do not add\n+  architectural information on this core: `write_data` duplicates the already\n+  forwarded `rs2_val`, and `branch_taken` / `branch_target` are registered but\n+  never consumed after EX. Replace the top-level EBREAK fence compare with a\n+  one-bit `is_ebreak` marker captured in EX/MEM, and rewrite the normal-RAM\n+  store-slot range check as an explicit high-bit-zero decode instead of a\n+  32-bit less-than comparator.\n+\n+  This keeps CoreMark IPC, RVFI order, and memory ordering unchanged while\n+  shrinking the EX/MEM register, the MEM-stage store-data/control muxing, and\n+  the stall network fed by the pending-store slot. It stays off the frontend\n+  critical path and should stack cleanly with the current divider-offload plus\n+  one-deep-store-slot design.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Trim `ex_mem_t` by removing redundant `write_data`, `branch_taken`, and `branch_target` fields, and add a 1-bit registered `is_ebreak` marker for the store-slot fence path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Stop populating unused branch metadata, keep `rs2_val` as the single post-forwarded store operand, and capture the EX/MEM `is_ebreak` flag without changing redirect or divide behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Build replicated store write data from `rs2_val` instead of a duplicate payload field, and replace the normal-RAM `< 0x0010_0000` check with an equivalent high-bit decode on the store-slot control path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Drive `ex_mem_end_fence` from the registered EX/MEM EBREAK marker instead of a live 32-bit instruction compare, keeping the existing hazard, RVFI, and bus interfaces unchanged.\"\n","additions":41,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778838831001,"end":1778838831004}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01451f3f35cce3e2016a06ed2007a0819bbd53ed74a8bc315a"}},"id":"prt_e2b0e4575001YVTZJwOD2g9yDZ","sessionID":"ses_1d4f68b8cffeG5Xlzhh3tTXwJ0","messageID":"msg_e2b0de306001YC1pLhRFDhPLq8"}}
