ctions, then carry those registered fields in EX/MEM. MEM can then drive dmem_wen/dmem_ren, RVFI masks, and store write data mostly from registered descriptor fields while retaining the existing load-data extraction from dmem_rdata. This should shorten the MEM address/control-to-writeback and dmem-enable paths with no CPI cost, while...\n\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/bench/gpt-5_5_high/rep2/log.jsonl:\n  Line 21: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260513-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Use zero-bubble load forwarding\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current pipeline still injects a one-cycle bubble for every true load-use\\ndependency even though MEM-stage forwarding already formats load data and can\\nfeed the EX operand muxes. CoreMark has many pointer-chasing and state-update\\nsequences where removing those bubbles should improve iterations per cycle.\\nPrior structural attempts lost by adding front-end or store-buffer control;\\nthis keeps the pipeline shape intact and changes only the interlock policy.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current pipeline still injects a one-cycle bubble for every true load-use\\ndependency even though MEM-stage forwarding already formats load data and can\\nfeed the EX operand muxes. CoreMark has many pointer-chasing and state-update\\nsequences where removing those bubbles should improve iterations per cycle.\\nPrior structural attempts lost by adding front-end or store-buffer control;\\nthis keeps the pipeline shape intact and changes only the interlock policy.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Restructure the load-use path so a consumer immediately behind a load is\\nallowed to enter EX while the load is in MEM, using the existing EX/MEM\\nforwarding select to supply formatted load data directly from mem_stage.\\nIf dmem backpressure occurs, the existing dmem stall should hold both the\\nload in MEM and the dependent consumer in ID/EX until data is available, so\\ncorrectness remains in-order without adding a new buffer. This trades a\\nlonger dmem-to-EX bypass path for fewer CoreMark dependency bubbles; the\\nprevious lane-mux load formatter win makes that timing path cheaper than it\\nwas before.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the unconditional load-use bubble and rely on dmem stalls plus MEM-stage load forwarding for true dependent consumers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\"...\n\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/bench/gpt-5_5_high/rep1/log.jsonl:\n  Line 5: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260512-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Prune false load-use stalls\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current load-use hazard check compares a load destination against both\\nIF/ID register fields for every following instruction. That is conservative:\\nI-type, load, JALR, U-type, JAL, FENCE, and EBREAK do not consume the rs2\\nfield in EX, and store rs2 is store data that can be supplied later in MEM.\\nCoreMark has many immediate operations and memory copies, so these false or\\navoidable bubbles directly reduce iterations per cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current load-use hazard check compares a load destination against both\\nIF/ID register fields for every following instruction. That is conservative:\\nI-type, load, JALR, U-type, JAL, FENCE, and EBREAK do not consume the rs2\\nfield in EX, and store rs2 is store data that can be supplied later in MEM.\\nCoreMark has many immediate operations and memory copies, so these false or\\navoidable bubbles directly reduce iterations per cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make the load-use interlock source-aware. Only stall when the following\\ninstruction actually needs the loaded register in EX: rs1 for address/JALR/ALU\\noperations and both operands for R-type or branch compares. For store data\\ndependencies,