zard unit stalls the STORE for 1 cycle because it assumes rs2 is needed in the EX stage, but a STORE only needs its payload in the MEM stage. A previous attempt to optimize this failed formal verification because the bypass was gated by the valid bit, which is cleared during dmem stalls, corrupting the bypassed data and RVFI traces.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Exempt STORE instructions from load-use stalls on rs2 by modifying the hazard unit. To resolve the data dependency, add a direct forwarding bypass within the MEM stage: if the preceding instruction in the MEM/WB register writes to the STORE's rs2_addr, bypass its result directly into the STORE's memory write-data path. By carefully removing the `valid` check from the bypass condition, we ensure correct forwarding even during multi-cycle dmem stalls where `hold_wb` clears the valid bit but retains the data fields specifically for forwarding. This eliminates frequent load-store bubbles and increases IPC safely without extending the critical path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace `if_id_rs1` and `if_id_rs2` inputs with `input logi...\n  Line 39: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"Bypass load-to-store in MEM with fwd_valid\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"A LOAD followed immediately by a STORE of the loaded value is an extremely common pattern in the CoreMark benchmark. The baseline hazard unit stalls the STORE for 1 cycle because it assumes rs2 is needed in the EX stage, but a STORE only needs its payload in the MEM stage. Bypassing this false pipeline dependency saves 1 cycle per occurrence.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"A LOAD followed immediately by a STORE of the loaded value is an extremely common pattern in the CoreMark benchmark. The baseline hazard unit stalls the STORE for 1 cycle because it assumes rs2 is needed in the EX stage, but a STORE only needs its payload in the MEM stage. Bypassing this false pipeline dependency saves 1 cycle per occurrence.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Exempt STORE instructions from load-use stalls on rs2 in the hazard unit. Add a direct forwarding bypass in the MEM stage: if the instruction in MEM/WB writes to the STORE's rs2_addr, bypass its result into the STORE's write-data path. To handle multi-cycle dmem stalls where the MEM/WB valid bit is cleared to prevent double-retirement, maintain a separate `fwd_valid` flop that holds its state during stalls, ensuring correct data forwarding without breaking RVFI traces or liveness checks.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"1. Replace the two input ports `input logic [4:0] if_id_rs1` and `if_id_rs2` with a single port `input logic [31:0] if_id_instr`.\\n2. Inside `always_comb`, decode `logic [4:0] if_id_rs1 = if_id_instr[19:15];`, `logic [4:0] if_id_rs2 = if_id_instr[24:20];`, and `logic if_id_is_store = (if_id_instr[6:0] == 7'b0100011);`.\\n3. Update the `load_use_hazard` equation to exempt stores from stalling on rs2: `load_use_hazard = id_ex_mem_read && (id_ex_rd != 5'b0) && (id_ex_rd == if_id_rs1 || (id_ex_rd == if_...\n  Line 41: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-001-r14s0\", \"title\": \"(slot 0 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent modified off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv']\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 14, \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark makes heavy use of pointer chasing and memory copies where a LOAD is immediately followed by a STORE of the loaded data. The current hazard unit stalls this sequence for 1 cycle because the STORE is caught by the generic load-use hazard logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Adding a direct forwarding path from the MEM/WB register to the dmem_wdata mux in the MEM stage allows us to exempt stores from load-use stalls when they only depend on the load for rs2 (store data). The bypass relies on MEM/WB's data fields and ignores the valid bit, allowing it to correctly handle dmem_stalls without regressions.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add if_id_opcode input. Exempt instructions with opcode 7'b0100011 (STORE) from load-use stalls when the dependency is only on rs2.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire if_id_w.instr[6:0] to the new if_id_opcode port on u_hazard.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a bypass mux for store_data that selects reg_q.read_data instead of in.write_data if reg_q is a LOAD and reg_q.rd == in.rs2_addr.\"}]}, \"scribe_skipped\": \"PermissionError: scribe touched off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv']\"}\n\n  Line 42: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-002-r14s1\", \"title\": \"(slot 1 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent modified off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/core.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv']\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14, \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"A common pattern in CoreMark is a LOAD followed immediately by a STORE of the loaded data.\\nCurrently, this incurs a 1-cycle load-use stall because the STORE's rs2 is checked in ID.\\nBypassing the load data directly to the memory stage removes this penalty.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Update the hazard unit to exempt the rs2 register of STORE instructions from load-use stalls.\\nIn the MEM stage, add a bypass mux from the MEM/WB register (the retiring LOAD) to the memory write data.\\nThis structurally eliminates the stall cycle for load-to-store dependencies, improving IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add if_id_instr port and exempt store instructions' rs2 from load-use hazard stall.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire if_id_w.instr to the hazard unit's new port.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a bypass mux from reg_q (MEM/WB) read_data to dmem_wdata and rs2_val when the retired instruction is a load matching rs2.\"}]}}\n\n  Line 44: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-001-r15s0\", \"title\": \"Load-to-store bypass\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark's string and memory copy loops frequently feature a STORE immediately following a LOAD.\\nThe baseline core stalls for one cycle on this dependency, artificially limiting IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark's string and memory copy loops frequently feature a STORE immediately following a LOAD.\\nThe baseline core stalls for one cycle on this dependency, artificially limiting IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"By adding a load-to-store bypass path in the MEM stage and exempting stores from the load-use hazard stall for their data operand (rs2), we can save one cycle per load-store pair without lengthening the critical path, yielding a significant IPC boost on memory-heavy workloads.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire if_id_w.instr to hazard_unit to enable store decoding for the load-use check.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode if_id_instr as a store and exempt id_ex_rd == if_id_rs2 dependencies from triggering a load-use stall.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a forwarding mux from the MEM/WB register to the dmem_wdata output and RVFI rs2_val field to supply the freshly loaded data for the store.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire if_id_w.instr to hazard_unit to enable store decoding for the load-use check.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode if_id_instr as a store and exempt id_ex_rd == if_id_rs2 dependencies from triggering a load-use stall.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a forwarding mux from the MEM/WB register to the dmem_wdata output and RVFI rs2_val field to supply the freshly loaded data for the store.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": fal...\n  Line 45: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-002-r15s1\", \"title\": \"Bypass load-to-store in MEM stage to avoid load-use stall\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"A LOAD followed by a STORE using the loaded data currently stalls the pipeline for 1 cycle. The store's data is only needed in the MEM stage, not EX, so forwarding the data directly from WB to MEM eliminates this stall and improves IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"A LOAD followed by a STORE using the loaded data currently stalls the pipeline for 1 cycle. The store's data is only needed in the MEM stage, not EX, so forwarding the data directly from WB to MEM eliminates this stall and improves IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a forwarding path in mem_stage from WB's output to the store data replication logic. Update the hazard unit to exempt instructions from load-use stalls when the destination register matches only rs2 and the instruction is a STORE, thereby avoiding the stall while ensuring the STORE correctly bypasses the load result.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Map wb_rd, wb_w_en (from mem_wb_w.ctrl.reg_write), and wb_data to u_mem. Map if_id_is_store to u_hazard by checking if the instruction opcode is 7'b0100011.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add wb_rd, wb_w_en, and wb_data inputs. Add mem_fwd_wdata logic to bypass wb_data if wb_w_en is true and wb_rd matches in.rs2_addr, and use it instead of in.write_data for wdata_rep.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add if_id_is_store input. Modify load_use_hazard to not stall if the only collision is with rs2 and if_id_is_store is true.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Map wb_rd, wb_w_en (from mem_wb_w.ctrl.reg_write), and wb_data to u_mem. Map if_id_is_store to u_hazard by checking if the instruction opcode is 7'b0100011.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"descrip...\n\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/bench/gemini-3_1-pro/rep1/log.jsonl:\n  Line 17: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"(slot 0 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent modified off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['test_prec_load.sv']\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 6, \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current hazard unit checks for load-use dependencies by unconditionally comparing the LOAD's destination register against bits 19:15 and 24:20 of the following instruction. For instructions like LUI, AUIPC, JAL, and OP-IMM, these bits contain random immediate data. If they coincidentally match the LOAD's destination, the pipeline suffers a false 1-cycle stall, degrading IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replacing the raw rs1/rs2 inputs to the hazard unit with the full instruction allows us to decode whether the instruction actually reads rs1 and/or rs2. By qualifying the load-use check with these decode enables, we will eliminate false stalls and increase IPC. We keep rs2_en=1 for STOREs to preserve the architecturally required load-to-store stall without needing complex Fmax-killing bypasses.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace `if_id_rs1` and `if_id_rs2` inputs with `input logic [31:0] if_id_instr`.\\nInside the module, extract the opcode: `logic [6:0] opcode; assign opcode = if_id_instr[6:0];`.\\nCreate a combinational block that sets `rs1_en` and `rs2_en` based on `opcode`. Initialize both to 0. Set `rs1_en=1` and `rs2_en=1` for OP (0110011), STORE (0100011), and BRANCH (1100011). Set `rs1_en=1` and `rs2_en=0` for OP-IMM (0010011), LOAD (0000011), and JALR (1100111).\\nExtract `logic [4:0] if_id_rs1 = if_id_instr[19:15];` and `logic [4:0] if_id_rs2 = if_id_instr[24:20];`.\\nModify `load_use_hazard` to require the enables: `id_ex_mem_read && ((rs1_en && id_ex_rd == if_id_rs1) || (rs2_en && id_ex_rd == if_id_rs2)) && (id_ex_rd != 5'b0)...","metadata":{"matches":30,"truncated":false},"title":"store data|late load-store|load-to-store|store-data forwarding|Forward load data to stores|rs2-only","time":{"start":1778853938455,"end":1778853938492}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ea456bffd0d0f2a016a0728325d7881988c6e9c5000bac9b8"}},"id":"prt_e2bf50512001j0TfxIjcrg0dsf","sessionID":"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG","messageID":"msg_e2bf4c3ad0013nRn3lYpEHcm5N"}}
