{"type":"text","timestamp":1778854013001,"sessionID":"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG","part":{"id":"prt_e2bf61dec001uQbAFuKUMHNsFe","messageID":"msg_e2bf5755e001IokRrUQSvaptuD","sessionID":"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG","type":"text","text":"The strongest remaining `micro_opt` looks like a stage-accurate load-use interlock: keep stalls only for values truly needed in EX, and let STORE `rs2` arrive one stage later through MEM/WB-to-MEM forwarding. That targets real CoreMark bubbles without adding fetch-side or ALU-path timing risk.","time":{"start":1778854010348,"end":1778854013000},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0d6fa325dba2051b016a07287a4218819aa470bdcea487c1a5","phase":"commentary"}}}}
