{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778854047980,"sessionID":"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_079GpSI9lfP3BXhTEaXvbQX1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\n+title: \"Stage-Accurate Load-Use Interlock\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  After divider offload and the one-deep store retirement slot, the cheapest\n+  remaining CoreMark IPC loss is likely the still-conservative load-use\n+  interlock. `hazard_unit` compares a load destination against raw IF/ID rs1\n+  and rs2 bitfields even when the younger instruction does not actually need\n+  those fields in EX, and it still forces a bubble for STORE rs2 even though\n+  store data is only consumed one stage later in MEM.\n+\n+  That means the core can still lose cycles to false immediate-field matches\n+  and to real load-then-store-data dependencies that do not protect any EX\n+  critical operand. This is a narrow backend/control cleanup that attacks IPC\n+  without adding predictor state, fetch-path muxing, or a new EX datapath.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Make the load-use detector stage-accurate instead of field-accurate.\n+  Decode conservative `uses_rs1_ex` / `uses_rs2_ex` bits from the IF/ID\n+  instruction inside `hazard_unit`, and only stall when the older load feeds a\n+  value that the younger instruction truly needs in EX. Keep unknown or\n+  illegal encodings conservative, but stop treating OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR,\n+  LUI/AUIPC/JAL, FENCE, and EBREAK as two-source consumers.\n+\n+  For STORE specifically, treat rs1 as an EX-time dependency and rs2 as a\n+  MEM-time dependency. Allow a load followed immediately by a STORE of that\n+  loaded value to advance without the bubble, then repair the data in\n+  `mem_stage` with a local MEM/WB-to-store-data bypass that also updates the\n+  retiring store's RVFI-visible rs2/mem_wdata fields. The bypass must use the\n+  held MEM/WB payload rather than `valid`, because `hold_wb` intentionally\n+  clears only retirement while preserving forwarding data during dmem stalls.\n+\n+  This should recover a small but real class of CoreMark bubbles while keeping\n+  the change off the fetch critical path and away from the hot ALU/branch cone.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Replace the raw rs1/rs2 load-use test with conservative opcode-based EX-operand use bits, so only true EX-time consumers stall and STORE rs2 stops forcing a bubble.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Pass the IF/ID instruction into hazard detection so the interlock can classify source timing without changing the architectural pipeline fields or top-level IO contract.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a local MEM/WB-to-store-data bypass and use the forwarded value for store write-data formation plus RVFI rs2/mem_wdata reporting, even across `hold_wb` cycles.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add coverage for non-consuming post-load instructions that should no longer stall spuriously, and for a load-then-store-data sequence that must retire correctly with and without dmem backpressure.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\n+title: \"Stage-Accurate Load-Use Interlock\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  After divider offload and the one-deep store retirement slot, the cheapest\n+  remaining CoreMark IPC loss is likely the still-conservative load-use\n+  interlock. `hazard_unit` compares a load destination against raw IF/ID rs1\n+  and rs2 bitfields even when the younger instruction does not actually need\n+  those fields in EX, and it still forces a bubble for STORE rs2 even though\n+  store data is only consumed one stage later in MEM.\n+\n+  That means the core can still lose cycles to false immediate-field matches\n+  and to real load-then-store-data dependencies that do not protect any EX\n+  critical operand. This is a narrow backend/control cleanup that attacks IPC\n+  without adding predictor state, fetch-path muxing, or a new EX datapath.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Make the load-use detector stage-accurate instead of field-accurate.\n+  Decode conservative `uses_rs1_ex` / `uses_rs2_ex` bits from the IF/ID\n+  instruction inside `hazard_unit`, and only stall when the older load feeds a\n+  value that the younger instruction truly needs in EX. Keep unknown or\n+  illegal encodings conservative, but stop treating OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR,\n+  LUI/AUIPC/JAL, FENCE, and EBREAK as two-source consumers.\n+\n+  For STORE specifically, treat rs1 as an EX-time dependency and rs2 as a\n+  MEM-time dependency. Allow a load followed immediately by a STORE of that\n+  loaded value to advance without the bubble, then repair the data in\n+  `mem_stage` with a local MEM/WB-to-store-data bypass that also updates the\n+  retiring store's RVFI-visible rs2/mem_wdata fields. The bypass must use the\n+  held MEM/WB payload rather than `valid`, because `hold_wb` intentionally\n+  clears only retirement while preserving forwarding data during dmem stalls.\n+\n+  This should recover a small but real class of CoreMark bubbles while keeping\n+  the change off the fetch critical path and away from the hot ALU/branch cone.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Replace the raw rs1/rs2 load-use test with conservative opcode-based EX-operand use bits, so only true EX-time consumers stall and STORE rs2 stops forcing a bubble.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Pass the IF/ID instruction into hazard detection so the interlock can classify source timing without changing the architectural pipeline fields or top-level IO contract.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a local MEM/WB-to-store-data bypass and use the forwarded value for store write-data formation plus RVFI rs2/mem_wdata reporting, even across `hold_wb` cycles.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add coverage for non-consuming post-load instructions that should no longer stall spuriously, and for a load-then-store-data sequence that must retire correctly with and without dmem backpressure.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\n+title: \"Stage-Accurate Load-Use Interlock\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  After divider offload and the one-deep store retirement slot, the cheapest\n+  remaining CoreMark IPC loss is likely the still-conservative load-use\n+  interlock. `hazard_unit` compares a load destination against raw IF/ID rs1\n+  and rs2 bitfields even when the younger instruction does not actually need\n+  those fields in EX, and it still forces a bubble for STORE rs2 even though\n+  store data is only consumed one stage later in MEM.\n+\n+  That means the core can still lose cycles to false immediate-field matches\n+  and to real load-then-store-data dependencies that do not protect any EX\n+  critical operand. This is a narrow backend/control cleanup that attacks IPC\n+  without adding predictor state, fetch-path muxing, or a new EX datapath.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Make the load-use detector stage-accurate instead of field-accurate.\n+  Decode conservative `uses_rs1_ex` / `uses_rs2_ex` bits from the IF/ID\n+  instruction inside `hazard_unit`, and only stall when the older load feeds a\n+  value that the younger instruction truly needs in EX. Keep unknown or\n+  illegal encodings conservative, but stop treating OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR,\n+  LUI/AUIPC/JAL, FENCE, and EBREAK as two-source consumers.\n+\n+  For STORE specifically, treat rs1 as an EX-time dependency and rs2 as a\n+  MEM-time dependency. Allow a load followed immediately by a STORE of that\n+  loaded value to advance without the bubble, then repair the data in\n+  `mem_stage` with a local MEM/WB-to-store-data bypass that also updates the\n+  retiring store's RVFI-visible rs2/mem_wdata fields. The bypass must use the\n+  held MEM/WB payload rather than `valid`, because `hold_wb` intentionally\n+  clears only retirement while preserving forwarding data during dmem stalls.\n+\n+  This should recover a small but real class of CoreMark bubbles while keeping\n+  the change off the fetch critical path and away from the hot ALU/branch cone.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Replace the raw rs1/rs2 load-use test with conservative opcode-based EX-operand use bits, so only true EX-time consumers stall and STORE rs2 stops forcing a bubble.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Pass the IF/ID instruction into hazard detection so the interlock can classify source timing without changing the architectural pipeline fields or top-level IO contract.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a local MEM/WB-to-store-data bypass and use the forwarded value for store write-data formation plus RVFI rs2/mem_wdata reporting, even across `hold_wb` cycles.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add coverage for non-consuming post-load instructions that should no longer stall spuriously, and for a load-then-store-data sequence that must retire correctly with and without dmem backpressure.\"\n","additions":45,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778854047973,"end":1778854047979}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01ef5258e7d90f54016a072890a4c481999e84b6c5a642ccea"}},"id":"prt_e2bf675d30013U6RLfgsEYOgNk","sessionID":"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG","messageID":"msg_e2bf6298c0015UWLMxoLuIgnP6"}}
