entation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-05-15T08:52:45.091730Z\\\", \\\"round_id\\\": 0, \\\"slot\\\": 0}\\n2: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Iterative Cold Divider Off EX Path\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address generation, branch support, and\\\\nMUL. On a Tang Nano 20K, a full 32-bit divider is a strong candidate for\\\\nthe universal EX-stage critical path, yet CoreMark's timed loop is mostly\\\\nmultiply, load/store, and branch traffic and should pay little or no steady\\\\nstate penalty from slower divide instructions.\\\\n\\\\nThis makes divider extraction the highest-leverage micro-opt still missing\\\\nfrom the frozen bench fixture: it targets Fmax directly while preserving the\\\\nhot one-cycle behavior for the instructions that dominate CoreMark.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address gen... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n27: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778854013244,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf6293b001sE0Jt3PXUXFhgW\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"9a619dfd69c68205dabe2c22ba0b6720c15f89c3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf5755e001IokRrUQSvaptuD\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":108681,\"input\":7207,\"output\":222,\"reasoning\":1924,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":99328}},\"cost\":0}}\n28: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778854014640,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf62eaf001WcfOqMgGtoxhpt\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf6298c0015UWLMxoLuIgnP6\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"snapshot\":\"9a619dfd69c68205dabe2c22ba0b6720c15f89c3\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n29: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778854032850,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf67422001KWpWCOxu5RYvyC\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf6298c0015UWLMxoLuIgnP6\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Writing the hypothesis YAML now with the hazard-precision/store-data-bypass direction and explicit test coverage.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778854032418,\"end\":1778854032850},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_01ef5258e7d90f54016a07289047188199bef0e3f6c5920ca8\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n30: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778854047980,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"apply_patch\",\"callID\":\"call_079GpSI9lfP3BXhTEaXvbQX1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"patchText\":\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\\n+title: \\\"Stage-Accurate Load-Use Interlock\\\"\\n+category: micro_opt\\n+motivation: |\\n+  After divider offload and the one-deep store retirement slot, the cheapest\\n+  remaining CoreMark IPC loss is likely the still-conservative load-use\\n+  interlock. `hazard_unit` compares a load destination against raw IF/ID rs1\\n+  and rs2 bitfields even when the younger instruction does not actually need\\n+  those fields in EX, and it still forces a bubble for STORE rs2 even though\\n+  store data is only consumed one stage later in MEM.\\n+\\n+  That means the core can still lose cycles to false immediate-field matches\\n+  and to real load-then-store-data dependencies that do not protect any EX\\n+  critical operand. This is a narrow backend/control cleanup that attacks IPC\\n+  without adding predictor state, fetch-path muxing, or a new EX datapath.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Make the load-use detector stage-accurate instead of field-accurate.\\n+  Decode conservative `uses_rs1_ex` / `uses_rs2_ex` bits from the IF/ID\\n+  instruction inside `hazard_unit`, and only stall when the older load feeds a\\n+  value that the younger instruction truly needs in EX. Keep unknown or\\n+  illegal encodings conservative, but stop treating OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR,\\n+  LUI/AUIPC/JAL, FENCE, and EBREAK as two-source consumers.\\n+\\n+  For STORE specifically, treat rs1 as an EX-time dependency and rs2 as a\\n+  MEM-time dependency. Allow a load followed immediately by a STORE of that\\n+  loaded value to advance without the bubble, then repair the data in\\n+  `mem_stage` with a local MEM/WB-to-st... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n31: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778854048133,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf6b184001gAgH4ien7v17T9\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"9a619dfd69c68205dabe2c22ba0b6720c15f89c3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf6298c0015UWLMxoLuIgnP6\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":115313,\"input\":7536,\"output\":876,\"reasoning\":917,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":105984}},\"cost\":0}}\n32: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778854050246,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf6b9c3001MoPqNmxIYyHJ4a\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf6b1e3001TfH8VA0aiy93jT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"snapshot\":\"9a619dfd69c68205dabe2c22ba0b6720c15f89c3\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n33: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778854055040,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_wehoys212PAjzod9mW2dOtrF\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":200},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: id: hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\\n2: title: \\\"Stage-Accurate Load-Use Interlock\\\"\\n3: category: micro_opt\\n4: motivation: |\\n5:   After divider offload and the one-deep store retirement slot, the cheapest\\n6:   remaining CoreMark IPC loss is likely the still-conservative load-use\\n7:   interlock. `hazard_unit` compares a load destination against raw IF/ID rs1\\n8:   and rs2 bitfields even when the younger instruction does not actually need\\n9:   those fields in EX, and it still forces a bubble for STORE rs2 even though\\n10:   store data is only consumed one stage later in MEM.\\n11: \\n12:   That means the core can still lose cycles to false immediate-field matches\\n13:   and to real load-then-store-data dependencies that do not protect any EX\\n14:   critical operand. This is a narrow backend/control cleanup that attacks IPC\\n15:   without adding predictor state, fetch-path muxing, or a new EX datapath.\\n16: hypothesis: |\\n17:   Make the load-use detector stage-accurate instead of field-accurate.\\n18:   Decode conservative `uses_rs1_ex` / `uses_rs2_ex` bits from the IF/ID\\n19:   instruction inside `hazard_unit`, and only stall when the older load feeds a\\n20:   value that the younger instruction truly needs in EX. Keep unknown or\\n21:   illegal encodings conservative, but stop treating OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR,\\n22:   LUI/AUIPC/JAL, FENCE, and EBREAK as two-source consumers.\\n23: \\n24:   For STORE specifi... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n34: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778854055111,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"todowrite\",\"callID\":\"call_ZLcNL9i9rL9hGIqD2jr6JkJ3\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Read bench lessons and recent micro_opt history\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"priority\":\"high\