":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778853885683,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf436d00016ABQPx0RvFLxGs\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf40940001F7ZLV1259C1OWI\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Reviewing `cores/bench` history first to avoid repeating failed `micro_opt` ideas, then I’ll write the hypothesis YAML in the required location.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778853885648,\"end\":1778853885681},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_065b52c951b89b9b016a0727fd6120819bb76f46a9131e2681\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778853886403,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"todowrite\",\"callID\":\"call_qySKg9JKrg7kDNGx7M0NF1Pw\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Read bench lessons and recent micro_opt history\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Select the strongest single micro_opt hypothesis for cores/bench\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Write hypothesis YAML at the required path\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"}]},\"output\":\"[\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Read bench lessons and recent micro_opt history\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"in_progress\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Select the strongest single micro_opt hypothesis for cores/bench\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Write hypothesis YAML at the required path\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n  }\\n]\",\"metadata\":{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Read bench lessons and recent micro_opt history\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Select the strongest single micro_opt hypothesis for cores/bench\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Write hypothesis YAML at the required path\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"high\"}],\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"3 todos\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778853886396,\"end\":1778853886398}},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"fc_065b52c951b89b9b016a0727fd7898819b85136c5567ea61b3\"}},\"id\":\"prt_e2bf436f3001xmUFNWjNGKAgV2\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf40940001F7ZLV1259C1OWI\"}}\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778853886497,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf43a1f001Pu4XqDJuEcv60p\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"9a619dfd69c68205dabe2c22ba0b6720c15f89c3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf40940001F7ZLV1259C1OWI\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":41296,\"input\":40729,\"output\":123,\"reasoning\":444,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778853887658,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf43ea8001JPPn7t12Q68mrK\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf43a6a001yT2y9ef5wb46V4\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"snapshot\":\"9a619dfd69c68205dabe2c22ba0b6720c15f89c3\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778853894363,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_srtGeQVQpfHdusdw1zQXd801\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":200},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.23%): Pulling DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the one-cycle EX ALU and handling them with a stall-on-use iterative unit can buy large Fmax gains because CoreMark's hot loop is dominated by MUL, load/store, and branch traffic, so rare divide stalls cost less than keeping a 32-bit divider on the common critical path.\\n2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, -14.32%): On this core's combinational IF/ID path, adding ID-stage BTFNT and always-taken JAL prediction pulled decode, immediate-target add, and next-PC select onto the fetch critical path, and the resulting Fmax loss outweighed any CoreMark loop-branch bubble savings.\\n3: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r2s0 (regression, +5.57%): After DIV/REM already moved to `rtl/div_unit.sv`, splitting `alu_op` into hot/cold classes and replacing one flat ALU result `case` with separate `hot_result`/`m_result` muxes plus an `op[4]` final select regressed, suggesting bench's real EX critical path is elsewhere and extra class-select structure can cost more Fmax than it saves.\\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (improvement, +10.45%): Backend-only buffering of aligned normal-RAM stores is a good lever on this RTL because CoreMark issues enough stack/list/matrix/state stores that turning `io_dmemReady=0` on STOREs from a whole-pipeline freeze into a one-deep deferred write raises IPC, as long as younger memory ops and end-visible markers stay fenced behind the pending slot... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778853894428,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_qoWXXtxJp2gYpPN1MyIrzpOf\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"micro_opt|store slot|divider|replay|target cache|predict\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 10 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 1: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"baseline-bench-2c63e03\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Baseline retest for cores/bench\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 282.82, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 0.0, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 0.0, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 127.03, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 9563, \\\"ff\\\": 1866, \\\"seeds\\\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-05-15T08:52:45.091730Z\\\", \\\"round_id\\\": 0, \\\"slot\\\": 0}\\n\\n  Line 2: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Iterative Cold Divider Off EX Path\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address generation, branch support, and\\\\nMUL. On a Tang Nano 20K, a full 32-bit divider is a strong candidate for\\\\nthe universal EX-stage critical path, yet CoreMark's timed loop is mostly\\\\nmultiply, load/store, and branch traffic and should pay little or no steady\\\\nstate penalty from slower divide instructions.\\\\n\\\\nThis makes divider extraction the highest-leverage micro-opt still missing\\\\nfrom the frozen bench fixture: it targets Fmax directly while preserving the\\\\nhot one-cycle behavior for the instructions that dominate CoreMark.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the sa... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778853894586,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf459b9001yJkpbX1TlvXKLy\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"9a619dfd69c68205dabe2c22ba0b6720c15f89c3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf43a6a001yT2y9ef5wb46V4\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":41642,\"input\":959,\"output\":159,\"reasoning\":76,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":40448}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778853895787,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf45e6a001oeK5gWewMGf5OK\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf45a150016hshNR4MKA1Xtb\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"snapshot\":\"9a619dfd69c68205dabe2c22ba0b6720c15f89c3\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778853921344,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf4c024001GWHt0jrAF2PDIG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf45a150016hshNR4MKA1Xtb\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"One promising untried angle is IPC cleanup in the existing 5-stage core: the current load-use detector ignores whether the younger instruction actually reads `rs1`/`rs2`, which can inject false bubbles after loads. I’m checking whether that idea already appeared elsewhere before writing it up.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778853920804,\"end\":1778853921340},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0994eb2a9625e3ba016a072820b53881999c3b9f35fa707e53\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778853921456,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_vXlFPs6h3FlMeXnRumF0AjMG\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"if_id_rs1|if_id_rs2|load_use_hazard\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores\",\"include\":\"*.sv\"},\"output\":\"Found 30 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:\\n  Line 23:   input  logic [4:0] if_id_rs1,         // IF/ID instr[19:15]  (next rs1)\\n\\n  Line 24:   input  logic [4:0] if_id_rs2,         // IF/ID instr[24:20]  (next rs2)\\n\\n  Line 48:   logic load_use_hazard;\\n\\n  Line 54:     load_use_hazard = id_ex_mem_read\\n\\n  Line 55:                    && (id_ex_rd == if_id_rs1 || id_ex_rd == if_id_rs2)\\n\\n  Line 68:     stall_if      = load_use_hazard || imem_stall || dmem_stall\\n\\n  Line 82:     stall_id      = dmem_stall || slot_fence_stall || load_use_hazard || div_stall;\\n\\n  Line 83:     flush_id      = (load_use_hazard || redirect) && !(dmem_stall || slot_fence_stall);\\n\\n\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/core.sv:\\n  Line 187:     .if_id_rs1      (if_id_w.instr[19:15]),\\n\\n  Line 188:     .if_id_rs2      (if_id_w.instr[24:20]),\\n\\n\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/v1/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:\\n  Line 22:   input  logic [4:0] if_id_rs1,         // IF/ID instr[19:15]  (next rs1)\\n\\n  Line 23:   input  logic [4:0] if_id_rs2,         // IF/ID instr[24:20]  (next rs2)\\n\\n  Line 41:   logic load_use_hazard;\\n\\n  Line 45:     load_use_hazard = id_ex_mem_read\\n\\n  Line 46:                    && (id_ex_rd == if_id_rs1 || id_ex_rd == if_id_rs2)\\n\\n  Line 51:     stall_if      = load_use_hazard || imem_stall || mem_wait || ex_long_busy;\\n\\n  Line 64:     stall_id      = mem_wait || load_use_hazard || ex_long_bus... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778853921473,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_bwZn0y9KXIaG3cDlscn8UKpH\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"source-qualified hazard|source qualified hazard|load-use|false stall|rs1_used|rs2_used|uses_rs1|uses_rs2\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3\",\"include\":\"*.{md,jsonl,yaml,sv,py}\"},\"output\":\"Found 231 matches (showing first 100)\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 2: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Iterative Cold Divider Off EX Path\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address generation, branch support, and\\\\nMUL. On a Tang Nano 20K, a full 32-bit divider is a strong candidate for\\\\nthe universal EX-stage critical path, yet CoreMark's timed loop is mostly\\\\nmultiply, load/store, and branch traffic and should pay little or no steady\\\\nstate penalty from slower divide instructions.\\\\n\\\\nThis makes divider extraction the highest-leverage micro-opt still missing\\\\nfrom the frozen bench fixture: it targets Fmax directly while preserving the\\\\nhot one-cycle behavior for the instructions that dominate CoreMark.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address generation, branch support, and\\\\nMUL. On a Tang Nano 20K, a full 32-bit divider is a strong candidate for\\\\nthe universal EX-stage critical path, yet CoreMark's timed loop is mostly\\\\nmultiply, load/store, and branch traffic and should pay little or no steady\\\\nstate penalty from slower divide instructions.\\\\n\\\\nThis makes divider extraction the highest-leverage micro-opt still missing\\\\nfrom the frozen bench fixture: it targets Fmax directly ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778853921611,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf4c349001dp4z4BL4bEDonP\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"9a619dfd69c68205dabe2c22ba0b6720c15f89c3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf45a150016hshNR4MKA1Xtb\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":48391,\"input\":6081,\"output\":250,\"reasoning\":1100,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":40960}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778853923275,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2bf4c9c2001TY7VtnzeRPNu7v\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2bf4c3ad0013nRn3lYpEHcm5N\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"snapshot\":\"9a619dfd69c68205dabe2c22ba0b6720c15f89c3\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778853938493,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_yjduqVpR2DDCLqjKk8punoP3\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"store data|late load-store|load-to-store|store-data forwarding|Forward load data to stores|rs2-only\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3\",\"include\":\"*.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 30 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/v1/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 6: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260427-005-r2s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"MEM-to-EX Load-Use Bypass\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current five-stage pipeline still has the textbook structural load-use gap: a load in EX always forces the immediately following consumer to wait one extra cycle, even when the dmem bus is ready and the loaded word is already available combinationally in MEM. CoreMark's list, matrix, and state kernels contain many load-to-use pairs, so this fixed bubble directly lowers iterations per cycle. The recent predictor win improved control flow without changing the backend; the next most promising structural angle is to add the missing MEM-to-EX load-data path and remove the mandatory interlock while preserving the single-issue in-order retirement contract.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current five-stage pipeline still has the textbook structural load-use gap: a load in EX always forces the immediately following consumer 