{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778862614356,"sessionID":"ses_1d38f39aeffe2eKN4DQTNPadMu","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_dsAuLUzwDJ2mvtdatZW4HJIW","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260515-001-r6s0.log","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260515-001-r6s0.log</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778862507745,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39aeffe2eKN4DQTNPadMu\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2c77c6ca001wG3k7Ax5L1p2ER\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2c70c860001d6KZ3wdtdv3O36\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39aeffe2eKN4DQTNPadMu\",\"snapshot\":\"7e597f9fdf228778dd04439df2a285971435d7a6\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n2: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778862516926,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39aeffe2eKN4DQTNPadMu\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2c77e30b001KfAz81wkCHGD7B\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2c70c860001d6KZ3wdtdv3O36\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39aeffe2eKN4DQTNPadMu\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Reviewing `cores/bench` history first to avoid repeating failed micro-opts, then I'll write the hypothesis file with one focused change.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778862514955,\"end\":1778862516911},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_01b64108febd76e0016a0749b2c66081969427d1cab903a747\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n3: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778862517037,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39aeffe2eKN4DQTNPadMu\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_RIehH9hnFuUebbYiSp8goSrC\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":200},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.23%): Pulling DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the one-cycle EX ALU and handling them with a stall-on-use iterative unit can buy large Fmax gains because CoreMark's hot loop is dominated by MUL, load/store, and branch traffic, so rare divide stalls cost less than keeping a 32-bit divider on the common critical path.\\n2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, -14.32%): On this core's combinational IF/ID path, adding ID-stage BTFNT and always-taken JAL prediction pulled decode, immediate-target add, and next-PC select onto the fetch critical path, and the resulting Fmax loss outweighed any CoreMark loop-branch bubble savings.\\n3: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r2s0 (regression, +5.57%): After DIV/REM already moved to `rtl/div_unit.sv`, splitting `alu_op` into hot/cold classes and replacing one flat ALU result `case` with separate `hot_result`/`m_result` muxes plus an `op[4]` final select regressed, suggesting bench's real EX critical path is elsewhere and extra class-select structure can cost more Fmax than it saves.\\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (improvement, +10.45%): Backend-only buffering of aligned normal-RAM stores is a good lever on this RTL because CoreMark issues enough stack/list/matrix/state stores that turning `io_dmemReady=0` on STOREs from a whole-pipeline freeze into a one-deep deferred write raises IPC, as long as younger memory ops and end-visible markers stay fenced behind the pending slot... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n4: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778862517075,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39aeffe2eKN4DQTNPadMu\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_ic4Hnyy6JmLcluiKt1cmHRWg\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"category.*micro_opt|micro_opt|forward|bypass|hazard|store|load|branch|predict\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-a