 13:59:16 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260515-001-r6s0/formal/last_run-29898.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260515-001-r6s0/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-29898/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 6, \"scribe_skipped\": \"TimeoutError: scribe timed out after 240s\"}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Zero-Bubble Store Slot Refill\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current best `bench` core already proved that deferred normal-RAM stores\\nare a winning backend lever, but the one-deep slot still loses a bubble\\nwhenever a pending store finally drains and the next instruction in MEM is\\nanother bufferable RAM store. Hazard control fences that younger store until\\nthe slot bit clears, so bursty CoreMark store traffic still pays a handoff\\npenalty even though the core already knows both stores' addr/data/mask and\\nonly needs to preserve oldest-first external visibility.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current best `bench` core already proved that deferred normal-RAM stores\\nare a winning backend lever, but the one-deep slot still loses a bubble\\nwhenever a pending store finally drains and the next instruction in MEM is\\nanother bufferable RAM store. Hazard control fences that younger store until\\nthe slot bit clears, so bursty CoreMark store traffic still pays a handoff\\npenalty even though the core already knows both stores' addr/data/mask and\\nonly needs to preserve oldest-first external visibility.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Teach the existing single deferred-store slot to drain and refill in the same\\ncycle instead of growing it into a true two-entry queue. When\\n`store_slot_valid` is set and `io_dmemReady` returns, `mem_stage` should\\ndrive the older deferred store to the bus and, if the current EX/MEM\\ninstruction is another aligned normal-RAM store, immediately capture that\\nyounger store into the same slot while retiring it once through RVFI.\\n\\n`hazard_unit` would then keep fencing loads, MMIO/non-bufferable stores, and\\n`EBREAK` behind a pending slot, but allow exactly one younger bufferable RAM\\nstore through on the drain cycle for a refill. This keeps the proven\\nbackend-only store-buffering strategy, avoids the placement/routing cost that\\nkilled the real two-entry queue, and should recover part of the store-burst\\nIPC win that the deeper queue was chasing.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a same-cycle drain-and-refill path so a bufferable RAM store can retire into the existing slot while the older deferred store drains to dmem, with RVFI and mem_wdata metadata still tied to the younger retiring store and physical write ordering kept oldest-first.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Refine the pending-store fence so loads, MMIO/non-bufferable stores, and EBREAK still stall behind a full slot, but the exact dmem-ready drain cycle may admit one younger bufferable RAM store for refill.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add a cocotb regression for back-to-back stalled RAM stores that verifies retire-once behavior, same-cycle slot refill, preserved external write order, and continued fencing for EBREAK or a younger load behind the slot.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a same-cycle drain-and-refill path so a bufferable RAM store can retire into the existing slot while the older deferred store drains to dmem, with RVFI and mem_wdata metadata still tied to the younger retiring store and physical write ordering kept oldest-first.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Refine the pending-store fence so loads, MMIO/non-bufferable stores, and EBREAK still stall behind a full slot, but the exact dmem-ready drain cycle may admit one younger bufferable RAM store for refill.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add a cocotb regression for back-to-back stalled RAM stores that verifies retire-once behavior, same-cycle slot refill, preserved external write order, and continued fencing for EBREAK or a younger load behind the slot.\"}], \"outcome\": \"placement_failed\", \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": \"placement_failed\", \"seeds\": [null, null, null], \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r8s0 (placement_failed, n/a): On this FPGA, even a one-deep deferred-store slot can hit placement limits if `hazard_unit` and `mem_stage` try to use same-cycle `io_dmemReady` drain-and-refill control to let a younger RAM store retire into the slot, because the ready-gated refill/fence-release path itself becomes expensive under CoreMark's bursty store traffic.\"}\n","exit":0,"description":"Show prior slot-0 hypothesis records","truncated":false},"title":"Show prior slot-0 hypothesis records","time":{"start":1778870940620,"end":1778870940623}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07dc4ae3e0e4cd92016a076a994f90819aa48f366394f595ae"}},"id":"prt_e2cf86750001qgs2NoQHzHhHVu","sessionID":"ses_1d3082364ffeSUTMfN6QLwgtRN","messageID":"msg_e2cf83f67001xSOzx5vuEUCcIO"}}
