{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778873183095,"sessionID":"ses_1d2ee2901fferLJYlGEB1Ino4t","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_UyoifqDsIoLOjBq8lEEi74oW","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r10s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r10s1\n+title: \"Cold High-Half Multiply Offload\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current `bench` ALU still builds three 64-bit multiply products on every\n+  EX cycle (`mul_ss`, `mul_uu`, and `mul_su`) even though CoreMark's hot path\n+  is dominated by plain `MUL`, load/store traffic, and branches rather than the\n+  rarer high-half multiply instructions. The successful divider offload showed\n+  that this core benefits when cold RV32M work leaves the always-hot EX path,\n+  while the later shared-multiplier regression suggests simply reshaping the\n+  hot combinational multiplier cone is not enough.\n+\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Keep single-cycle `MUL` on the fast ALU path, but move only\n+  `MULH`/`MULHU`/`MULHSU` onto a small multi-cycle side unit launched from EX,\n+  using the same in-order stall-and-retire discipline already proven by the\n+  divider path. In the real build, `rtl/alu.sv` would stop synthesizing the\n+  signed/high-half multiplier trees on the common EX path; EX would instead\n+  latch operands and retirement metadata for high-half multiply ops, stall\n+  younger issue until the result is ready, and then emit exactly one EX/MEM\n+  result with unchanged RVFI behavior.\n+\n+  This is a structural change rather than another local ALU rewrite: it turns a\n+  cold RV32M subset into an explicit long-latency execution lane while\n+  preserving one-cycle throughput for the hot `MUL` case. That should reduce EX\n+  datapath pressure and routing cost without repeating the larger IPC hit that a\n+  full multi-cycle multiply scheme would impose on CoreMark.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Keep `MUL` single-cycle, preserve ALTOPS behavior, and remove real `MULH`/`MULHU`/`MULHSU` hardware from the always-hot ALU fast path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Detect high-half multiply ops, launch a long-latency side unit, hold the in-flight EX metadata until completion, and retire exactly one result with the existing single-issue ordering rules.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mulh_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Add a small iterative or registered high-half multiply unit that returns exact RV32M `MULH`/`MULHU`/`MULHSU` results without lengthening the common EX cycle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add any minimal control or pipeline metadata needed to classify high-half multiply ops as long-latency while keeping the existing RVFI-visible bundle contracts intact.\"\n+  - file: test/test_alu.py\n+    description: \"Extend arithmetic coverage so the real-build path still checks exact `MULH`/`MULHU`/`MULHSU` bit results after the datapath split.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add a pipeline-level regression that proves high-half multiply instructions stall younger issue, retire once, and preserve architectural writeback and RVFI ordering.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r10s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r10s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r10s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/