{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778874667503,"sessionID":"ses_1d2d0d3c9ffeSQE1aIf1BCjWph","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_8zXvhgrAUEdXfFK7B9RPdo87","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r11s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r11s1\n+title: \"Decode-Owned Hazard Source Sideband\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The remaining bench structural space is narrow. Fetch-side decoupling,\n+  prediction, and wider MEM-side buffering have mostly regressed, while the\n+  recent source-canonicalization failure showed that the false load-use issue\n+  is real but cannot be solved by rewriting RVFI-visible `rs1`/`rs2` fields.\n+  The current interlock still compares an older load destination against raw\n+  IF/ID bitfields, so legal single-source or zero-source instructions can\n+  still alias through immediate bits and burn bubbles that do not protect any\n+  real dependency.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Split the decode view used for hazards from the architectural source view\n+  used for RVFI. Add conservative `hazard_uses_rs1` / `hazard_uses_rs2`\n+  metadata that says whether the younger instruction truly needs each raw\n+  source for the current pipeline's existing dependency rules, but keep the\n+  raw source addresses themselves unchanged through ID/EX, MEM/WB, and RVFI.\n+\n+  Then gate the load-use compare with those liveness bits: OP-IMM, LOAD, and\n+  JALR stop stalling on bogus `rs2` aliases; JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, and\n+  EBREAK stop stalling on either fake source; BRANCH, R-type, STORE, and\n+  other real consumers remain conservative. This stays off the fragile fetch\n+  path and avoids the late-store-data / MEM fanout that already regressed, so\n+  it is a cleaner structural way to recover IPC from false dependencies.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Add conservative source-liveness outputs for hazard use, default-live on unknown or illegal encodings and clear them only inside validated opcode or funct matches.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Forward the new hazard-source liveness sideband while leaving raw rs1 and rs2 addresses plus RVFI-visible source data unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the decode liveness sideband from ID into hazard control so dependency tracking can use a separate non-RVFI hazard view.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate load-use comparisons with the new source-live bits to remove false stalls without relaxing STORE-data or other real dependencies.\"\n+  - file: test/test_decoder.py\n+    description: \"Add unit coverage for hazard-source liveness on single-source, zero-source, and conservative illegal encodings.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add pipeline tests proving aliasing immediates no longer stall after a load while true dependencies still stall and retire with unchanged RVFI source fields.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r11s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r11s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r11s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r11s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r11s1\n+title: \"Decode-Owned Hazard Source Sideband\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The remaining ben