lePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":200},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments</path>\\n<type>directory</type>\\n<entries>\\n.gitkeep\\nhypotheses/\\nlog.jsonl\\nprogress.png\\nrun_summary.json\\n\\n(5 entries)\\n</entries>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\".gitkeep\\nhypotheses/\\nlog.jsonl\\nprogress.png\\nrun_summary.json\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[]},\"title\":\"cores/bench/experiments\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778876090588,\"end\":1778876090589}},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"fc_0f09a8e92f6eff22016a077eba745c819aa49503cd0b180f83\"}},\"id\":\"prt_e2d4708db002NpNdM7RYFmQ0yd\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d46c907001fVS5iWgT9CFkUD\"}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876090592,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_Ei1Z5jhHwOY6ZLESY2M0wDsT\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"category.?[:=].?structural|\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 11 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 3: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Port v1-proven iterative divider into EX\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench baseline still carries real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators\\\\ninside the always-live combinational ALU. Archived bench runs on this same\\\\nbaseline show that moving divider-class ops off the fast EX path was the\\\\nbiggest structural win, because CoreMark almost never uses integer division\\\\nwhile the FPGA still pays its timing and LUT cost on every cycle.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench baseline still carries real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators\\\\ninside the always-live combinational ALU. Archived bench runs on this same\\\\nbaseline show that moving divider-class ops off the fast EX path was the\\\\nbiggest structural win, because CoreMark almost never uses integer division\\\\nwhile the FPGA still pays its timing and LUT cost on every cycle.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Reuse the already-proven iterative divider structure from cores/v1 and\\\\nintegrate it only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, leaving the existing single-cycle\\\\nRV32I and MUL-family datapaths intact. alu.sv stops synthesizing real\\\\ndivider hardware; ex_stage.sv launches the divider for divide-class ops,\\\\nholds the in-flight EX payload until completion, and commits exactly one\\\\nEX/MEM result with the original RVFI metadata and RV32M corner-case behavior\\\\npreserved. This is the l... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876090595,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_Ni433mCwB0h11fB2j7tTpIoO\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":300},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.23%): Pulling DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the one-cycle EX ALU and handling them with a stall-on-use iterative unit can buy large Fmax gains because CoreMark's hot loop is dominated by MUL, load/store, and branch traffic, so rare divide stalls cost less than keeping a 32-bit divider on the common critical path.\\n2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, -14.32%): On this core's combinational IF/ID path, adding ID-stage BTFNT and always-taken JAL prediction pulled decode, immediate-target add, and next-PC select onto the fetch critical path, and the resulting Fmax loss outweighed any CoreMark loop-branch bubble savings.\\n3: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r2s0 (regression, +5.57%): After DIV/REM already moved to `rtl/div_unit.sv`, splitting `alu_op` into hot/cold classes and replacing one flat ALU result `case` with separate `hot_result`/`m_result` muxes plus an `op[4]` final select regressed, suggesting bench's real EX critical path is elsewhere and extra class-select structure can cost more Fmax than it saves.\\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (improvement, +10.45%): Backend-only buffering of aligned normal-RAM stores is a good lever on this RTL because CoreMark issues enough stack/list/matrix/state stores that turning `io_dmemReady=0` on STOREs from a whole-pipeline freeze into a one-deep deferred write raises IPC, as long as younger memory ops and end-visible markers stay fenced behind the pending slot... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778876090690,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d470941001y55Jbv74YZkFGi\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d46c907001fVS5iWgT9CFkUD\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":42924,\"input\":32474,\"output\":251,\"reasoning\":471,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":9728}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778876091571,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d470cb3001kOPNdqsHscu8pT\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d470978001O5KD5LchMcQhBT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778876120072,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d477594002MZ0jxqmUcdw22T\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d470978001O5KD5LchMcQhBT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Looking for untried structural space around pipeline retiming rather than more frontend prediction or MEM buffering.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778876118420,\"end\":1778876120072},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0807ffc85fb35b90016a077ed6476881988f028f281807c2c6\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876120099,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_lBlI5PSE32L0bGs2KEyQ6Tzx\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"IF/ID|fetch buffer|pipeline|6-stage|split decode|regfile|operand|retim|retime|stage\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 30 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 2: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Iterative Cold Divider Off EX Path\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address generation, branch support, and\\\\nMUL. On a Tang Nano 20K, a full 32-bit divider is a strong candidate for\\\\nthe universal EX-stage critical path, yet CoreMark's timed loop is mostly\\\\nmultiply, load/store, and branch traffic and should pay little or no steady\\\\nstate penalty from slower divide instructions.\\\\n\\\\nThis makes divider extraction the highest-leverage micro-opt still missing\\\\nfrom the frozen bench fixture: it targets Fmax directly while preserving the\\\\nhot one-cycle behavior for the instructions that dominate CoreMark.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address generation, branch support, and\\\\nMUL. On a Tang Nano 20K, a full 32-bit divider is a strong candidate for\\\\nthe universal EX-stage critical path, yet CoreMark's timed loop is mostly\\\\nmultiply, load/store, and branch traffic and should pay little or no steady\\\\nstate penalty from slower divide instructions.\\\\n\\\\nThis makes divider extraction the highest-leverage micro-opt still missing\\\\nfrom the frozen bench fixture: it targets Fmax directly while preserving the\\\\nhot one-c... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876120101,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_AryfWZYefSr7DsjFCISJtq1T\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":220},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: // rtl/id_stage.sv\\n2: //\\n3: // Decode stage. Combinationally drives the regfile read ports and the\\n4: // ID/EX register's next-state from the IF/ID combinational bundle plus\\n5: // the regfile read data. The ID/EX register is owned by this module so\\n6: // the decoded view of instruction n is latched by end of cycle n+1.\\n7: //\\n8: // Latency:        1 cycle (ID/EX register clocked here).\\n9: // RVFI fields:    feeds rs1_addr, rs1_rdata, rs2_addr, rs2_rdata, insn,\\n10: //                 trap (via ctrl.is_illegal).\\n11: module id_stage (\\n12:   input  logic              clock,\\n13:   input  logic              reset,\\n14:   input  logic              stall,\\n15:   input  logic              flush,\\n16:   input  if_id_t  in,\\n17:   // regfile read interface\\n18:   output logic [4:0]        rs1_addr,\\n19:   output logic [4:0]        rs2_addr,\\n20:   input  logic [31:0]       rs1_data,\\n21:   input  logic [31:0]       rs2_data,\\n22:   // ID/EX register output\\n23:   output id_ex_t  out\\n24: );\\n25: \\n26:   // ── Combinational decode ────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n27:   logic [4:0]  dec_alu_op;\\n28:   logic        dec_alu_src;\\n29:   logic [2:0]  dec_branch_op;\\n30:   logic        dec_is_branch;\\n31:   logic        dec_is_jump;\\n32:   logic        dec_is_jalr;\\n33:   logic        dec_is_lui;\\n34:   logic        dec_is_auipc;\\n35:   logic        dec_mem_read;\\n36:   logic        dec_mem_write;\\n37:   logic [1:0]  dec_mem_width;\\n38:   logic  ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876120105,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_4KajRMKkBYgwxkkx3b8J2M0N\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":220},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: // rtl/if_stage.sv\\n2: //\\n3: // Instruction fetch stage. Holds the PC register; the IF/ID payload\\n4: // (pc + instr + valid) is *combinational* — there is no separate IF/ID\\n5: // flop in this microarchitecture, the next-stage's ID/EX register\\n6: // captures everything one cycle later.\\n7: //\\n8: // On flush or redirect, the instruction emitted to ID is forced to NOP\\n9: // (`0x00000013` = ADDI x0,x0,0). This prevents the hazard unit from\\n10: // observing a real rs1/rs2 from a wrong-path instruction and inserting\\n11: // a spurious load-use stall the cycle after a taken branch.\\n12: //\\n13: // Latency:        PC-reg update is synchronous; output is combinational.\\n14: // RVFI fields:    feeds pc_rdata (via ID/EX/MEM/WB) and pc_wdata (via\\n15: //                 EX-stage redirect).\\n16: module if_stage (\\n17:   input  logic              clock,\\n18:   input  logic              reset,\\n19:   input  logic              stall,            // hold PC (load-use)\\n20:   input  logic              flush,            // emit NOP into ID this cycle\\n21:   input  logic              redirect,         // EX has resolved a branch/jump\\n22:   input  logic [31:0]       redirect_target,\\n23:   output logic [31:0]       imem_addr,\\n24:   input  logic [31:0]       imem_data,\\n25:   output if_id_t  out\\n26: );\\n27: \\n28:   localparam logic [31:0] RESET_PC = 32'h0000_0000;\\n29: \\n30:   logic [31:0] pc;\\n31:   logic [31:0] next_pc;\\n32: \\n33:   always_comb begin\\n34:     next_pc... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778876120201,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d477c88001HOJXetAxBEe41t\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d470978001O5KD5LchMcQhBT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":51934,\"input\":8384,\"output\":264,\"reasoning\":1302,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":41984}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778876121165,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d47804d0011PiIEZa8PpbewR\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d477cb1002BPoG2R71HR96uB\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778876222105,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d48fab9001zRIRuntKXfEsvH\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d477cb1002BPoG2R71HR96uB\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Checking whether an RVFI-source refresh path has already been tried; if not, that may be the narrow structural opening left.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778876218041,\"end\":1778876222103},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_011954f9665f43d3016a077f39d1cc8199b1b175f69a7be9c6\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876222148,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_GcPStvDcGFaiApLGLGF1I1y5\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":260},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: // rtl/ex_stage.sv\\n2: //\\n3: // Execute stage. Resolves the operand muxes (forwarding from EX/MEM and\\n4: // MEM/WB), runs the ALU, resolves branches, computes the redirect\\n5: // target. Owns the EX/MEM pipeline register.\\n6: //\\n7: // Forwarding select encoding (driven by forward_unit):\\n8: //   00 = ID/EX register value (no forward)\\n9: //   01 = EX/MEM aluResult (instruction immediately ahead in MEM)\\n10: //   10 = MEM/WB result (instruction two ahead, post regfile-write mux)\\n11: //\\n12: // DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU leave the common ALU path: the EX stage launches them\\n13: // into div_unit and stalls younger issue until the result is ready.\\n14: //\\n15: // Latency:        1 cycle for non-div ops; multi-cycle for divide-class ops.\\n16: // RVFI fields:    feeds pc_wdata (= pc_next), the rd_wdata path for\\n17: //                 ALU and JAL/JALR (PC+4), and the branch resolve.\\n18: module ex_stage (\\n19:   input  logic               clock,\\n20:   input  logic               reset,\\n21:   input  logic               stall,         // freeze EX/MEM register (dmem stall)\\n22:   input  id_ex_t   in,\\n23:   input  logic [1:0]         fwd_rs1_sel,\\n24:   input  logic [1:0]         fwd_rs2_sel,\\n25:   input  logic [31:0]        fwd_ex_mem,    // EX/MEM.alu_result (registered)\\n26:   input  logic [31:0]        fwd_mem_wb,    // WB-stage write-data mux output\\n27:   output ex_mem_t  out,\\n28:   output logic               div_stall,\\n29:   output logic               redir... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876222150,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_Z689sc5mPBUjZYiNoYhHjaC3\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":320},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: // rtl/mem_stage.sv\\n2: //\\n3: // Memory access stage. Drives the dmem read/write ports combinationally\\n4: // from the EX/MEM register, and sign/zero-extends the loaded data into\\n5: // the MEM/WB register.\\n6: //\\n7: // Byte-lane discipline:\\n8: //   - Write data is replicated across all four byte lanes; the\\n9: //     byte-mask (mem_wmask) selects the actual destination bytes.\\n10: //   - Load: shift the raw word right by `addr[1:0]*8`, then sign- or\\n11: //     zero-extend the low 8/16 bits per the LB/LBU/LH/LHU encoding.\\n12: //   - For RVFI ALIGNED_MEM, mem_addr is reported word-aligned and the\\n13: //     byte position is captured in mem_rmask / mem_wmask.\\n14: //\\n15: // Latency:        1 cycle (MEM/WB register clocked here).\\n16: // RVFI fields:    feeds mem_addr, mem_rmask, mem_wmask, mem_rdata,\\n17: //                 mem_wdata, plus rd_wdata via the loaded-data path.\\n18: module mem_stage (\\n19:   input  logic               clock,\\n20:   input  logic               reset,\\n21:   input  logic               dmem_ready,\\n22:   // hold_wb: dmem stall is in effect. MEM/WB's data fields are RETAINED\\n23:   // (so the previously-retired LOAD's `rd` / `read_data` / `ctrl.reg_write`\\n24:   // remain visible to forward_unit), but `valid` is cleared so:\\n25:   //   - rvfi_order doesn't increment for held cycles\\n26:   //   - wb_stage doesn't write the regfile twice\\n27:   // Zeroing the whole register would lose the LOAD's load_data, breaking\\n28:   // M... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876222153,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_CoP6lMWFicB8cVeO1bVkWD0a\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"rvfi.*rs1|rvfi.*rs2|source refresh|architectural source|late source|reg_check|stale rs|fresh rs\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 15 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 4: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 8, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire an ID-stage prediction path i... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778876222262,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d490b35001qHRSo21XJ0iMsL\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d477cb1002BPoG2R71HR96uB\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":69939,\"input\":181,\"output\":273,\"reasoning\":1389,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":68096}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778876223725,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d4910eb001rKWkt5aWSqzTdK\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d490b59001a4akBLMUKJl0vP\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778876290786,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d4a0f2400275dbH7SYSdvB7v\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d490b59001a4akBLMUKJl0vP\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Pulling the exact failure note for the last structural hazard-sideband attempt so the new hypothesis can address that gap directly.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778876288804,\"end\":1778876290786},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_01b79f745220589d016a077f80a770819a8c2b716622946b46\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260515-002-r12s1.log","time":{"start":1778876314914,"end":1778876314921}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_006921e82cfb4729016a077f9a8f9881988451e6e1debcf630"}},"id":"prt_e2d4a74250010TYTqCSuagMGI1","sessionID":"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g","messageID":"msg_e2d4a5c2e001ovRW4iW1lTM2OB"}}
