{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778876346047,"sessionID":"ses_1d2b937bbffejBUFyDIrJ1Mo8g","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_lD49kdbbY858kPVm5rYS6lPj","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r12s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r12s1\n+title: \"Hazard Liveness with RVFI Source Repair\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The remaining structural space on `bench` is narrow, and the recent hazard\n+  sideband failure clarified exactly why. False load-use stalls from raw\n+  IF/ID bitfield aliases are still a real IPC loss, but simply teaching the\n+  interlock which sources are live is not enough because RVFI still expects the\n+  raw encoded `rs1`/`rs2` read-data lanes to be fresh at retirement.\n+\n+  That leaves one focused opening: pair the hazard-sideband idea with an\n+  explicit architectural-source repair path, so the core can stop bubbling on\n+  provably-unused EX operands without letting stale or mis-forwarded source\n+  values leak into `rvfi_rs*_rdata`.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Split \"source needed for EX timing\" from \"source value must be correct for\n+  RVFI\" and handle both deliberately. Decode conservative\n+  `hazard_uses_rs1` / `hazard_uses_rs2` sidebands for load-use purposes, but\n+  keep the raw source addresses unchanged in the pipeline. When a younger\n+  instruction is allowed past an older load only because an aliased source is\n+  unused in EX, carry a small repair flag so MEM/WB rewrites that source value\n+  from the matching WB load result before retirement.\n+\n+  This stays off the fragile fetch path, keeps STORE `rs2` conservative, and\n+  avoids the broad MEM-side store-data fanout that already regressed. The key\n+  structural change is adding a precise RVFI-source-refresh lane alongside the\n+  hazard liveness sideband, so OP-IMM, LOAD, JAL, LUI/AUIPC, FENCE, and EBREAK\n+  can stop paying bogus load-use bubbles while formal still sees fresh\n+  `rvfi_rs1_rdata` / `rvfi_rs2_rdata` for the raw encoded source fields.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact sideband bits to the pipeline bundles for hazard-source liveness and one-cycle-late RVFI source repair, while keeping the existing raw `rs1_addr` / `rs2_addr` fields unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Decode conservative `hazard_uses_rs1` / `hazard_uses_rs2` metadata for each legal opcode class and latch the sideband next to the existing raw source addresses and values.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate the load-use interlock with the decoded liveness sideband so only true EX-time source dependencies still stall, while STORE data and unknown/illegal cases remain conservative.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Detect the specific case where an unused raw source would otherwise pick up an EX/MEM load-address forward and mark that source for later WB-based repair instead of letting stale RVFI state retire.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Apply the flagged RVFI source repair in MEM/WB by replacing the affected `rs1_val` / `rs2_val` with the matching WB load result just before retirement-visible state is registered.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the new hazard-liveness and source-repair sidebands between ID, hazard control, EX, and MEM while preserving the current top-level nret=1 and RVFI contract.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add a regression that exercises a false load-use alias on an instruction with an architecturally-unused source and checks both bubble removal and correct RVFI-visible source read data.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp