{"type":"text","timestamp":1778879663469,"sessionID":"ses_1d28633a4ffexDsv3Er74Ax1zs","part":{"id":"prt_e2d7d897f002s44ljYSJzIJvRK","messageID":"msg_e2d7c1e06001hJcRDYsfv72EHg","sessionID":"ses_1d28633a4ffexDsv3Er74Ax1zs","type":"text","text":"Writing the hypothesis YAML now. I’m anchoring it on a narrower, registered one-entry load replay path, because the logs say load-stall hiding helps IPC but bench loses when the replay lookup sits on the live MEM stall path.","time":{"start":1778879662463,"end":1778879663468},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_01c607e7b70cb841016a078cae53a8819894f730ff89124d1d","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778879678556,"sessionID":"ses_1d28633a4ffexDsv3Er74Ax1zs","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_uV1YjYazlUsG57OgUPgnwpOc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r14s1\n+title: \"Registered One-Entry Load Replay Latch\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  `bench`'s proven structural wins both came from backend-only stall handling:\n+  cold divide offload and the one-deep deferred store slot. The next obvious\n+  remaining IPC loss is load-side dmem backpressure. Prior bench experiments\n+  already showed that replaying hot loads can recover cycles, but the direct\n+  MEM-stage replay-table lookup, tag compare, and stall-escape logic cost too\n+  much Fmax when they sat on the live `io_dmemReady` path.\n+\n+  The best structural follow-up is therefore not another wider replay table or\n+  fetch-side structure, but a much smaller load replay mechanism that keeps the\n+  timing cost local and attacks only repeated exact-word load stalls.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a one-entry last-load replay latch for aligned normal-RAM words and turn\n+  it into a registered replay candidate instead of a same-cycle MEM lookup.\n+  Successful ready loads refresh the latch with `{aligned_addr, raw_word}`.\n+  When a younger aligned load to the same word is about to enter MEM, capture a\n+  replay-eligible sideband once; if that load later sees `io_dmemReady=0`, MEM\n+  may complete it from the registered candidate rather than freezing the whole\n+  pipeline.\n+\n+  Keep the mechanism conservative so it stays cheaper than the prior replay\n+  buffer: exact aligned-word matches only, no effect for MMIO, misaligned\n+  accesses, or any cycle with a pending deferred store, and invalidate or\n+  refresh the latch on same-word stores so stale data never leaks into physical\n+  loads or RVFI `mem_rdata`. This stays off the fragile fetch path, avoids a\n+  broader MEM replay table, and targets the exact load-stall opportunity that\n+  bench has already identified without reintroducing the timing shape that\n+  previously regressed.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact replay-candidate sideband fields so a repeated aligned load can carry prequalified last-load replay metadata into MEM without another live table lookup.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the replay-candidate signal path between MEM-side state and hazard control while preserving the existing single-channel RVFI contract and store-slot fencing.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Treat dmem-not-ready as a true pipeline stall only when the in-flight memory op cannot complete from the registered load-replay candidate; keep loads/stores with ordering risk conservative.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add the one-entry last-load latch, exact-hit replay completion, and conservative invalidation/update rules around stores and the deferred RAM-store slot so replayed loads return RVFI-correct `mem_rdata` and `rd_wdata`.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add cocotb coverage for a forced dmem stall on a repeated RAM load that should retire from replay, plus a stale-data guard case showing an intervening store blocks or refreshes the latch before replay is allowed.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r14s1\n+title: \"Registered One-Entry Load Replay Latch\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  `bench`'s proven structural wins both came from backend-only stall handling:\n+  cold divide offload and the one-deep deferred store slot. The next obvious\n+  remaining IPC loss is load-side dmem backpressure. Prior bench experiments\n+  already showed that replaying hot loads can recover cycles, but the direct\n+  MEM-stage replay-table lookup, tag compare, and stall-escape logic cost too\n+  much Fmax when they sat on the live `io_dmemReady` path.\n+\n+  The best structural follow-up is therefore not another wider replay table or\n+  fetch-side structure, but a much smaller load replay mechanism that keeps the\n+  timing cost local and attacks only repeated exact-word load stalls.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a one-entry last-load replay latch for aligned normal-RAM words and turn\n+  it into a registered replay candidate instead of a same-cycle MEM lookup.\n+  Successful ready loads refresh the latch with `{aligned_addr, raw_word}`.\n+  When a younger aligned load to the same word is about to enter MEM, capture a\n+  replay-eligible sideband once; if that load later sees `io_dmemReady=0`, MEM\n+  may complete it from the registered candidate rather than freezing the whole\n+  pipeline.\n+\n+  Keep the mechanism conservative so it stays cheaper than the prior replay\n+  buffer: exact aligned-word matches only, no effect for MMIO, misaligned\n+  accesses, or any cycle with a pending deferred store, and invalidate or\n+  refresh the latch on same-word stores so stale data never leaks into physical\n+  loads or RVFI `mem_rdata`. This stays off the fragile fetch path, avoids a\n+  broader MEM replay table, and targets the exact load-stall opportunity that\n+  bench has already identified without reintroducing the timing shape that\n+  previously regressed.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact replay-candidate sideband fields so a repeated aligned load can carry prequalified last-load replay metadata into MEM without another live table lookup.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the replay-candidate signal path between MEM-side state and hazard control while preserving the existing single-channel RVFI contract and store-slot fencing.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Treat dmem-not-ready as a true pipeline stall only when the in-flight memory op cannot complete from the registered load-replay candidate; keep loads/stores with ordering risk conservative.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add the one-entry last-load latch, exact-hit replay completion, and conservative invalidation/update rules around stores and the deferred RAM-store slot so replayed loads return RVFI-correct `mem_rdata` and `rd_wdata`.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add cocotb coverage for a forced dmem stall on a repeated RAM load that should retire from replay, plus a stale-data guard case showing an intervening store blocks or refreshes the latch before replay is allowed.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r14s1\n+title: \"Registered One-Entry Load Replay Latch\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  `bench`'s proven structural wins both came from backend-only stall handling:\n+  cold divide offload and the one-deep deferred store slot. The next obvious\n+  remaining IPC loss is load-side dmem backpressure. Prior bench experiments\n+  already showed that replaying hot loads can recover cycles, but the direct\n+  MEM-stage replay-table lookup, tag compare, and stall-escape logic cost too\n+  much Fmax when they sat on the live `io_dmemReady` path.\n+\n+  The best structural follow-up is therefore not another wider replay table or\n+  fetch-side structure, but a much smaller load replay mechanism that keeps the\n+  timing cost local and attacks only repeated exact-word load stalls.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a one-entry last-load replay latch for aligned normal-RAM words and turn\n+  it into a registered replay candidate instead of a same-cycle MEM lookup.\n+  Successful ready loads refresh the latch with `{aligned_addr, raw_word}`.\n+  When a younger aligned load to the same word is about to enter MEM, capture a\n+  replay-eligible sideband once; if that load later sees `io_dmemReady=0`, MEM\n+  may complete it from the registered candidate rather than freezing the whole\n+  pipeline.\n+\n+  Keep the mechanism conservative so it stays cheaper than the prior replay\n+  buffer: exact aligned-word matches only, no effect for MMIO, misaligned\n+  accesses, or any cycle with a pending deferred store, and invalidate or\n+  refresh the latch on same-word stores so stale data never leaks into physical\n+  loads or RVFI `mem_rdata`. This stays off the fragile fetch path, avoids a\n+  broader MEM replay table, and targets the exact load-stall opportunity that\n+  bench has already identified without reintroducing the timing shape that\n+  previously regressed.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact replay-candidate sideband fields so a repeated aligned load can carry prequalified last-load replay metadata into MEM without another live table lookup.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the replay-candidate signal path between MEM-side state and hazard control while preserving the existing single-channel RVFI contract and store-slot fencing.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Treat dmem-not-ready as a true pipeline stall only when the in-flight memory op cannot complete from the registered load-replay candidate; keep loads/stores with ordering risk conservative.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add the one-entry last-load latch, exact-hit replay completion, and conservative invalidation/update rules around stores and the deferred RAM-store slot so replayed loads return RVFI-correct `mem_rdata` and `rd_wdata`.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add cocotb coverage for a forced dmem stall on a repeated RAM load that should retire from replay, plus a stale-data guard case showing an intervening store blocks or refreshes the latch before replay is allowed.\"\n","additions":45,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778879678552,"end":1778879678555}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01c607e7b70cb841016a078caf5ebc8198850ff1f8c3deba07"}},"id":"prt_e2d7d8d70001tx9JUb5C4PFyaR","sessionID":"ses_1d28633a4ffexDsv3Er74Ax1zs","messageID":"msg_e2d7c1e06001hJcRDYsfv72EHg"}}
