{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778882471901,"sessionID":"ses_1d25b7e98ffeiWzznDDW6uMkiU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_N20RblzQBk8BF9DxqKp8TzeT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r15s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r15s1\n+title: \"Two-Cycle Pipelined Multiply Lane\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The remaining `bench` structural space is narrow: fetch-side ideas have mostly\n+  been Fmax-negative, and wider MEM-side buffering or replay logic has either\n+  regressed or failed placement. The still-untried always-hot structure is the\n+  multiply cone in `rtl/alu.sv`, which currently builds three 64-bit products on\n+  every EX cycle even though only one MUL-family result is ever used.\n+\n+  Prior lessons already bracket the local alternatives. Shared combinational\n+  multiplier reshaping regressed, which suggests the win is not in another mux\n+  rewrite, and high-half-only offload regressed because plain `MUL` still left\n+  the DSP-heavy path on the common EX cone. That makes a full multiply-lane\n+  retiming the most credible remaining structural lever.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move `MUL`, `MULH`, `MULHU`, and `MULHSU` out of the one-cycle ALU and into a\n+  dedicated two-cycle pipelined `rtl/mul_unit.sv` that is launched from EX and\n+  returns exactly one result into the existing EX/MEM retirement path. In the\n+  normal build, `rtl/alu.sv` would stop synthesizing the three parallel 64-bit\n+  multiply trees, leaving the hot EX datapath focused on RV32I arithmetic,\n+  branch/jump resolution, address generation, and the already-offloaded divider.\n+\n+  Keep the design single-issue and in-order: when a MUL-family op enters EX,\n+  latch its operands plus retirement metadata, hold younger issue until the\n+  two-cycle result comes back, and then emit the same architecturally visible\n+  writeback and RVFI data the current single-cycle path would have produced.\n+  This is a stronger version of the already-proven \"move cold/expensive math off\n+  the universal EX path\" strategy: unlike the failed high-half-only attempt, it\n+  actually removes all multiplier delay from the common cycle, while the IPC\n+  cost is bounded to one extra cycle on multiply instructions instead of on\n+  every instruction.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/mul_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Add a two-cycle RV32M multiply unit that returns exact `MUL`/`MULH`/`MULHU`/`MULHSU` results with the same signedness rules as the current ALU path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Launch MUL-family ops into the new pipeline, hold EX/MEM until the multiply result is ready, and preserve existing single-retire metadata and forwarding-visible results.\"\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Remove real multiply hardware from the normal combinational ALU path while keeping the formal ALTOPS behavior aligned with riscv-formal expectations.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Plumb a unified long-op stall from EX so hazard control treats the new multiply lane the same way it already treats divide-class backpressure.\"\n+  - file: test/test_mul_unit.py\n+    description: \"Add focused cocotb vectors for the new multiply lane so exact RV32M bit results remain guarded after MUL-family logic leaves `rtl/alu.sv`.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r15s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r15s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r15s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bon