es the synthesis tool to infer\\nmultiple wide multipliers and large cross-products that consume DSP\\nblocks and routing resources around the EX stage.  CoreMark is\\nmultiply-heavy (matrix operations), so the ALU multiplier path is\\nlikely on or near the critical path.  By sharing a single 64-bit\\nmultiplier and selecting the signedness mode per-op, we cut the\\nmultiplier area by roughly two thirds and relieve routing\\ncongestion, which should raise median Fmax with zero IPC impact.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the three always-computed 64-bit products in alu.sv with one\\nshared 64-bit multiplier whose operands are muxed per the active ALU\\nop: unsigned*unsigned for MUL/MULHU, signed*signed for MULH, and\\nsigned*unsigned for MULHSU.  Add a small case block before the\\nmultiplication that selects the correctly-extended a and b inputs.\\nThe DIV/REM family remains combinational (unchanged); only the MUL\\nfamily is touched.  This reduces inferred multi...\n\n(Results truncated: showing 100 of 675 matches (575 hidden). Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":675,"truncated":true},"title":"\"title\":|\"id\":|\"outcome\":|\"fitness\":|\"delta_pct\":|\"hypothesis\":","time":{"start":1778835228978,"end":1778835229081}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0633164f32c99733016a06df1cda40819981a8c7d48a696b22"}},"id":"prt_e2ad7892f001Ofj50UwoKPMH7l","sessionID":"ses_1d5292540ffepjDgtvUr54dZ4p","messageID":"msg_e2ad76100001RTYbur3yGWf1bp"}}
