ruction. On a subsequent\\nsingle-cycle imem stall the buffered instruction keeps the decode stage fed,\\nturning an otherwise dead cycle into productive work. This is a pure\\nstructural decoupling with no ISA or pipeline-depth change.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 1-entry skid buffer inside `if_stage.sv` consisting of a single\\n`if_id_t` register and a valid bit. When the downstream ID stage is stalled\\n(`stall_id` asserted) the buffer latches the current valid fetch bundle;\\nwhen valid it drives the `out` port instead of the raw combinational fetch.\\nThe buffer is flushed on redirect so wrong-path instructions never pollute\\nit.  Restructure `hazard_unit.sv` so that `stall_if` only asserts when the\\nbuffer is already full (second consecutive ID stall) or on multi-cycle dmem\\nstalls, and so that `flush_if` is suppressed during single-cycle imem stalls\\nwhen the buffer can cover the ready-drop. Wire the buffer status signals\\nthrough `core.sv`. This removes the front-end idle cycles that currently\\noccur during load-use bubbles and one-cycle imem stalls.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a 1-entry skid buffer (if_id_t regist...\n  Line 33: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-002-r11s1\", \"title\": \"1-entry skid buffer in IF to decouple fetch from back-end stalls\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline front-end stalls the PC on every load-use hazard and dmem stall,\\nand emits NOPs on every imem ready-drop. CoreMark cosim injects ~22% random\\nimem/dmem stalls. A tiny 1-entry skid buffer decouples fetch from decode: it\\ncaptures the fetched instruction when the back-end cannot accept it, allowing\\nthe PC to advance and prefetch the next instruction. On a subsequent\\nsingle-cycle stall the buffered instruction keeps the decode stage fed,\\nturning an otherwise dead cycle into productive work. Two prior structural\\nattempts