redict taken and decrement the counter.\\n  - down-counter == 0 \\u2192 predict not-taken.\\nIn EX, resolved backward branches update the table:\\n  - During training (confidence low) the table counts taken outcomes;\\n    the first not-taken exit stores the count as the trained length\\n    and sets confidence high.\\n  - On a correct ex...\n  Line 37: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260514-003-r12s2\", \"title\": \"Add 4-entry return-address stack for JALR prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current predictor correctly handles conditional branches (32-entry BHT)\\nand JAL (always-taken), but JALR is never predicted. Every function return\\ncauses a 2-cycle redirect bubble in EX. CoreMark contains many small function\\ncalls; a return-address stack predicts return targets with near-perfect\\naccuracy for a tiny area cost (~130 flops), improving IPC without degrading\\nFmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current predictor correctly handles conditional branches (32-entry BHT)\\nand JAL (always-taken), but JALR is never predicted. Every function return\\ncauses a 2-cycle redirect bubble in EX. CoreMark contains many small function\\ncalls; a return-address stack predicts return targets with near-perfect\\naccuracy for a tiny area cost (~130 flops), improving IPC without degrading\\nFmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 4-entry return-address stack (RAS) to the IF stage. Push PC+4 on\\nany JAL or JALR call (rd = x1/x5). Pop the RAS and predict taken on any\\nJALR return (rd = x0, rs1 = x1/x5). Thread the predicted target through a\\nnew `pred_target` field in the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles. In EX stage,\\ncompare the actual JALR target with `pred_target`; only redirect on\\nmispredict or when JALR was not predicted. This eliminates the redirect\\nbubble on correct function returns.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add `pred_target` 