{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778835362586,"sessionID":"ses_1d5292540ffepjDgtvUr54dZ4p","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Zm5HVKdrVAO59BShVtTF3oLE","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\n+title: \"Port v1-proven iterative divider into EX\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current bench baseline still carries real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators\n+  inside the always-live combinational ALU. Archived bench runs on this same\n+  baseline show that moving divider-class ops off the fast EX path was the\n+  biggest structural win, because CoreMark almost never uses integer division\n+  while the FPGA still pays its timing and LUT cost on every cycle.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Reuse the already-proven iterative divider structure from cores/v1 and\n+  integrate it only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, leaving the existing single-cycle\n+  RV32I and MUL-family datapaths intact. alu.sv stops synthesizing real\n+  divider hardware; ex_stage.sv launches the divider for divide-class ops,\n+  holds the in-flight EX payload until completion, and commits exactly one\n+  EX/MEM result with the original RVFI metadata and RV32M corner-case behavior\n+  preserved. This is the lowest-risk structural path to a large Fmax gain on\n+  the current baseline because it attacks the known worst cone without adding\n+  fetch-side control, store reordering, or multiply bubbles.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 20\n+  confidence: high\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/div_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Add the v1-proven iterative RV32 divider/remainder unit with ALTOPS compatibility and exact divide-by-zero / INT_MIN-overflow semantics.\"\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU hardware from the normal ALU fast path while keeping existing RV32I and MUL-family behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Detect divide-class ops, launch the divider, hold the EX instruction and forwarded operands while it runs, and emit one EX/MEM result only on completion.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Add an EX long-op busy input so IF/ID/EX stall behind an in-flight divider exactly like a structural back-end hold.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the divider busy/result handshake between EX and the hazard logic without changing the top-level IO contract or RVFI port shape.\"\n+  - file: test/test_alu.py\n+    description: \"Retarget combinational ALU tests to the retained fast-path ops and keep MUL-family exact-result coverage after divider removal from alu.sv.\"\n+  - file: test/test_div_unit.py\n+    description: \"Add exact RV32M DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU vectors so arithmetic correctness stays loudly checked after the divider moves into its own structural unit.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\n+title: \"Port v1-proven iterative divider into EX\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current bench baseline still carries real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators\n+  inside the always-live combinational ALU. Archived bench runs on this same\n+  baseline show that moving divider-class ops off the fast EX path was the\n+  biggest structural win, because CoreMark almost never uses integer division\n+  while the FPGA still pays its timing and LUT cost on every cycle.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Reuse the already-proven iterative divider structure from cores/v1 and\n+  integrate it only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, leaving the existing single-cycle\n+  RV32I and MUL-family datapaths intact. alu.sv stops synthesizing real\n+  divider hardware; ex_stage.sv launches the divider for divide-class ops,\n+  holds the in-flight EX payload until completion, and commits exactly one\n+  EX/MEM result with the original RVFI metadata and RV32M corner-case behavior\n+  preserved. This is the lowest-risk structural path to a large Fmax gain on\n+  the current baseline because it attacks the known worst cone without adding\n+  fetch-side control, store reordering, or multiply bubbles.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 20\n+  confidence: high\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/div_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Add the v1-proven iterative RV32 divider/remainder unit with ALTOPS compatibility and exact divide-by-zero / INT_MIN-overflow semantics.\"\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU hardware from the normal ALU fast path while keeping existing RV32I and MUL-family behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Detect divide-class ops, launch the divider, hold the EX instruction and forwarded operands while it runs, and emit one EX/MEM result only on completion.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Add an EX long-op busy input so IF/ID/EX stall behind an in-flight divider exactly like a structural back-end hold.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the divider busy/result handshake between EX and the hazard logic without changing the top-level IO contract or RVFI port shape.\"\n+  - file: test/test_alu.py\n+    description: \"Retarget combinational ALU tests to the retained fast-path ops and keep MUL-family exact-result coverage after divider removal from alu.sv.\"\n+  - file: test/test_div_unit.py\n+    description: \"Add exact RV32M DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU vectors so arithmetic correctness stays loudly checked after the divider moves into its own structural unit.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r1s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\n+title: \"Port v1-proven iterative divider into EX\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current bench baseline still carries real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators\n+  inside the always-live combinational ALU. Archived bench runs on this same\n+  baseline show that moving divider-class ops off the fast EX path was the\n+  biggest structural win, because CoreMark almost never uses integer division\n+  while the FPGA still pays its timing and LUT cost on every cycle.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Reuse the already-proven iterative divider structure from cores/v1 and\n+  integrate it only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, leaving the existing single-cycle\n+  RV32I and MUL-family datapaths intact. alu.sv stops synthesizing real\n+  divider hardware; ex_stage.sv launches the divider for divide-class ops,\n+  holds the in-flight EX payload until completion, and commits exactly 