sed forward conditional branches. A tiny forward-only override\\nshould retain much of the cycle-count gain with far less table area, fanout,\\nand IF routing pressure than the full agree predictor.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 16-entry PC-indexed two-bit saturating override table that is consulted\\nonly for legal, aligned, forward B-type conditional branches. Backward\\nbranches keep the current static taken prediction, and direct JAL prediction\\nremains unchanged. Forward branches cold-start as strongly not-taken so the\\nreset behavior exactly matches the current... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n\n(Showing lines 16-16 of 74. Use offset=17 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"id\": \"hyp-20260428-009-r5s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny Forward-Branch Override Predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current best frontend already predicts backward conditional branches and\\ndirect JAL targets in IF, reaching 324.48 fitness. The 64-entry agree\\npredictor experiment showed that residual conditional-branch misses still\\nmatter: it reduced CoreMark cycles from 4,259,699 to 4,194,484, but the\\nlarger always-consulted table cost enough Fmax to regress overall fitness.\\nThat result points to a narrower predictor: keep the proven BTFNT and direct\\nJAL behavior intact, but learn only the static predictor's most expensive\\nblind spot, biased forward conditional branches. A tiny forward-only override\\nshould retain much of the cycle-count gain with far less table area, fanout,\\nand IF routing pressure than the full agree predictor.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current best frontend already predicts backward conditional branches and\\ndirect JAL targets in IF, reaching 324.48 fitness. The 64-entry agree\\npredictor experiment showed that residual conditional-branch misses still\\nmatter: it reduced CoreMark cycles from 4,259,699 to 4,194,484, but the\\nlarger always-consulted table cost enough Fmax to regress overall fi