{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778838710935,"sessionID":"ses_1d4f68af8ffe5pM27eXjh0W1gN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_4oSZXXIwaNGo1TBuQCkUltw0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r3s2.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r3s2.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-003-r3s2\n2: title: \"Tiny EX-trained taken-target cache\"\n3: category: predictor\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The two failed predictor attempts exposed the boundary on this core: bench\n6:   does not tolerate extra decode, immediate-generation, or replay-control work\n7:   on the frontend critical path. But CoreMark is still rich in tight counted\n8:   loops and unconditional jumps, so always waiting for EX to redirect leaves\n9:   predictable control-flow bubbles on the table.\n10: \n11:   The remaining predictor opportunity is a much smaller one: predict only from\n12:   already-resolved history, with a fetch-side structure light enough that the\n13:   Fmax cost stays below the IPC gain.\n14: hypothesis: |\n15:   Add a very small direct-mapped taken-target cache in IF, trained only by\n16:   control-flow instructions once EX has already resolved their real next PC.\n17:   On a tag hit, IF speculatively uses the cached target instead of `pc + 4`;\n18:   on a miss, fetch stays exactly as it is today. This avoids any ID-stage\n19:   branch decode, immediate reconstruction, or same-cycle target add.\n20: \n21:   The predictor should only cache taken conditional branches and unconditional\n22:   jumps, with EX comparing the predicted next PC against the architectural one\n23:   and asserting recovery only on mismatch. A last-taken policy is a good fit\n24:   for CoreMark's loop backedges: it predicts the many taken iterations while\n25:   missing only on loop exit, and the hardware cost is just a tiny tag/target\n26:   array plus one fetch-side compare and mux.\n27: expected_impact:\n28:   fitness_delta_pct: 6\n29:   confidence: medium\n30: changes:\n31:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n32:     description: \"Add prediction metadata fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so EX can validate speculative next-PC choices against the architectural result.\"\n33:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n34:     description: \"Implement a tiny direct-mapped taken-target cache indexed by fetch PC, use it to choose speculative next PC, and expose the predicted next-PC metadata alongside the fetched instruction.\"\n35:   - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n36:     description: \"Latch the fetch-stage prediction metadata into the ID/EX register without adding any new decode-stage branch or immediate logic.\"\n37:   - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n38:     description: \"Train the cache from resolved taken branches and jumps, compare predicted vs actual next PC, and request redirect recovery only on mispredict.\"\n39:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n40:     description: \"Wire the IF predictor update path from EX and keep the existing single-channel RVFI and bus interfaces unchanged while redirect now means recovery-only for correctly predicted taken control flow.\"\n\n(End of file - total 40 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Tiny EX-trained taken-target cache\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The two failed predictor attempts exposed the boundary on this core: bench\n  does not tolerate extra decode, immediate-generation, or replay-control work\n  on the frontend critical path. But CoreMark is still rich in tight counted\n  loops and unconditional jumps, so always waiting for EX to redirect leaves\n  predictable control-flow bubbles on the table.\n\n  The remaining predictor opportunity is a much smaller one: predict only from\n  already-resolved history, with a fetch-side structure light enough that the\n  Fmax cost stays below the IPC gain.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a very small direct-mapped taken-target cache in IF, trained only by\n  control-flow instructions once EX has already resolved their real next PC.\n  On a tag hit, IF speculatively uses the cached target instead of `pc + 4`;\n  on a miss, fetch stays exactly as it is today. This avoids any ID-stage\n  branch decode, immediate reconstruction, or same-cycle target add.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r3s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778838710929,"end":1778838710935}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_00283f0217af55b4016a06ecb6745c819bacdc1062c33b926f"}},"id":"prt_e2b0ca9090011buUxvOBPz5PE6","sessionID":"ses_1d4f68af8ffe5pM27eXjh0W1gN","messageID":"msg_e2b0c9a6d0012fnV8PnEUnpM40"}}
