{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778838728787,"sessionID":"ses_1d4f68af8ffe5pM27eXjh0W1gN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_x0cvv0kY8WM2KtAj1j1C23SJ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"jq -r 'select(.id==\"hyp-20260428-029-r12s1\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, (.changes[] | \"- \" + .file + \": \" + .description)' \"log.jsonl\"","timeout":120000,"workdir":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/v1/experiments","description":"Extract v1 load replay hypothesis"},"output":"Add a small normal-RAM load replay buffer in the MEM stage, for example a\n16-entry direct-mapped table indexed by word address. Each entry holds a\nvalid bit, word tag, and the raw 32-bit memory word returned by a previous\nlegal aligned or byte/halfword load. On `io_dmemReady=1`, loads keep using\nthe live `io_dmemRData` exactly as today and refresh the replay entry for the\naligned word address. On `io_dmemReady=0`, a legal normal-RAM load may\ncomplete from the replay buffer on a valid tag hit: suppress the external\ndmem read, use the cached raw word for sign/zero extension and RVFI\n`mem_rdata`, and do not assert `mem_wait`.\n\nReplay is deliberately conservative. It is disabled while the pending-store\nslot is valid, for MMIO/marker/UART addresses, for trapping or misaligned\naccesses, and for stores. Normal-RAM stores invalidate or update the matching\nreplay entry before they retire or enqueue into the pending-store slot, so a\nlater replayed load cannot observe stale data. Replay misses preserve the\ncurrent dmem wait behavior exactly. The top-level IO, single-retire RVFI\nchannel-0 convention, tied-off channel 1, divider interlock, branch\nprediction, and pending-store ordering all remain unchanged. The expected win\nis lower CoreMark cycle count under the 22% random dStall model with much\nless Fmax risk than MEM-to-EX load forwarding or IF replay caches.\n\n- rtl/load_replay.sv: Add a small direct-mapped normal-RAM replay table with valid, tag, and\nraw-word data state. Provide lookup-hit/data outputs for legal load word\naddresses, refresh entries from live dmem load responses, and invalidate\nor byte-merge-update matching entries on legal normal-RAM stores. Reset\nclears only valid bits.\n\n- rtl/mem_stage.sv: Integrate the replay lookup into load handling. Select cached raw word\ndata only when `dmem_ready` is low, the access is a legal non-trapping\nnormal-RAM load, no pending store slot owns the port, and the replay tag\nhits. On a replay hit, gate off `dmem_ren`, clear `mem_wait`, drive\nload-data extraction and RVFI `mem_rdata` from the cached word, and keep\nreplay misses plus all nonbufferable accesses on the existing wait path.\n\n- rtl/core.sv: Wire any replay-buffer module instance or MEM-stage sideband signals\nneeded for store invalidation/update and dmem request gating. Preserve\nthe existing pending-store-slot arbitration, top-level core IO, RVFI\nNRET=2 port layout, strict channel-0 order sequence, and tied-off\nchannel 1 behavior.\n\n- rtl/core_pkg.sv: Add only comments or compact helper typedefs if needed to document\nnormal-RAM replay eligibility and raw-word cache metadata. Do not change\narchitectural state semantics, decoder legality defaults, RVFI field\nwidths, or the NRET=2 contract.\n\n","metadata":{"output":"Add a small normal-RAM load replay buffer in the MEM stage, for example a\n16-entry direct-mapped table indexed by word address. Each entry holds a\nvalid bit, word tag, and the raw 32-bit memory word returned by a previous\nlegal aligned or byte/halfword load. On `io_dmemReady=1`, loads keep using\nthe live `io_dmemRData` exactly as today and refresh the replay entry for the\naligned word address. On `io_dmemReady=0`, a legal normal-RAM load may\ncomplete from the replay buffer on a valid tag hit: suppress the external\ndmem read, use the cached raw word for sign/zero extension and RVFI\n`mem_rdata`, and do not assert `mem_wait`.\n\nReplay is deliberately conservative. It is disabled while the pending-store\nslot is valid, for MMIO/marker/UART addresses, for trapping or misaligned\naccesses, and for stores. Normal-RAM stores invalidate or update the matching\nreplay entry before they retire or enqueue into the pending-store slot, so a\nlater replayed load cannot observe stale data. Replay misses preserve the\ncurrent dmem wait behavior exactly. The top-level IO, single-retire RVFI\nchannel-0 convention, tied-off channel 1, divider interlock, branch\nprediction, and pending-store ordering all remain unchanged. The expected win\nis lower CoreMark cycle count under the 22% random dStall model with much\nless Fmax risk than MEM-to-EX load forwarding or IF replay caches.\n\n- rtl/load_replay.sv: Add a small direct-mapped normal-RAM replay table with valid, tag, and\nraw-word data state. Provide lookup-hit/data outputs for legal load word\naddresses, refresh entries from live dmem load responses, and invalidate\nor byte-merge-update matching entries on legal normal-RAM stores. Reset\nclears only valid bits.\n\n- rtl/mem_stage.sv: Integrate the replay lookup into load handling. Select cached raw word\ndata only when `dmem_ready` is low, the access is a legal non-trapping\nnormal-RAM load, no pending store slot owns the port, and the replay tag\nhits. On a replay hit, gate off `dmem_ren`, clear `mem_wait`, drive\nload-data extraction and RVFI `mem_rdata` from the cached word, and keep\nreplay misses plus all nonbufferable accesses on the existing wait path.\n\n- rtl/core.sv: Wire any replay-buffer module instance or MEM-stage sideband signals\nneeded for store invalidation/update and dmem request gating. Preserve\nthe existing pending-store-slot arbitration, top-level core IO, RVFI\nNRET=2 port layout, strict channel-0 order sequence, and tied-off\nchannel 1 behavior.\n\n- rtl/core_pkg.sv: Add only comments or compact helper typedefs if needed to document\nnormal-RAM replay eligibility and raw-word cache metadata. Do not change\narchitectural state semantics, decoder legality defaults, RVFI field\nwidths, or the NRET=2 contract.\n\n","exit":0,"description":"Extract v1 load replay hypothesis","truncated":false},"title":"Extract v1 load replay hypothesis","time":{"start":1778838728783,"end":1778838728786}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_084b153cbd4de20b016a06ecc779ac8198af8eed3f8e75c894"}},"id":"prt_e2b0ceb98001vB80BhEk5PoJnj","sessionID":"ses_1d4f68af8ffe5pM27eXjh0W1gN","messageID":"msg_e2b0cdcb8001wuzHNI3On0ZSip"}}
