{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778838792844,"sessionID":"ses_1d4f68af8ffe5pM27eXjh0W1gN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_yTB2lCcRKWfdfg6pmdwNcAiY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\n+title: \"Tiny MEM-stage load replay buffer\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The two successful structural changes on `bench` both stayed off the fetch\n+  and hot EX paths: iterative DIV/REM and the one-deep store retirement slot.\n+  The remaining backend stall source is load-side dmem backpressure. Today a\n+  normal-RAM load freezes IF, ID, EX, and MEM whenever `io_dmemReady=0`, even\n+  if the same aligned word was returned recently and CoreMark's 6 KB working\n+  set is revisiting it.\n+\n+  That makes load-side stall hiding the cleanest remaining structural lever:\n+  it attacks iterations/cycle without pulling new decode or prediction logic\n+  onto the frontend path that already regressed on prior bench attempts.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a tiny normal-RAM load replay structure in MEM, such as a small\n+  direct-mapped raw-word buffer keyed by aligned word address. Live ready\n+  loads keep using `io_dmemRData` exactly as they do today and refresh the\n+  replay entry for that word. When `io_dmemReady=0`, a legal aligned\n+  normal-RAM load may complete from the replay buffer on a tag hit: use the\n+  cached raw word for sign/zero extension and RVFI `mem_rdata`, suppress the\n+  global dmem wait for that instruction, and let the pipeline keep retiring in\n+  order.\n+\n+  Replay must stay conservative. Disable it for MMIO/marker/UART accesses,\n+  misaligned or trapping loads, misses, and any cycle where the pending store\n+  slot is valid. Normal-RAM stores should invalidate or update matching replay\n+  entries before they retire or enter the store slot so replayed loads cannot\n+  observe stale data. This keeps the ready-load fast path unchanged while\n+  targeting the next obvious IPC loss without adding MEM-to-EX load bypassing\n+  or more fetch-side control logic.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/load_replay.sv\n+    description: \"Add a tiny direct-mapped normal-RAM load replay table that stores valid bits, aligned-word tags, and raw 32-bit data, with refresh from successful loads and invalidation or update on normal-RAM stores.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consult the replay table only for legal aligned normal-RAM loads when `io_dmemReady` is low, use cached raw-word data for load extraction and RVFI memory fields on a hit, and preserve the current live-load and store-slot behavior on misses and non-replayable accesses.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Refine the dmem-stall condition so a load that completes from MEM replay does not freeze IF/ID/EX, while replay misses and all other memory operations keep the existing backpressure behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the MEM replay-hit or mem-wait sideband into hazard control without changing the current top-level imem/dmem or single-channel RVFI interface.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add cocotb coverage for replayed stalled loads, replay invalidation by older stores, and the rule that MMIO or misaligned loads still stall and trap exactly as before.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\n+title: \"Tiny MEM-stage load replay buffer\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The two successful structural changes on `bench` both stayed off the fetch\n+  and hot EX paths: iterative DIV/REM and the one-deep store retirement slot.\n+  The remaining backend stall source is load-side dmem backpressure. Today a\n+  normal-RAM load freezes IF, ID, EX, and MEM whenever `io_dmemReady=0`, even\n+  if the same aligned word was returned recently and CoreMark's 6 KB working\n+  set is revisiting it.\n+\n+  That makes load-side stall hiding the cleanest remaining structural lever:\n+  it attacks iterations/cycle without pulling new decode or prediction logic\n+  onto the frontend path that already regressed on prior bench attempts.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a tiny normal-RAM load replay structure in MEM, such as a small\n+  direct-mapped raw-word buffer keyed by aligned word address. Live ready\n+  loads keep using `io_dmemRData` exactly as they do today and refresh the\n+  replay entry for that word. When `io_dmemReady=0`, a legal aligned\n+  normal-RAM load may complete from the replay buffer on a tag hit: use the\n+  cached raw word for sign/zero extension and RVFI `mem_rdata`, suppress the\n+  global dmem wait for that instruction, and let the pipeline keep retiring in\n+  order.\n+\n+  Replay must stay conservative. Disable it for MMIO/marker/UART accesses,\n+  misaligned or trapping loads, misses, and any cycle where the pending store\n+  slot is valid. Normal-RAM stores should invalidate or update matching replay\n+  entries before they retire or enter the store slot so replayed loads cannot\n+  observe stale data. This keeps the ready-load fast path unchanged while\n+  targeting the next obvious IPC loss without adding MEM-to-EX load bypassing\n+  or more fetch-side control logic.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/load_replay.sv\n+    description: \"Add a tiny direct-mapped normal-RAM load replay table that stores valid bits, aligned-word tags, and raw 32-bit data, with refresh from successful loads and invalidation or update on normal-RAM stores.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consult the replay table only for legal aligned normal-RAM loads when `io_dmemReady` is low, use cached raw-word data for load extraction and RVFI memory fields on a hit, and preserve the current live-load and store-slot behavior on misses and non-replayable accesses.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Refine the dmem-stall condition so a load that completes from MEM replay does not freeze IF/ID/EX, while replay misses and all other memory operations keep the existing backpressure behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the MEM replay-hit or mem-wait sideband into hazard control without changing the current top-level imem/dmem or single-channel RVFI interface.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add cocotb coverage for replayed stalled loads, replay invalidation by older stores, and the rule that MMIO or misaligned loads still stall and trap exactly as before.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\n+title: \"Tiny MEM-stage load replay buffer\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The two successful structural changes on `bench` both stayed off the fetch\n+  and hot EX paths: iterative DIV/REM and the one-deep store retirement slot.\n+  The remaining backend stall source is load-side dmem backpressure. Today a\n+  normal-RAM load freezes IF, ID, EX, and MEM whenever `io_dmemReady=0`, even\n+  if the same aligned word was returned recently and CoreMark's 6 KB working\n+  set is revisiting it.\n+\n+  That makes load-side stall hiding the cleanest remaining structural lever:\n+  it attacks iterations/cycle without pulling new decode or prediction logic\n+  onto the frontend path that already regressed on prior bench attempts.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a tiny normal-RAM load replay structure in MEM, such as a small\n+  direct-mapped raw-word buffer keyed by aligned word address. Live ready\n+  loads keep using `io_dmemRData` exactly as they do today and refresh the\n+  replay entry for that word. When `io_dmemReady=0`, a legal aligned\n+  normal-RAM load may complete from the replay buffer on a tag hit: use the\n+  cached raw word for sign/zero extension and RVFI `mem_rdata`, suppress the\n+  global dmem wait for that instruction, and let the pipeline keep retiring in\n+  order.\n+\n+  Replay must stay conservative. Disable it for MMIO/marker/UART accesses,\n+  misaligned or trapping loads, misses, and any cycle where the pending store\n+  slot is valid. Normal-RAM stores should invalidate or update matching replay\n+  entries before they retire or enter the store slot so replayed loads cannot\n+  observe stale data. This keeps the ready-load fast path unchanged while\n+  targeting the next obvious IPC loss without adding MEM-to-EX load bypassing\n+  or more fetch-side control logic.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/load_replay.sv\n+    description: \"Add a tiny direct-mapped normal-RAM load replay table that stores valid bits, aligned-word tags, and raw 32-bit data, with refresh from successful loads and invalidation or update on normal-RAM stores.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consult the replay table only for legal aligned normal-RAM loads when `io_dmemReady` is low, use cached raw-word data for load extraction and RVFI memory fields on a hit, and preserve the current live-load and store-slot behavior on misses and non-replayable accesses.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Refine the dmem-stall condition so a load that completes from MEM replay does not freeze IF/ID/EX, while replay misses and all other memory operations keep the existing backpressure behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the MEM replay-hit or mem-wait sideband into hazard control without changing the current top-level imem/dmem or single-channel RVFI interface.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add cocotb coverage for replayed stalled loads, replay invalidation by older stores, and the rule that MMIO or misaligned loads still stall and trap exactly as before.\"\n","additions":45,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778838792841,"end":1778838792843}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_09bc9a28d1198a0b016a06ecf910e4819a85b0740f9dd9ae29"}},"id":"prt_e2b0dae95001bZ6pksWNn7eHqr","sessionID":"ses_1d4f68af8ffe5pM27eXjh0W1gN","messageID":"msg_e2b0d08210010opLD63QdslSvg"}}
