{"type":"text","timestamp":1778855829485,"sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","part":{"id":"prt_e2c11c8c70012WRacOIn4cuMid","messageID":"msg_e2c11ac9c00125lsPiK4P6GI1F","sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","type":"text","text":"The structural history points away from frontend prediction and deeper MEM-side structures. I’m checking the exact prior structural proposals to avoid repeating the same failure mode.","time":{"start":1778855823559,"end":1778855829471},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_04d1e0472f756cde016a072f8f30a48198b94226c116a4f0b2","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778855829545,"sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_wiZq490jFEQ2KX8gx8ZY42Mk","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\"|\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r4s1\"|\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\"|\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\"","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments","include":"log.jsonl"},"output":"Found 4 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 3: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Port v1-proven iterative divider into EX\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current bench baseline still carries real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators\\ninside the always-live combinational ALU. Archived bench runs on this same\\nbaseline show that moving divider-class ops off the fast EX path was the\\nbiggest structural win, because CoreMark almost never uses integer division\\nwhile the FPGA still pays its timing and LUT cost on every cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current bench baseline still carries real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators\\ninside the always-live combinational ALU. Archived bench runs on this same\\nbaseline show that moving divider-class ops off the fast EX path was the\\nbiggest structural win, because CoreMark almost never uses integer division\\nwhile the FPGA still pays its timing and LUT cost on every cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Reuse the already-proven iterative divider structure from cores/v1 and\\nintegrate it only for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, leaving the existing single-cycle\\nRV32I and MUL-family datapaths intact. alu.sv stops synthesizing real\\ndivider hardware; ex_stage.sv launches the divider for divide-class ops,\\nholds the in-flight EX payload until completion, and commits exactly one\\nEX/MEM result with the original RVFI metadata and RV32M corner-case behavior\\npreserved. This is the lowest-risk structural path to a large Fmax gain on\\nthe current baseline because it attacks the known worst cone without adding\\nfetch-side control, store reordering, or multiply bubbles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 20, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/div_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the v1-proven iterative RV32 divider/remainder unit with ALTOPS compatibility and exact divide-by-zero / INT_MIN-overflow semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU hardware from the normal ALU fast path while keeping existing RV32I and MUL-f...\n  Line 6: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"One-Deep Store Retirement Slot\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current bench core's biggest proven gain came from a backend-only timing\\nchange: moving DIV/REM off the one-cycle EX path. The recent failed branch\\nprediction attempt showed the opposite boundary on this RTL: pulling more\\ndecode/target work into the frontend can erase the IPC gain with Fmax loss.\\n\\nThe next structural hypothesis should therefore stay off the fetch path and\\nattack the other obvious whole-core bubble source. Today any `io_dmemReady=0`\\ncycle on a STORE freezes IF, ID, EX, and MEM even though the store address,\\nreplicated data, and byte mask are already known in MEM, and CoreMark does a\\nsteady stream of normal-RAM stores to stack, list, matrix, and state data.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current bench core's biggest proven gain came from a backend-only timing\\nchange: moving DIV/REM off the one-cycle EX path. The recent failed branch\\nprediction attempt showed the opposite boundary on this RTL: pulling more\\ndecode/target work into the frontend can erase the IPC gain with Fmax loss.\\n\\nThe next structural hypothesis should therefore stay off the fetch path and\\nattack the other obvious whole-core bubble source. Today any `io_dmemReady=0`\\ncycle on a STORE freezes IF, ID, EX, and MEM even though the store address,\\nreplicated data, and byte mask are already known in MEM, and CoreMark does a\\nsteady stream of normal-RAM stores to stack, list, matrix, and state data.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-deep pending-store retirement slot with a direct ready-store fast\\npath. When an aligned STORE to normal RAM `[0x00000000, 0x00100000)` reaches\\nMEM and `io_dmemReady` is low, capture its byte address, replicated write\\ndata, byte mask, and RVFI-visible memory metadata into the slot, retire that\\nstore once, and drain the physical dmem write oldest-first after the stall.\\n\\nKeep the zero-wait STORE path identical to the current d...\n  Line 9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Tiny MEM-stage load replay buffer\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The two successful structural changes on `bench` both stayed off the fetch\\nand hot EX paths: iterative DIV/REM and the one-deep store retirement slot.\\nThe remaining backend stall source is load-side dmem backpressure. Today a\\nnormal-RAM load freezes IF, ID, EX, and MEM whenever `io_dmemReady=0`, even\\nif the same aligned word was returned recently and CoreMark's 6 KB working\\nset is revisiting it.\\n\\nThat makes load-side stall hiding the cleanest remaining structural lever:\\nit attacks iterations/cycle without pulling new decode or prediction logic\\nonto the frontend path that already regressed on prior bench attempts.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The two successful structural changes on `bench` both stayed off the fetch\\nand hot EX paths: iterative DIV/REM and the one-deep store retirement slot.\\nThe remaining backend stall source is load-side dmem backpressure. Today a\\nnormal-RAM load freezes IF, ID, EX, and MEM whenever `io_dmemReady=0`, even\\nif the same aligned word was returned recently and CoreMark's 6 KB working\\nset is revisiting it.\\n\\nThat makes load-side stall hiding the cleanest remaining structural lever:\\nit attacks iterations/cycle without pulling new decode or prediction logic\\nonto the frontend path that already regressed on prior bench attempts.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny normal-RAM load replay structure in MEM, such as a small\\ndirect-mapped raw-word buffer keyed by aligned word address. Live ready\\nloads keep using `io_dmemRData` exactly as they do today and refresh the\\nreplay entry for that word. When `io_dmemReady=0`, a legal aligned\\nnormal-RAM load may complete from the replay buffer on a tag hit: use the\\ncached raw word for sign/zero extension and RVFI `mem_rdata`, suppress the\\nglobal dmem wait for that instruction, and let the pipeline keep retiring in\\norder.\\n\\nReplay must stay conservative. Disable it for...\n  Line 12: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Two-Entry Deferred Store Queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The best `bench` gains so far have come from backend-only structural changes\\nthat avoid adding logic to the fetch path: first moving DIV/REM off EX, then\\nbuffering one stalled RAM store. The current one-deep store slot still\\nserializes store bursts behind a single pending write, even though CoreMark\\nissues clustered stack, list, matrix, and state stores under the random\\n`io_dmemReady` stall model.\\n\\nA deeper store queue is the next clean extension of the one change that has\\nalready proven it can raise IPC on this RTL without paying the frontend Fmax\\npenalties seen in prior predictor experiments.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The best `bench` gains so far have come from backend-only structural changes\\nthat avoid adding logic to the fetch path: first moving DIV/REM off EX, then\\nbuffering one stalled RAM store. The current one-deep store slot still\\nserializes store bursts behind a single pending write, even though CoreMark\\nissues clustered stack, list, matrix, and state stores under the random\\n`io_dmemReady` stall model.\\n\\nA deeper store queue is the next clean extension of the one change that has\\nalready proven it can raise IPC on this RTL without paying the frontend Fmax\\npenalties seen in prior predictor experiments.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the current one-deep pending-store slot with a two-entry oldest-first\\ndeferred store queue for aligned normal-RAM stores. When `io_dmemReady` is\\nlow, the oldest queued store keeps draining to the physical bus while a\\nyounger bufferable store can still retire into the second queue entry instead\\nof freezing the whole pipeline immediately.\\n\\nKeep the existing zero-wait direct-store fast path when the queue is empty,\\nand preserve architectural ordering by continuing to fence younger loads,\\nnon-bufferable stores, and EBREAK behind any queued store. This should hide\\nmore of CoreMark's store-s...","metadata":{"matches":4,"truncated":false},"title":"\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\"|\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r4s1\"|\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\"|\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\"","time":{"start":1778855829504,"end":1778855829543}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04d1e0472f756cde016a072f952c9481989444bf57d43ecec6"}},"id":"prt_e2c11dfee001im4YMe5NRQ7cfg","sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","messageID":"msg_e2c11ac9c00125lsPiK4P6GI1F"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778855829764,"sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_UukAMAM1Q36wngZ0v0JIT2kt","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv","offset":1,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: // rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n2: //\n3: // Detects the pipeline conditions that must freeze younger issue:\n4: //   - load-use (textbook 5-stage hazard not covered by forwarding)\n5: //   - divider busy in EX\n6: //   - imem / dmem backpressure\n7: //   - pending-store slot fencing for younger memory ops and EBREAK\n8: //\n9: // Outputs:\n10: //   stall_if / stall_id : freeze the PC reg and the IF/ID combinational\n11: //                          payload (cleared by ID's flush input).\n12: //   flush_if / flush_id : on EX redirect, kill the two in-flight\n13: //                          instructions ahead of the redirect target.\n14: //   flush_id            : also kills ID's own register on load-use to\n15: //                          inject a single-cycle bubble between LOAD\n16: //                          and the dependent instruction.\n17: //\n18: // Latency:        combinational.\n19: // RVFI fields:    n/a (governs validity of subsequent retirements).\n20: module hazard_unit (\n21:   input  logic       id_ex_mem_read,    // ID/EX.ctrl.mem_read (LOAD in EX)\n22:   input  logic [4:0] id_ex_rd,          // ID/EX.rd            (LOAD's dest)\n23:   input  logic [4:0] if_id_rs1,         // IF/ID instr[19:15]  (next rs1)\n24:   input  logic [4:0] if_id_rs2,         // IF/ID instr[24:20]  (next rs2)\n25:   input  logic       redirect,          // EX has resolved a branch/jump\n26:   // Bus backpressure (default-1 in zero-wait testbenches; VexRiscv-style\n27:   // random ~22% stall in vex_main.cpp). When low, the corresponding\n28:   // memory request is NOT serviced this cycle.\n29:   input  logic       imem_ready,\n30:   input  logic       dmem_ready,\n31:   // EX/MEM has a memory op in flight (the LOAD/STORE the dmem stall\n32:   // would actually be holding up). Computed at top level from the\n33:   // EX/MEM register's ctrl.mem_read | ctrl.mem_write.\n34:   input  logic       ex_mem_mem_op,\n35:   input  logic       ex_mem_store_bufferable,\n36:   input  logic       ex_mem_end_fence,\n37:   input  logic       store_slot_valid,\n38:   input  logic       div_stall,\n39:   output logic       stall_if,          // PC reg holds\n40:   output logic       stall_id,          // ID/EX register holds (vs. bubble)\n41:   output logic       flush_if,          // IF/ID comb output -> NOP\n42:   output logic       flush_id,          // ID/EX register captures '0\n43:   output logic       stall_ex_mem,      // EX/MEM register holds\n44:   output logic       hold_mem_wb        // MEM/WB clears valid only;\n45:                                         // data fields stay (for fwd)\n46: );\n47: \n48:   logic load_use_hazard;\n49:   logic imem_stall;\n50:   logic dmem_stall;\n51:   logic slot_fence_stall;\n52: \n53:   always_comb begin\n54:     load_use_hazard = id_ex_mem_read\n55:                    && (id_ex_rd == if_id_rs1 || id_ex_rd == if_id_rs2)\n56:                    && (id_ex_rd != 5'b0);\n57:     imem_stall = !imem_ready;\n58:     // dmem stall only matters if there's actually a memory op in EX/MEM\n59:     // — otherwise bus-not-ready is irrelevant to the pipeline.\n60:     dmem_stall = !dmem_ready && ex_mem_mem_op\n61:               && !(ex_mem_store_bufferable && !store_slot_valid);\n62:     // Once a deferred RAM store occupies the slot, it drains oldest-first.\n63:     // Younger memory ops and the architectural halt marker must wait until\n64:     // that externally-visible write has actually reached the bus.\n65:     slot_fence_stall = store_slot_valid && (ex_mem_mem_op || ex_mem_end_fence);\n66: \n67:     // PC reg holds on any stall reason.\n68:     stall_if      = load_use_hazard || imem_stall || dmem_stall\n69:                  || slot_fence_stall || div_stall;\n70:     // IF/ID combinational payload: NOP whenever we wouldn't have a valid\n71:     // instruction this cycle (redirect target unknown to IF, or imem\n72:     // didn't deliver).\n73:     flush_if      = redirect || imem_stall;\n74:     // ID/EX register:\n75:     //   - dmem_stall  -> hold        (preserve in-flight pipeline state)\n76:     //   - load_use    -> bubble      (1-cycle stall between LOAD + use)\n77:     //   - redirect    -> bubble      (kill wrong-path)\n78:     //   - otherwise   -> capture\n79:     // dmem_stall takes precedence over load_use's bubble: re-evaluate\n80:     // load_use next cycle when the bus unblocks. flush_id is 1 only when\n81:     // we want bubble (not hold).\n82:     stall_id      = dmem_stall || slot_fence_stall || load_use_hazard || div_stall;\n83:     flush_id      = (load_use_hazard || redirect) && !(dmem_stall || slot_fence_stall);\n84:     // EX/MEM register: holds on dmem_stall (LOAD waits in MEM until the\n85:     // bus delivers).\n86:     stall_ex_mem  = dmem_stall || slot_fence_stall;\n87:     // MEM/WB register: on dmem_stall the previously-retired instruction's\n88:     // data fields stay alive for forwarding (e.g. a held BNE needs the\n89:     // LOAD's load_data via fwd_mem_wb), but valid is cleared so we don't\n90:     // double-retire / double-write the regfile.\n91:     hold_mem_wb   = dmem_stall || slot_fence_stall;\n92:   end\n93: \n94: endmodule\n\n(End of file - total 94 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"// rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n//\n// Detects the pipeline conditions that must freeze younger issue:\n//   - load-use (textbook 5-stage hazard not covered by forwarding)\n//   - divider busy in EX\n//   - imem / dmem backpressure\n//   - pending-store slot fencing for younger memory ops and EBREAK\n//\n// Outputs:\n//   stall_if / stall_id : freeze the PC reg and the IF/ID combinational\n//                          payload (cleared by ID's flush input).\n//   flush_if / flush_id : on EX redirect, kill the two in-flight\n//                          instructions ahead of the redirect target.\n//   flush_id            : also kills ID's own register on load-use to\n//                          inject a single-cycle bubble between LOAD\n//                          and the dependent instruction.\n//\n// Latency:        combinational.\n// RVFI fields:    n/a (governs validity of subsequent retirements).\nmodule hazard_unit (","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv","time":{"start":1778855829731,"end":1778855829762}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04d1e0472f756cde016a072f952ce48198a6542feacef56950"}},"id":"prt_e2c11e00a001ojY2H4u7cT3aWG","sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","messageID":"msg_e2c11ac9c00125lsPiK4P6GI1F"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778855829766,"sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_jJlOSSM9OAd5ATRgGOC63Cyi","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv","offset":1,"limit":260},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: // rtl/mem_stage.sv\n2: //\n3: // Memory access stage. Drives the dmem read/write ports combinationally\n4: // from the EX/MEM register, and sign/zero-extends the loaded data into\n5: // the MEM/WB register.\n6: //\n7: // Byte-lane discipline:\n8: //   - Write data is replicated across all four byte lanes; the\n9: //     byte-mask (mem_wmask) selects the actual destination bytes.\n10: //   - Load: shift the raw word right by `addr[1:0]*8`, then sign- or\n11: //     zero-extend the low 8/16 bits per the LB/LBU/LH/LHU encoding.\n12: //   - For RVFI ALIGNED_MEM, mem_addr is reported word-aligned and the\n13: //     byte position is captured in mem_rmask / mem_wmask.\n14: //\n15: // Latency:        1 cycle (MEM/WB register clocked here).\n16: // RVFI fields:    feeds mem_addr, mem_rmask, mem_wmask, mem_rdata,\n17: //                 mem_wdata, plus rd_wdata via the loaded-data path.\n18: module mem_stage (\n19:   input  logic               clock,\n20:   input  logic               reset,\n21:   input  logic               dmem_ready,\n22:   // hold_wb: dmem stall is in effect. MEM/WB's data fields are RETAINED\n23:   // (so the previously-retired LOAD's `rd` / `read_data` / `ctrl.reg_write`\n24:   // remain visible to forward_unit), but `valid` is cleared so:\n25:   //   - rvfi_order doesn't increment for held cycles\n26:   //   - wb_stage doesn't write the regfile twice\n27:   // Zeroing the whole register would lose the LOAD's load_data, breaking\n28:   // MEM/WB->EX forwarding for any dependent instruction that's also held\n29:   // in ID/EX during the stall (e.g. a BNE that consumes a LOAD's result).\n30:   input  logic               hold_wb,\n31:   // ex_mem_t carries branch_taken / branch_target / pc_next / rs?_val\n32:   // for downstream RVFI use; mem_stage only consumes a subset, so the\n33:   // remaining fields look unused from this module's perspective.\n34:   /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n35:   input  ex_mem_t  in,\n36:   /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n37:   // dmem interface\n38:   output logic [31:0]        dmem_addr,\n39:   output logic [31:0]        dmem_wdata,\n40:   input  logic [31:0]        dmem_rdata,\n41:   output logic [3:0]         dmem_wen,\n42:   output logic               dmem_ren,\n43:   output logic               store_bufferable,\n44:   output logic               store_slot_valid,\n45:   // MEM/WB register output\n46:   output mem_wb_t  out\n47: );\n48: \n49:   logic [31:0] wdata_rep;\n50:   logic [3:0]  byte_mask;\n51:   logic [31:0] aligned_addr;\n52:   // shifted[31:16] is dropped on byte/halfword loads; only [15:0] feeds\n53:   // the sign/zero-extension mux.\n54:   /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n55:   logic [31:0] shifted;\n56:   /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n57:   logic [7:0]  byte_val;\n58:   logic [15:0] hword_val;\n59:   logic [31:0] load_data;\n60:   logic        ram_store;\n61:   logic        capture_store;\n62: \n63:   // Misaligned mem-access trap. RV32I requires word-aligned LW/SW and\n64:   // halfword-aligned LH/LHU/SH; byte ops are always aligned.\n65:   // riscv-formal's RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM contract demands rvfi_trap=1\n66:   // when the effective byte address is not aligned to the access width.\n67:   // On trap, the dmem ports are gated off and ctrl propagates is_illegal.\n68:   logic mem_misalign;\n69:   logic mem_op;\n70:   ctrl_t ctrl_with_trap;\n71: \n72:   logic        store_slot_valid_q;\n73:   logic [31:0] store_slot_addr_q;\n74:   logic [31:0] store_slot_wdata_q;\n75:   logic [3:0]  store_slot_wmask_q;\n76: \n77:   always_comb begin\n78:     // Byte/halfword replication for stores.\n79:     case (in.ctrl.mem_width)\n80:       2'd0:    wdata_rep = {4{in.write_data[7:0]}};\n81:       2'd1:    wdata_rep = {2{in.write_data[15:0]}};\n82:       default: wdata_rep = in.write_data;\n83:     endcase\n84: \n85:     // Byte-lane mask shifted to addr[1:0] * 1.\n86:     case (in.ctrl.mem_width)\n87:       2'd0:    byte_mask = (4'b0001 << in.alu_result[1:0]);\n88:       2'd1:    byte_mask = (4'b0011 << in.alu_result[1:0]);\n89:       default: byte_mask = 4'b1111;\n90:     endcase\n91: \n92:     mem_op       = in.ctrl.mem_read || in.ctrl.mem_write;\n93:     mem_misalign = mem_op && (\n94:                      (in.ctrl.mem_width == 2'd2 && in.alu_result[1:0] != 2'b00) ||\n95:                      (in.ctrl.mem_width == 2'd1 && in.alu_result[0]   != 1'b0)\n96:                      // 2'd0 (byte) is never misaligned.\n97:                    );\n98: \n99:     ctrl_with_trap = in.ctrl;\n100:     if (mem_misalign) begin\n101:       ctrl_with_trap.is_illegal = 1'b1;\n102:       ctrl_with_trap.reg_write  = 1'b0;\n103:     end\n104: \n105:     // Load extraction: shift right then sign/zero-extend the low N bits.\n106:     shifted   = dmem_rdata >> (in.alu_result[1:0] * 8);\n107:     byte_val  = shifted[7:0];\n108:     hword_val = shifted[15:0];\n109:     case (in.ctrl.mem_width)\n110:       2'd0:    load_data = in.ctrl.mem_sext\n111:                          ? {{24{byte_val[7]}},  byte_val}\n112:                          : {24'b0,              byte_val};\n113:       2'd1:    load_data = in.ctrl.mem_sext\n114:                          ? {{16{hword_val[15]}}, hword_val}\n115:                          : {16'b0,               hword_val};\n116:       default: load_data = dmem_rdata;\n117:     endcase\n118: \n119:     // RVFI ALIGNED_MEM expects word-aligned mem_addr; mem_addr=0 if no access.\n120:     aligned_addr = (mem_op && !mem_misalign)\n121:                  ? {in.alu_result[31:2], 2'b00}\n122:                  : 32'b0;\n123: \n124:     ram_store        = in.valid && in.ctrl.mem_write && !mem_misalign\n125:                     && (in.alu_result < 32'h0010_0000);\n126:     store_bufferable = ram_store;\n127:     capture_store    = ram_store && !dmem_ready && !store_slot_valid_q;\n128: \n129:     if (store_slot_valid_q) begin\n130:       dmem_addr  = store_slot_addr_q;\n131:       dmem_wdata = store_slot_wdata_q;\n132:       dmem_wen   = store_slot_wmask_q;\n133:       dmem_ren   = 1'b0;\n134:     end else begin\n135:       dmem_addr  = in.alu_result;\n136:       dmem_wdata = wdata_rep;\n137:       dmem_wen   = (in.ctrl.mem_write && !mem_misalign) ? byte_mask : 4'b0000;\n138:       dmem_ren   = in.ctrl.mem_read  && !mem_misalign;\n139:     end\n140:   end\n141: \n142:   // ── MEM/WB register ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n143:   mem_wb_t reg_q;\n144: \n145:   always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n146:     if (reset) begin\n147:       reg_q <= '0;\n148:       store_slot_valid_q <= 1'b0;\n149:       store_slot_addr_q  <= 32'b0;\n150:       store_slot_wdata_q <= 32'b0;\n151:       store_slot_wmask_q <= 4'b0;\n152:     end else begin\n153:       if (hold_wb) begin\n154:         // Clear valid (no double-retire / no double-regfile-write), but\n155:         // KEEP every other field. Forwarding from MEM/WB to a stalled\n156:         // dependent in ID/EX needs the held LOAD's rd/read_data/ctrl\n157:         // alive for as many cycles as the memory-side stall lasts.\n158:         reg_q.valid <= 1'b0;\n159:       end else begin\n160:         reg_q.pc         <= in.pc;\n161:         reg_q.alu_result <= in.alu_result;\n162:         reg_q.read_data  <= load_data;\n163:         reg_q.rd         <= in.rd;\n164:         reg_q.rs1_addr   <= in.rs1_addr;\n165:         reg_q.rs2_addr   <= in.rs2_addr;\n166:         reg_q.rs1_val    <= in.rs1_val;\n167:         reg_q.rs2_val    <= in.rs2_val;\n168:         reg_q.pc_next    <= in.pc_next;\n169:         reg_q.mem_addr   <= aligned_addr;\n170:         reg_q.mem_rdata  <= dmem_rdata;\n171:         reg_q.mem_wdata  <= wdata_rep;\n172:         reg_q.mem_wmask  <= (in.ctrl.mem_write && !mem_misalign) ? byte_mask : 4'b0000;\n173:         reg_q.mem_rmask  <= (in.ctrl.mem_read  && !mem_misalign) ? byte_mask : 4'b0000;\n174:         reg_q.ctrl       <= ctrl_with_trap;\n175:         reg_q.instr      <= in.instr;\n176:         reg_q.valid      <= in.valid;\n177:       end\n178: \n179:       if (capture_store) begin\n180:         store_slot_valid_q <= 1'b1;\n181:         store_slot_addr_q  <= in.alu_result;\n182:         store_slot_wdata_q <= wdata_rep;\n183:         store_slot_wmask_q <= byte_mask;\n184:       end else if (store_slot_valid_q && dmem_ready) begin\n185:         store_slot_valid_q <= 1'b0;\n186:       end\n187:     end\n188:   end\n189: \n190:   assign store_slot_valid = store_slot_valid_q;\n191:   assign out = reg_q;\n192: \n193: endmodule\n\n(End of file - total 193 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"// rtl/mem_stage.sv\n//\n// Memory access stage. Drives the dmem read/write ports combinationally\n// from the EX/MEM register, and sign/zero-extends the loaded data into\n// the MEM/WB register.\n//\n// Byte-lane discipline:\n//   - Write data is replicated across all four byte lanes; the\n//     byte-mask (mem_wmask) selects the actual destination bytes.\n//   - Load: shift the raw word right by `addr[1:0]*8`, then sign- or\n//     zero-extend the low 8/16 bits per the LB/LBU/LH/LHU encoding.\n//   - For RVFI ALIGNED_MEM, mem_addr is reported word-aligned and the\n//     byte position is captured in mem_rmask / mem_wmask.\n//\n// Latency:        1 cycle (MEM/WB register clocked here).\n// RVFI fields:    feeds mem_addr, mem_rmask, mem_wmask, mem_rdata,\n//                 mem_wdata, plus rd_wdata via the loaded-data path.\nmodule mem_stage (\n  input  logic               clock,\n  input  logic               reset,","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv","time":{"start":1778855829737,"end":1778855829765}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04d1e0472f756cde016a072f952cf081988954840559d8c3d3"}},"id":"prt_e2c11e0e6001JYfdgqG4phtMS7","sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","messageID":"msg_e2c11ac9c00125lsPiK4P6GI1F"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778855829778,"sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_fF6FJzsoXt06Twabyf791NUG","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv","offset":1,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: // rtl/id_stage.sv\n2: //\n3: // Decode stage. Combinationally drives the regfile read ports and the\n4: // ID/EX register's next-state from the IF/ID combinational bundle plus\n5: // the regfile read data. The ID/EX register is owned by this module so\n6: // the decoded view of instruction n is latched by end of cycle n+1.\n7: //\n8: // Latency:        1 cycle (ID/EX register clocked here).\n9: // RVFI fields:    feeds rs1_addr, rs1_rdata, rs2_addr, rs2_rdata, insn,\n10: //                 trap (via ctrl.is_illegal).\n11: module id_stage (\n12:   input  logic              clock,\n13:   input  logic              reset,\n14:   input  logic              stall,\n15:   input  logic              flush,\n16:   input  if_id_t  in,\n17:   // regfile read interface\n18:   output logic [4:0]        rs1_addr,\n19:   output logic [4:0]        rs2_addr,\n20:   input  logic [31:0]       rs1_data,\n21:   input  logic [31:0]       rs2_data,\n22:   // ID/EX register output\n23:   output id_ex_t  out\n24: );\n25: \n26:   // ── Combinational decode ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n27:   logic [4:0]  dec_alu_op;\n28:   logic        dec_alu_src;\n29:   logic [2:0]  dec_branch_op;\n30:   logic        dec_is_branch;\n31:   logic        dec_is_jump;\n32:   logic        dec_is_jalr;\n33:   logic        dec_is_lui;\n34:   logic        dec_is_auipc;\n35:   logic        dec_mem_read;\n36:   logic        dec_mem_write;\n37:   logic [1:0]  dec_mem_width;\n38:   logic        dec_mem_sext;\n39:   logic        dec_reg_write;\n40:   logic        dec_mem_to_reg;\n41:   logic        dec_is_illegal;\n42: \n43:   decoder u_decoder (\n44:     .instr      (in.instr),\n45:     .alu_op     (dec_alu_op),\n46:     .alu_src    (dec_alu_src),\n47:     .branch_op  (dec_branch_op),\n48:     .is_branch  (dec_is_branch),\n49:     .is_jump    (dec_is_jump),\n50:     .is_jalr    (dec_is_jalr),\n51:     .is_lui     (dec_is_lui),\n52:     .is_auipc   (dec_is_auipc),\n53:     .mem_read   (dec_mem_read),\n54:     .mem_write  (dec_mem_write),\n55:     .mem_width  (dec_mem_width),\n56:     .mem_sext   (dec_mem_sext),\n57:     .reg_write  (dec_reg_write),\n58:     .mem_to_reg (dec_mem_to_reg),\n59:     .is_illegal (dec_is_illegal)\n60:   );\n61: \n62:   logic [31:0] imm;\n63:   imm_gen u_imm (.instr(in.instr), .imm(imm));\n64: \n65:   // Regfile read addresses come straight from the IF/ID instruction — these\n66:   // are also wired to the hazard unit at top level for load-use detection.\n67:   assign rs1_addr = in.instr[19:15];\n68:   assign rs2_addr = in.instr[24:20];\n69: \n70:   ctrl_t ctrl_decoded;\n71:   always_comb begin\n72:     ctrl_decoded.alu_op     = dec_alu_op;\n73:     ctrl_decoded.alu_src    = dec_alu_src;\n74:     ctrl_decoded.branch_op  = dec_branch_op;\n75:     ctrl_decoded.is_branch  = dec_is_branch;\n76:     ctrl_decoded.is_jump    = dec_is_jump;\n77:     ctrl_decoded.is_jalr    = dec_is_jalr;\n78:     ctrl_decoded.is_lui     = dec_is_lui;\n79:     ctrl_decoded.is_auipc   = dec_is_auipc;\n80:     ctrl_decoded.mem_read   = dec_mem_read;\n81:     ctrl_decoded.mem_write  = dec_mem_write;\n82:     ctrl_decoded.mem_width  = dec_mem_width;\n83:     ctrl_decoded.mem_sext   = dec_mem_sext;\n84:     ctrl_decoded.reg_write  = dec_reg_write;\n85:     ctrl_decoded.mem_to_reg = dec_mem_to_reg;\n86:     ctrl_decoded.is_illegal = dec_is_illegal;\n87:   end\n88: \n89:   // ── ID/EX register ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n90:   id_ex_t reg_q;\n91: \n92:   always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n93:     if (reset || flush) begin\n94:       reg_q <= '0;\n95:     end else if (!stall) begin\n96:       reg_q.pc       <= in.pc;\n97:       reg_q.rs1_val  <= rs1_data;\n98:       reg_q.rs2_val  <= rs2_data;\n99:       reg_q.imm      <= imm;\n100:       reg_q.rd       <= in.instr[11:7];\n101:       reg_q.rs1_addr <= in.instr[19:15];\n102:       reg_q.rs2_addr <= in.instr[24:20];\n103:       reg_q.ctrl     <= ctrl_decoded;\n104:       reg_q.instr    <= in.instr;\n105:       reg_q.valid    <= in.valid;\n106:     end\n107:   end\n108: \n109:   assign out = reg_q;\n110: \n111: endmodule\n\n(End of file - total 111 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"// rtl/id_stage.sv\n//\n// Decode stage. Combinationally drives the regfile read ports and the\n// ID/EX register's next-state from the IF/ID combinational bundle plus\n// the regfile read data. The ID/EX register is owned by this module so\n// the decoded view of instruction n is latched by end of cycle n+1.\n//\n// Latency:        1 cycle (ID/EX register clocked here).\n// RVFI fields:    feeds rs1_addr, rs1_rdata, rs2_addr, rs2_rdata, insn,\n//                 trap (via ctrl.is_illegal).\nmodule id_stage (\n  input  logic              clock,\n  input  logic              reset,\n  input  logic              stall,\n  input  logic              flush,\n  input  if_id_t  in,\n  // regfile read interface\n  output logic [4:0]        rs1_addr,\n  output logic [4:0]        rs2_addr,\n  input  logic [31:0]       rs1_data,","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv","time":{"start":1778855829756,"end":1778855829777}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04d1e0472f756cde016a072f952cfc8198a1a54146675fcf8f"}},"id":"prt_e2c11e0e9002ScCcHXR4A3Y8wB","sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","messageID":"msg_e2c11ac9c00125lsPiK4P6GI1F"}}
