ores is a good lever on this RTL because CoreMark issues enough stack/list/matrix/state stores that turning `io_dmemReady=0` on STOREs from a whole-pipeline freeze into a one-deep deferred write raises IPC, as long as younger memory ops and end-visible markers stay fenced behind the pending slot... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n7: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778853894428,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d40bf73fffeu3RU5Gf0kIKttG\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_qoWXXtxJp2gYpPN1MyIrzpOf\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"micro_opt|store slot|divider|replay|target cache|predict\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 10 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 1: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"baseline-bench-2c63e03\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Baseline retest for cores/bench\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 282.82, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 0.0, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 0.0, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 127.03, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 9563, \\\"ff\\\": 1866, \\\"seeds\\\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-05-15T08:52:45.091730Z\\\", \\\"round_id\\\": 0, \\\"slot\\\": 0}\\n\\n  Line 2: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Iterative Cold Divider Off EX Path\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address generation, branch support, and\\\\nMUL. On a Tang Nano 20K, a full 32-bit divider is a strong candidate for\\\\nth