{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778856010366,"sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_RSpuTlRu4SokaEdBPzRlzwIS","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r5s1\n+title: \"MEM-Stage Store-Data Forwarding\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The proven `bench` wins so far have all stayed off the fragile frontend:\n+  moving DIV/REM off the universal EX path and adding the one-deep deferred\n+  store slot. The failed predictor, load-replay, and deeper-store-queue tries\n+  define the boundary clearly: extra fetch-path logic and wider MEM-side\n+  buffering cost too much Fmax or placement quality on this FPGA.\n+\n+  One structural bubble source remains in the existing 5-stage pipeline. A\n+  load followed immediately by a STORE of that loaded register still pays the\n+  full textbook load-use stall even when the STORE only needs the value as\n+  write data (`rs2`), not as its address base (`rs1`). That dependency does\n+  not need an EX-stage bubble because store data is not consumed until MEM.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move STORE data consumption to the stage where the core actually uses it.\n+  Keep STORE address generation in EX exactly as it is today, but stop\n+  treating a load->STORE `rs2` match as an EX-time hazard. Instead, let the\n+  STORE advance, carry its `rs2` register number and provisional value through\n+  EX/MEM, and in `mem_stage` select the final store data from the older\n+  MEM/WB writeback value when that writeback supplies the STORE's `rs2`.\n+\n+  This is a structural retiming of an existing dependency, not a new queue or\n+  predictor. It should recover a useful subset of load-use bubbles while\n+  keeping load data off the ALU, branch, and JALR critical paths. To avoid\n+  repeating the prior RVFI failure mode, the same late-selected value should\n+  also drive the STORE's RVFI-visible `rs2_rdata`, `mem_wdata`, and deferred\n+  store-slot capture path, so formal sees the architectural source value that\n+  the STORE really consumed.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Recognize younger STOREs and suppress the load-use bubble when the older load matches only STORE `rs2`, while preserving stalls for STORE `rs1` address dependencies and all non-STORE consumers.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add late store-data selection from MEM/WB writeback, use that value for dmem write data, pending-store-slot capture, and RVFI-visible store source/memory fields, and keep the existing misalign and store-slot ordering rules intact.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Plumb the extra hazard classification and MEM-stage writeback-bypass inputs needed for the late store-data path without changing the top-level IO contract.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add coverage for load->STORE-data pairs that should no longer bubble, plus RVFI checks that the retiring STORE reports the forwarded source value under both zero-wait and dmem-stall/store-slot cases.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r5s1\n+title: \"MEM-Stage Store-Data Forwarding\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The proven `bench` wins so far have all stayed off the fragile frontend:\n+  moving DIV/REM off the universal EX path and adding the one-deep deferred\n+  store slot. The failed predictor, load-replay, and deeper-store-queue tries\n+  define the boundary clearly: extra fetch-path logic and wider MEM-side\n+  buffering cost too much Fmax or placement quality on this FPGA.\n+\n+  One structural bubble source remains in the existing 5-stage pipeline. A\n+  load followed immediately by a STORE of that loaded register still pays the\n+  full textbook load-use stall even when the STORE only needs the value as\n+  write data (`rs2`), not as its address base (`rs1`). That dependency does\n+  not need an EX-stage bubble because store data is not consumed until MEM.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move STORE data consumption to the stage where the core actually uses it.\n+  Keep STORE address generation in EX exactly as it is today, but stop\n+  treating a load->STORE `rs2` match as an EX-time hazard. Instead, let the\n+  STORE advance, carry its `rs2` register number and provisional value through\n+  EX/MEM, and in `mem_stage` select the final store data from the older\n+  MEM/WB writeback value when that writeback supplies the STORE's `rs2`.\n+\n+  This is a structural retiming of an existing dependency, not a new queue or\n+  predictor. It should recover a useful subset of load-use bubbles while\n+  keeping load data off the ALU, branch, and JALR critical paths. To avoid\n+  repeating the prior RVFI failure mode, the same late-selected value should\n+  also drive the STORE's RVFI-visible `rs2_rdata`, `mem_wdata`, and deferred\n+  store-slot capture path, so formal sees the architectural source value that\n+  the STORE really consumed.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Recognize younger STOREs and suppress the load-use bubble when the older load matches only STORE `rs2`, while preserving stalls for STORE `rs1` address dependencies and all non-STORE consumers.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add late store-data selection from MEM/WB writeback, use that value for dmem write data, pending-store-slot capture, and RVFI-visible store source/memory fields, and keep the existing misalign and store-slot ordering rules intact.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Plumb the extra hazard classification and MEM-stage writeback-bypass inputs needed for the late store-data path without changing the top-level IO contract.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add coverage for load->STORE-data pairs that should no longer bubble, plus RVFI checks that the retiring STORE reports the forwarded source value under both zero-wait and dmem-stall/store-slot cases.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r5s1\n+title: \"MEM-Stage Store-Data Forwarding\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The proven `bench` wins so far have all stayed off the fragile frontend:\n+  moving DIV/REM off the universal EX path and adding the one-deep deferred\n+  store slot. The failed predictor, load-replay, and deeper-store-queue tries\n+  define the boundary clearly: extra fetch-path logic and wider MEM-side\n+  buffering cost too much Fmax or placement quality on this FPGA.\n+\n+  One structural bubble source remains in the existing 5-stage pipeline. A\n+  load followed immediately by a STORE of that loaded register still pays the\n+  full textbook load-use stall even when the STORE only needs the value as\n+  write data (`rs2`), not as its address base (`rs1`). That dependency does\n+  not need an EX-stage bubble because store data is not consumed until MEM.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move STORE data consumption to the stage where the core actually uses it.\n+  Keep STORE address generation in EX exactly as it is today, but stop\n+  treating a load->STORE `rs2` match as an EX-time hazard. Instead, let the\n+  STORE advance, carry its `rs2` register number and provisional value through\n+  EX/MEM, and in `mem_stage` select the final store data from the older\n+  MEM/WB writeback value when that writeback supplies the STORE's `rs2`.\n+\n+  This is a structural retiming of an existing dependency, not a new queue or\n+  predictor. It should recover a useful subset of load-use bubbles while\n+  keeping load data off the ALU, branch, and JALR critical paths. To avoid\n+  repeating the prior RVFI failure mode, the same late-selected value should\n+  also drive the STORE's RVFI-visible `rs2_rdata`, `mem_wdata`, and deferred\n+  store-slot capture path, so formal sees the architectural source value that\n+  the STORE really consumed.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Recognize younger STOREs and suppress the load-use bubble when the older load matches only STORE `rs2`, while preserving stalls for STORE `rs1` address dependencies and all non-STORE consumers.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add late store-data selection from MEM/WB writeback, use that value for dmem write data, pending-store-slot capture, and RVFI-visible store source/memory fields, and keep the existing misalign and store-slot ordering rules intact.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Plumb the extra hazard classification and MEM-stage writeback-bypass inputs needed for the late store-data path without changing the top-level IO contract.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add coverage for load->STORE-data pairs that should no longer bubble, plus RVFI checks that the retiring STORE reports the forwarded source value under both zero-wait and dmem-stall/store-slot cases.\"\n","additions":42,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778856010359,"end":1778856010364}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_089e7580e7cbd175016a07303d0c888198a8f2a8af7533d24a"}},"id":"prt_e2c146ed5001xqyl0myn9BCTuZ","sessionID":"ses_1d3eea7f2ffevXBifDVCm56EIH","messageID":"msg_e2c1435b700119iZBZkmCrIsvM"}}
