oo much Fmax or placement quality on this FPGA.\\n\\nOne structural bubble source remains in the existing 5-stage pipeline. A\\nload followed immediately by a STORE of that loaded register still pays the\\nfull textbook load-use stall even when the STORE only needs the value as\\nwrite data (`rs2`), not as its address base (`rs1`). That dependency does\\nnot need an EX-stage bubble because store data is not consumed until MEM.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The proven `bench` wins so far have all stayed off the fragile frontend:\\nmoving DIV/REM off the universal EX path and adding the one-deep deferred\\nstore slot. The failed predictor, load-replay, and deeper-store-queue tries\\ndefine the boundary clearly: extra fetch-path logic and wider MEM-side\\nbuffering cost too much Fmax or placement quality on this FPGA.\\n\\nOne structural bubble source remains in the existing 5-stage pipeline. A\\nload followed immediately by a STORE of that loaded register still pays the\\nfull textbook load-use stall even when the STORE only needs the value as\\nwrite data (`rs2`), not as its address base (`rs1`). That dependency does\\nnot need an EX-stage bubble because store data is not consumed until MEM.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move STORE data consumption to the stage where the core actually uses it.\\nKeep STORE address generation in EX exactly as it is today, but stop\\ntreating a load->STORE `rs2` match as an EX-time hazard. Instead, let the\\nSTORE advance, carry its `rs2` register number and provisional value through\\nEX/MEM, and in `mem_stage` select the final store data from the older\\nMEM/WB writeback value when that writeback supplies the STORE's `rs2`.\\n\\nThis is a structural retiming of an existing dependency, not a new queue or\\npredictor. It should recover a useful subset of load-use bubbles while\\nkeeping load data off the ALU, branch, and JALR critical paths. To avoid\\nrepeating the prior RVFI failure mode, the same late-selected value should\\nalso drive the STORE's RVFI-visible `rs2_rdata`, `mem_wdata`, and deferred\\nstore-slot capture path, so formal sees the architectural source value that\\nthe STORE really consumed.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize younger STOREs and suppress the load-use bubble when the older load matches only STORE `rs2`, while preserving stalls for STORE `rs1` address dependencies and all non-STORE consumers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add late store-data selection from MEM/WB writeback, use that value for dmem write data, pending-store-slot capture, and RVFI-visible store source/memory fields, and keep the existing misalign and store-slot ordering rules intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Plumb the extra hazard classification and MEM-stage writeback-bypass inputs needed for the late store-data path without changing the top-level IO contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add coverage for load->STORE-data pairs that should no longer bubble, plus RVFI checks that the retiring STORE reports the forwarded source value under both zero-wait and dmem-stall/store-slot cases.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize younger STOREs and suppress the load-use bubble when the older load matches only STORE `rs2`, while preserving stalls for STORE `rs1` address dependencies and all non-STORE consumers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add late store-data selection from MEM/WB writeback, use that value for dmem write data, pending-store-slot capture, and RVFI-visible store source/memory fields, and keep the existing misalign and store-slot ordering rules intact.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Plumb the extra hazard classification and MEM-stage writeback-bypass inputs needed for the late store-data path without changing the top-level IO contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add coverage for load->STORE-data pairs that should no longer bubble, plus RVFI checks that the retiring STORE reports the forwarded source value under both zero-wait and dmem-stall/store-slot cases.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\n48 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:40  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:40  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:40  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:40  Status: failed\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:43 (103)\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:21 (21)\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_44_60 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:44.6-44.59 step 20\\nSBY 11:55:48 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFormal: 52 passed, 1 failed\\nFailed: reg_ch0\\n\\n--- reg_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\\nSBY 11:54:09 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:01  Skipping step 10..\\nSBY 11:54:09 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:01  Skipping step 11..\\nSBY 11:54:10 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:01  Skipping step 12..\\nSBY 11:54:10 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:02  Skipping step 13..\\nSBY 11:54:10 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:02  Skipping step 14..\\nSBY 11:54:10 [reg_c