{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778862648622,"sessionID":"ses_1d38f3977ffeJ6hm6AtPHiJ1zg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_qHvr3C4Y7cle4pJqX3s2TVu8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r6s1\n+title: \"RVFI-Safe Late Store-Data Bypass\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The best `bench` gains so far have come from backend-only structural changes\n+  that leave the fragile fetch path alone: first moving DIV/REM off the hot EX\n+  cone, then letting stalled normal-RAM stores retire into a one-deep deferred\n+  slot. A remaining bubble source is the textbook load-use stall on a younger\n+  STORE whose dependency is only `rs2` store data, not the EX-time address\n+  operand.\n+\n+  That lever is still attractive even though the last attempt broke formal. The\n+  failure was a correctness-accounting problem around canonical RVFI source data,\n+  not evidence that the workload opportunity is gone.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Retiming STORE data to MEM is still the most promising structural next step,\n+  but it needs an explicit architectural-source shadow instead of a late ad hoc\n+  repair. Relax the load-use interlock only for the safe case where an older\n+  LOAD feeds a younger STORE's `rs2` while `rs1` remains independent. Carry\n+  store-data source metadata through EX/MEM, then in `mem_stage` select the\n+  final store payload from the older writeback/load result when needed.\n+\n+  Use that same canonical late-selected value everywhere the STORE becomes\n+  architecturally visible: physical `dmem_wdata`, deferred-store-slot capture,\n+  MEM/WB's store-source field, and RVFI `rs2_rdata` / `mem_wdata`. This keeps\n+  the frontend and hot ALU path unchanged, preserves the existing one-deep store\n+  slot, and should turn a real CoreMark load-update-store dependency pattern\n+  into overlap instead of a mandatory bubble.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add explicit pipeline metadata for late store-data sourcing so STORE rs2 can be canonicalized separately from EX-time operands.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Preserve STORE address generation in EX while tagging the cases where store data must be finalized later from an older load/writeback result.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Select canonical store data in MEM, use it for bus writes, deferred-store-slot capture, and the retiring STORE's RVFI-visible source and memory fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Relax the load-use bubble only for younger STORE rs2 dependencies, while keeping STORE rs1 address hazards and all other consumers conservative.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Plumb the extra writeback-to-MEM bypass inputs and keep top-level RVFI sourced from the canonical late-selected STORE value without changing the IO contract.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add regressions for immediate load-then-store-data pairs, including deferred-store-slot cases, and assert the retiring STORE reports the forwarded rs2/mem_wdata value.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r6s1\n+title: \"RVFI-Safe Late Store-Data Bypass\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The best `bench` gains so far have come from backend-only structural changes\n+  that leave the fragile fetch path alone: first moving DIV/REM off the hot EX\n+  cone, then letting stalled normal-RAM stores retire into a one-deep deferred\n+  slot. A remaining bubble source is the textbook load-use stall on a younger\n+  STORE whose dependency is only `rs2` store data, not the EX-time address\n+  operand.\n+\n+  That lever is still attractive even though the last attempt broke formal. The\n+  failure was a correctness-accounting problem around canonical RVFI source data,\n+  not evidence that the workload opportunity is gone.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Retiming STORE data to MEM is still the most promising structural next step,\n+  but it needs an explicit architectural-source shadow instead of a late ad hoc\n+  repair. Relax the load-use interlock only for the safe case where an older\n+  LOAD feeds a younger STORE's `rs2` while `rs1` remains independent. Carry\n+  store-data source metadata through EX/MEM, then in `mem_stage` select the\n+  final store payload from the older writeback/load result when needed.\n+\n+  Use that same canonical late-selected value everywhere the STORE becomes\n+  architecturally visible: physical `dmem_wdata`, deferred-store-slot capture,\n+  MEM/WB's store-source field, and RVFI `rs2_rdata` / `mem_wdata`. This keeps\n+  the frontend and hot ALU path unchanged, preserves the existing one-deep store\n+  slot, and should turn a real CoreMark load-update-store dependency pattern\n+  into overlap instead of a mandatory bubble.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add explicit pipeline metadata for late store-data sourcing so STORE rs2 can be canonicalized separately from EX-time operands.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Preserve STORE address generation in EX while tagging the cases where store data must be finalized later from an older load/writeback result.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Select canonical store data in MEM, use it for bus writes, deferred-store-slot capture, and the retiring STORE's RVFI-visible source and memory fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Relax the load-use bubble only for younger STORE rs2 dependencies, while keeping STORE rs1 address hazards and all other consumers conservative.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Plumb the extra writeback-to-MEM bypass inputs and keep top-level RVFI sourced from the canonical late-selected STORE value without changing the IO contract.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add regressions for immediate load-then-store-data pairs, including deferred-store-slot cases, and assert the retiring STORE reports the forwarded rs2/mem_wdata value.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r6s1\n+title: \"RVFI-Safe Late Store-Data Bypass\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The best `bench` gains so far have come from backend-only structural changes\n+  that leave the fragile fetch path alone: first moving DIV/REM off the hot EX\n+  cone, then letting stalled normal-RAM stores retire into a one-deep deferred\n+  slot. A remaining bubble source is the textbook load-use stall on a younger\n+  STORE whose dependency is only `rs2` store data, not the EX-time address\n+  operand.\n+\n+  That lever is still attractive even though the last attempt broke formal. The\n+  failure was a correctness-accounting problem around canonical RVFI source data,\n+  not evidence that the workload opportunity is gone.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Retiming STORE data to MEM is still the most promising structural next step,\n+  but it needs an explicit architectural-source shadow instead of a late ad hoc\n+  repair. Relax the load-use interlock only for the safe case where an older\n+  LOAD feeds a younger STORE's `rs2` while `rs1` remains independent. Carry\n+  store-data source metadata through EX/MEM, then in `mem_stage` select the\n+  final store payload from the older writeback/load result when needed.\n+\n+  Use that same canonical late-selected value everywhere the STORE becomes\n+  architecturally visible: physical `dmem_wdata`, deferred-store-slot capture,\n+  MEM/WB's store-source field, and RVFI `rs2_rdata` / `mem_wdata`. This keeps\n+  the frontend and hot ALU path unchanged, preserves the existing one-deep store\n+  slot, and should turn a real CoreMark load-update-store dependency pattern\n+  into overlap instead of a mandatory bubble.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add explicit pipeline metadata for late store-data sourcing so STORE rs2 can be canonicalized separately from EX-time operands.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Preserve STORE address generation in EX while tagging the cases where store data must be finalized later from an older load/writeback result.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Select canonical store data in MEM, use it for bus writes, deferred-store-slot capture, and the retiring STORE's RVFI-visible source and memory fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Relax the load-use bubble only for younger STORE rs2 dependencies, while keeping STORE rs1 address hazards and all other consumers conservative.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Plumb the extra writeback-to-MEM bypass inputs and keep top-level RVFI sourced from the canonical late-selected STORE value without changing the IO contract.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add regressions for immediate load-then-store-data pairs, including deferred-store-slot cases, and assert the retiring STORE reports the forwarded rs2/mem_wdata value.\"\n","additions":44,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778862648599,"end":1778862648619}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0349a74bd1bd3b17016a074a2b11488194a98907cdf1619478"}},"id":"prt_e2c79b88f001aWyUCVcVCiEbnh","sessionID":"ses_1d38f3977ffeJ6hm6AtPHiJ1zg","messageID":"msg_e2c794d4b001WBN0u65mhFjSHi"}}
