{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778862655202,"sessionID":"ses_1d38f3977ffeJ6hm6AtPHiJ1zg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_D7r577BG9Wm3BqmArUqHRGhX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml","offset":1,"limit":250},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-002-r6s1\n2: title: \"RVFI-Safe Late Store-Data Bypass\"\n3: category: structural\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The best `bench` gains so far have come from backend-only structural changes\n6:   that leave the fragile fetch path alone: first moving DIV/REM off the hot EX\n7:   cone, then letting stalled normal-RAM stores retire into a one-deep deferred\n8:   slot. A remaining bubble source is the textbook load-use stall on a younger\n9:   STORE whose dependency is only `rs2` store data, not the EX-time address\n10:   operand.\n11: \n12:   That lever is still attractive even though the last attempt broke formal. The\n13:   failure was a correctness-accounting problem around canonical RVFI source data,\n14:   not evidence that the workload opportunity is gone.\n15: hypothesis: |\n16:   Retiming STORE data to MEM is still the most promising structural next step,\n17:   but it needs an explicit architectural-source shadow instead of a late ad hoc\n18:   repair. Relax the load-use interlock only for the safe case where an older\n19:   LOAD feeds a younger STORE's `rs2` while `rs1` remains independent. Carry\n20:   store-data source metadata through EX/MEM, then in `mem_stage` select the\n21:   final store payload from the older writeback/load result when needed.\n22: \n23:   Use that same canonical late-selected value everywhere the STORE becomes\n24:   architecturally visible: physical `dmem_wdata`, deferred-store-slot capture,\n25:   MEM/WB's store-source field, and RVFI `rs2_rdata` / `mem_wdata`. This keeps\n26:   the frontend and hot ALU path unchanged, preserves the existing one-deep store\n27:   slot, and should turn a real CoreMark load-update-store dependency pattern\n28:   into overlap instead of a mandatory bubble.\n29: expected_impact:\n30:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n31:   confidence: medium\n32: changes:\n33:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n34:     description: \"Add explicit pipeline metadata for late store-data sourcing so STORE rs2 can be canonicalized separately from EX-time operands.\"\n35:   - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n36:     description: \"Preserve STORE address generation in EX while tagging the cases where store data must be finalized later from an older load/writeback result.\"\n37:   - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n38:     description: \"Select canonical store data in MEM, use it for bus writes, deferred-store-slot capture, and the retiring STORE's RVFI-visible source and memory fields.\"\n39:   - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n40:     description: \"Relax the load-use bubble only for younger STORE rs2 dependencies, while keeping STORE rs1 address hazards and all other consumers conservative.\"\n41:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n42:     description: \"Plumb the extra writeback-to-MEM bypass inputs and keep top-level RVFI sourced from the canonical late-selected STORE value without changing the IO contract.\"\n43:   - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n44:     description: \"Add regressions for immediate load-then-store-data pairs, including deferred-store-slot cases, and assert the retiring STORE reports the forwarded rs2/mem_wdata value.\"\n\n(End of file - total 44 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-002-r6s1\ntitle: \"RVFI-Safe Late Store-Data Bypass\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The best `bench` gains so far have come from backend-only structural changes\n  that leave the fragile fetch path alone: first moving DIV/REM off the hot EX\n  cone, then letting stalled normal-RAM stores retire into a one-deep deferred\n  slot. A remaining bubble source is the textbook load-use stall on a younger\n  STORE whose dependency is only `rs2` store data, not the EX-time address\n  operand.\n\n  That lever is still attractive even though the last attempt broke formal. The\n  failure was a correctness-accounting problem around canonical RVFI source data,\n  not evidence that the workload opportunity is gone.\nhypothesis: |\n  Retiming STORE data to MEM is still the most promising structural next step,\n  but it needs an explicit architectural-source shadow instead of a late ad hoc\n  repair. Relax the load-use interlock only for the safe case where an older\n  LOAD feeds a younger STORE's `rs2` while `rs1` remains independent. Carry\n  store-data source metadata through EX/MEM, then in `mem_stage` select the","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r6s1.yaml","time":{"start":1778862655178,"end":1778862655202}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_088378a55e2246e0016a074a3eb2f88196bb3fc24af7dd7554"}},"id":"prt_e2c7a05b20018nhpZTx2BUGCzi","sessionID":"ses_1d38f3977ffeJ6hm6AtPHiJ1zg","messageID":"msg_e2c79eead001uQAzu4XMOyDXM7"}}
