{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778869428437,"sessionID":"ses_1d321652dffeLxfBtvQNP2V0z4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_8NckF1tiXlF1lUASM1pEMez4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r8s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r8s1\n+title: \"Canonical Late Store-Data Lane\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The proven `bench` wins have come from backend-only structural changes that\n+  improve IPC or Fmax without touching the fragile fetch path. The remaining\n+  bubble that still looks worth chasing is the forced load-use stall when a\n+  younger STORE depends on an older LOAD only for `rs2` write data: the store\n+  address is ready in EX, but the current pipeline still treats store data as\n+  an EX-time operand and burns a full bubble.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Retiming STORE data to the stage where it becomes architecturally visible is\n+  still the best structural next step, but it has to be implemented as a\n+  coherent data lane rather than a late one-off bypass. Add explicit metadata\n+  for when store data may arrive from WB and carry it through EX/MEM; relax the\n+  load-use interlock only for the safe case where a younger STORE's `rs2`\n+  depends on an older LOAD while `rs1` remains independent. In MEM, choose one\n+  canonical final store-data value and use that same value for physical\n+  `dmem_wdata`, deferred-store-slot capture, MEM/WB `rs2_val`, and RVFI\n+  `rs2_rdata` / `mem_wdata`. This keeps the fetch path unchanged, preserves the\n+  existing zero-wait store fast path, and directly targets a real CoreMark\n+  bubble source that prior attempts exposed but did not yet implement\n+  correctly.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add late-store-data metadata to the ID/EX and EX/MEM bundles so the store-data source stays explicit through retirement.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Expose the decode information needed to identify STOREs whose `rs2` can be consumed late, without broadening the rest of the hazard policy.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Relax the load-use interlock only for the single safe LOAD->STORE-data case, while keeping all EX-time dependencies conservative.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Carry the provisional store payload plus the late-source metadata into EX/MEM while leaving STORE address generation and the non-store fast path unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Select one canonical final store-data value in MEM, use it for direct stores and deferred-store-slot capture, and write the same value into the MEM/WB RVFI-facing fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the new late-store metadata through the top level and keep RVFI sourced from the canonical MEM/WB value.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add directed pipeline tests for LOAD->STORE `rs2` dependencies, including deferred-store-slot and RVFI-visible source-data cases.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r8s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r8s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r8s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r8s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r8s1\n+title: \"Canonical Late Store-Data Lane\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The proven `bench` wins have come from backend-only structural changes that\n+  improve IPC or Fmax without touching the fragile fetch path. The remaining\n+  bubble that still looks worth chasing is the forced load-use stall when a\n+  younger STORE depends on an older LOAD only for `rs2` write data: the store\n+  address is ready in EX, but the current pipeline still treats store data as\n+  an EX-time operand and burns a full bubble.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Retiming STORE data to the stage where it becomes architecturally visible is\n+  still the best structural next step, but it has to be implemented as a\n+  coherent data lane rather than a late one-off bypass. Add explicit metadata\n+  for when store data may arrive from WB and carry it through EX/MEM; relax the\n+  load-use interlock only for the safe case where a younger STORE's `rs2`\n+  depends on an older LOAD while `rs1` remains independent. In MEM, choose one\n+  canonical final store-data value and use that same value for physical\n+  `dmem_wdata`, deferred-store-slot capture, MEM/WB `rs2_val`, and RVFI\n+  `rs2_rdata` / `mem_wdata`. This keeps the fetch path unchanged, preserves the\n+  existing zero-wait store fast path, and directly targets a real CoreMark\n+  bubble source that prior attempts exposed but did not yet implement\n+  correctly.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add late-store-data metadata to the ID/EX and EX/MEM bundles so the store-data source stays explicit through retirement.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Expose the decode information needed to identify STOREs whose `rs2` can be consumed late, without broadening the rest of the hazard policy.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Relax the load-use interlock only for the single safe LOAD->STORE-data case, while keeping all EX-time dependencies conservative.\"\n+  - 