en\\nfill the slot's cached target instruction the next time that target is fetched\\narchitecturally. On a later hit for the same branch PC, keep the normal\\nsequential PC path, but mark the branch as predicted-taken and inject the\\ncached target instruction/PC into IF->ID on the following cycle instead of the\\nwrong-path sequential word.\\n\\nEX remains the architectural source of truth. A correctly folded branch would\\nrepair the fetch PC to `target + 4` while preserving the injected target in\\nID, and a loop-exit miss would redirect back to `pc + 4` and flush the folded\\nwrong-path instruction. This aims to win back one cycle on the hottest loop\\nbackedges while avoiding the extra `next_pc` compare/mux cost that sank the\\nearlier predictor attempts.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend IF/ID and ID/EX metadata with branch-fold prediction bits and predicted target PC fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a one-slot branch-fold entry that trains from EX, captures the first target instruction on a live fetch, and can inject that cached instruction without changing the PC increment path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the fold-prediction metadata alongside the branch instruction so EX can distinguish a correct fold from a repair redirect.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Train only taken backward branches, compare predicted versus architectural next PC, and emit separate repair semantics for correct folded hits versus loop-exit misses.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the new IF training and EX repair signals through the top level while keeping the existing nret=1 RVFI contract unchanged.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Refine redirect flushing so a correct folded prediction preserves the injected target in ID while still killing the stray IF word