0260515-003-r6s2\",\"title\":\"Single-Slot Backedge Branch Fold Buffer\",\"category\":\"predictor\",\"motivation\":\"Every predictor attempt on `bench` that touched the frontend `pc -> next_pc`\\ncone regressed: ID-stage BTFNT added decode and target-generation delay, and\\neven tiny taken-target caches still paid too much tag-compare and target-mux\\ncost in IF. But CoreMark remains dominated by tight taken loop backedges, so\\nalways waiting for EX to redirect still leaves repeatable control bubbles on\\nthe table.\\n\\nThe best remaining predictor angle is therefore one that predicts only the\\nhottest already-seen backedge while leaving `io_imemAddr` generation on its\\ncurrent simple sequential path.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"Every predictor attempt on `bench` that touched the frontend `pc -> next_pc`\\ncone regressed: ID-stage BTFNT added decode and target-generation delay, and\\neven tiny taken-target caches still paid too much tag-compare and target-mux\\ncost in IF. But CoreMark remains dominated by tight taken loop backedges, so\\nalways waiting for EX to redirect still leaves repeatable control bubbles on\\nthe table.\\n\\nThe best remaining predictor angle is therefore one that predicts only the\\nhottest already-seen backedge while leaving `io_imemAddr` generation on its\\ncurrent simple sequential path.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a one-entry EX-trained branch-fold buffer for taken backward conditional\\nbranches. When EX resolves a taken backedge, record the branch PC and target\\nPC, then capture the target instruction the next time that target is fetched\\narchitecturally. On a later hit for the same branch PC, keep the normal\\nsequential fetch address path, but tag the branch as predicted-taken and\\ninject the cached target instruction/PC into IF->ID on the following cycle\\ninstead of the wrong-path fallthrough word.\\n\\nEX remains the architectural source of truth. A correct prediction repairs\\nthe fetch PC to `target + 4` after the folded target has already entered the\\npipe, while a loop-exit miss or stale slot falls back to the existing flush\\nand redirect behavior. This tries to recover one taken-branch bubble in the\\nCoreMark hot loops without reintroducing the Fmax loss from putting target\\nselection directly on the fetch-address critical path.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the minimal fold-prediction metadata that must travel with an in-flight branch and a folded target instruction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire fold-buffer train, hit, and repair signals between IF, EX, and hazard control without changing the top-level IO contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement a one-entry backedge fold buffer that caches branch PC, target PC, and target instruction, and injects the cached target into IF->ID while leaving `io_imemAddr` on the normal sequential path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the fold-hit metadata alongside the branch so EX can tell whether the younger target instruction was injected speculatively.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Train the buffer from resolved taken backward branches and convert redirect handling into fold success, stale-slot repair, or loop-exit mispredict recovery.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Adjust flush logic so a correctly folded target survives branch resolution while wrong-path or stale folded instructions are still killed safely.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the minimal fold-prediction metadata that must travel with an in-flight branch and a folded target instruction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire fold-buffer train, hit, and repair signals between IF, EX, and hazard control without changing the t