st remaining predictor angle is therefore one that predicts only the\\nhottest already-seen backedge while leaving `io_imemAddr` generation on its\\ncurrent simple sequential path.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a one-entry EX-trained branch-fold buffer for taken backward conditional\\nbranches. When EX resolves a taken backedge, record the branch PC and target\\nPC, then capture the target instruction the next time that target is fetched\\narchitecturally. On a later hit for the same branch PC, keep the normal\\nsequential fetch address path, but tag the branch as predicted-taken and\\ninject the cached target instruction/PC into IF->ID on the following cycle\\ninstead of the wrong-path fallthrough word.\\n\\nEX remains the architectural source of truth. A correct prediction repairs\\nthe fetch PC to `target + 4` after the folded target has already entered the\\npipe, while a loop-exit miss or stale slot falls back to the existing flush\\nand redirect behavior. This tries to recover one taken-branch bubble in the\\nCoreMark hot loops without reintroducing the Fmax loss from putting target\\nselection directly on the fetch-address critical path.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the minimal fold-prediction metadata that must travel with an in-flight branch and a folded target instruction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire fold-buffer train, hit, and repair signals between IF, EX, and hazard control without changing the top-level IO contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement a one-entry backedge fold buffer that caches branch PC, target PC, and target instruction, and injects the cached target into IF->ID while leaving `io_imemAddr` on the normal sequential path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the fold-hit metadata alongside the branch so EX can tell whether the younger target instruction was injected speculatively.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Train the buffer from resolved taken backward branches and convert redirect handling into fold success, stale-slot repair, or loop-exit mispredict recovery.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Adjust flush logic so a correctly folded target survives branch resolution while wrong-path or stale folded instructions are still killed safely.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the minimal fold-prediction metadata that must travel with an in-flight branch and a folded target instruction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire fold-buffer train, hit, and repair signals between IF, EX, and hazard control without changing the top-level IO contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement a one-entry backedge fold buffer that caches branch PC, target PC, and target instruction, and injects the cached target into IF->ID while leaving `io_imemAddr` on the normal sequential path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the fold-hit metadata alongside the branch so EX can tell whether the younger target instruction was injected speculatively.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Train the buffer from resolved taken backward branches and convert redirect handling into fold success, stale-slot repair, or loop-exit mispredict recovery.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Adjust flush logic so a correctly folded target survives branch resolution while wrong-path or stale folded instructions are still killed safely.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":447.4,\"delta_pct\":0.0,\"vs_baseline\":58.19,\"fmax_mhz\":199.44,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4457730,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":5847,\"ff\":2255,\"seeds\":[199.44,202.63,197.59],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementati