{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778872801570,"sessionID":"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_4P1CuC1cFQ7mIgMnviJ5rjRF","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r10s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r10s2\n+title: \"Single-Slot JAL and Backedge Fold Buffer\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Every `bench` predictor that changed the live fetch `pc -> next_pc` path\n+  regressed, but the one-slot backedge fold buffer was effectively timing\n+  neutral at 447.40 fitness. That points to a narrow remaining predictor\n+  window: recover taken-control bubbles by injecting already-cached target\n+  instructions, not by adding another frontend target mux, tag lookup, or\n+  decode-armed redirect.\n+\n+  CoreMark still spends cycles on both hot loop backedges and repeated direct\n+  calls. The prior fold buffer only covered backward conditional branches, so\n+  it left all direct `JAL` bubbles on the table even though `JAL` is perfectly\n+  predictable and should not suffer loop-exit misses.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Introduce a one-slot control-flow fold buffer that trains on two low-entropy\n+  classes only: taken backward conditional branches and direct `JAL`. The slot\n+  records the control PC, resolved target PC, and the first target instruction\n+  once that target is fetched architecturally. On a later hit, `if_stage`\n+  leaves `io_imemAddr` on the normal sequential path but tags the control\n+  instruction so the following cycle can inject the cached target instruction\n+  into IF/ID instead of a bubble or fallthrough word.\n+\n+  EX remains the architectural source of truth. A correct folded hit repairs\n+  the fetch PC to `target + 4`, while loop-exit misses, stale slots, and any\n+  non-covered control flow fall back to the current flush-and-redirect path.\n+  Compared with the prior backedge-only fold buffer, this adds very little new\n+  timing risk while broadening coverage to CoreMark's direct-call traffic,\n+  which is the most plausible remaining predictor lever on this core.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: low\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add minimal fold metadata bits that travel with a predicted control instruction and its injected target.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Implement a one-slot control-flow fold entry keyed by control PC, cache the first target instruction after an architectural fetch, and inject it on later hits without changing the sequential `io_imemAddr` path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch fold-hit metadata with the control instruction so later stages can distinguish a normal redirect from a successful folded hit.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Train the slot on taken backward branches and direct `JAL`, validate folded hits against the architectural next PC, and request `target + 4` repair only when the injected instruction was correct.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire fold-train, fold-hit, and repair signals across IF, ID, EX, and hazard control while preserving the nret=1 top-level contract.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Refine flush behavior so a correct folded target survives branch resolution while stale or wrong folded injections are still killed.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add a pipeline test that warms the fold slot on repeated direct calls and taken backedges and checks RVFI-order-safe recovery on loop exit and stale-slot misses.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r10s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/co