658407},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0c10bffe56b6101c016a074a41fc54819691fdbb42ac3da329\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}}}}\n33: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778862658532,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39a0ffeX2wiAJx0ZaPdZq\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2c7a13e3001h29bw4HIQAaN1Y\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"7e597f9fdf228778dd04439df2a285971435d7a6\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2c7a050b001pSAUDtvAYezoJG\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39a0ffeX2wiAJx0ZaPdZq\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":63896,\"input\":802,\"output\":73,\"reasoning\":45,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":62976}},\"cost\":0}}\n\n(End of file - total 33 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778862507862,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39a0ffeX2wiAJx0ZaPdZq\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2c77c73e001Wj6vV0cyTmMO0J\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2c70c8b2001wLwmXTY0GF55Er\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39a0ffeX2wiAJx0ZaPdZq\",\"snapshot\":\"7e597f9fdf228778dd04439df2a285971435d7a6\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778862517387,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39a0ffeX2wiAJx0ZaPdZq\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2c77e961001lRSs9u4Mr5gNYL\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2c70c8b2001wLwmXTY0GF55Er\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39a0ffeX2wiAJx0ZaPdZq\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Checking prior predictor attempts and bench lessons before drafting the hypothesis.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778862516577,\"end\":1778862517383},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0b7dd64764029257016a0749b479988197beac8348257c58b3\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778862517494,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39a0ffeX2wiAJx0ZaPdZq\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_w8QmqbIUsbNEPlhxoSZ1zFpw\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"category[\\\"': ]+predictor|predictor|branch folding|loop backedge|taken-target|BTFNT|replay cache\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 8 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 4: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 8, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire an ID-stage prediction path i... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778862517524,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39a0ffeX2wiAJx0ZaPdZq\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_nvYFKW5OSmQaOtR2hHdJktAf\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":250},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.23%): Pulling DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the one-cycle EX ALU and handling them with a stall-on-use iterative unit can buy large Fmax gains because CoreMark's hot loop is dominated by MUL, load/store, and branch traffic, so rare divide stalls cost less than keeping a 32-bit divider on the common critical path.\\n2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, -14.32%): On this core's combinational IF/ID path, adding ID-stage BTFNT and always-taken JAL prediction pulled decode, immediate-target add, and next-PC select onto the fetch critical path, and the resulting Fmax loss outweighed any CoreMark loop-branch bubble savings.\\n3: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r2s0 (regression, +5.57%): After DIV/REM already moved to `rtl/div_unit.sv`, splitting `alu_op` into hot/cold classes and replacing one flat ALU result `case` with separate `hot_result`/`m_result` muxes plus an `op[4]` final select regressed, suggesting bench's real EX critical path is elsewhere and extra class-select structure can cost more Fmax than it saves.\\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (improvement, +10.45%): Backend-only buffering of aligned normal-RAM stores is a good lever on this RTL because CoreMark issues enough stack/list/matrix/state stores that turning `io_dmemReady=0` on STOREs from a whole-pipeline freeze into a one-deep deferred write raises IPC, as long as younger memory ops and end-visible markers stay fenced behind the pending slot... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778862518139,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d38f39a0ffeX2wiAJx0ZaPdZq\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2c77ef71001jTJSmoyG6jotgU\",\"reason