output\":76,\"reasoning\":24,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":70144}},\"cost\":0}}\n36: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778872767077,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d145264001IWW8ozmH0O7VN4\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d144ee7001MwiCFzx0p1O3GF\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"snapshot\":\"7bd3b6ba7b2b03399fa115816285708a3d623c16\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n37: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778872786646,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d149eca001t60e34rSYPgP1A\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d144ee7001MwiCFzx0p1O3GF\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Writing the hypothesis YAML now.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778872786634,\"end\":1778872786646},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_07b45622d717f707016a0771d28690819ab705e583b931174e\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n38: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778872801570,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"apply_patch\",\"callID\":\"call_4P1CuC1cFQ7mIgMnviJ5rjRF\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"patchText\":\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r10s2.yaml\\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r10s2\\n+title: \\\"Single-Slot JAL and Backedge Fold Buffer\\\"\\n+category: predictor\\n+motivation: |\\n+  Every `bench` predictor that changed the live fetch `pc -> next_pc` path\\n+  regressed, but the one-slot backedge fold buffer was effectively timing\\n+  neutral at 447.40 fitness. That points to a narrow remaining predictor\\n+  window: recover taken-control bubbles by injecting already-cached target\\n+  instructions, not by adding another frontend target mux, tag lookup, or\\n+  decode-armed redirect.\\n+\\n+  CoreMark still spends cycles on both hot loop backedges and repeated direct\\n+  calls. The prior fold buffer only covered backward conditional branches, so\\n+  it left all direct `JAL` bubbles on the table even though `JAL` is perfectly\\n+  predictable and should not suffer loop-exit misses.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Introduce a one-slot control-flow fold buffer that trains on two low-entropy\\n+  classes only: taken backward conditional branches and direct `JAL`. The slot\\n+  records the control PC, resolved target PC, and the first target instruction\\n+  once that target is fetched architecturally. On a later hit, `if_stage`\\n+  leaves `io_imemAddr` on the normal sequential path but tags the control\\n+  instruction so the following cycle can inject the cached target instruction\\n+  into IF/ID instead of a bubble or fallthrough word.\\n+\\n+  EX remains the architectural source of truth. A correct folded hit repairs\\n+  the fetch PC to `target + 4`, while loop-exit misses, stale slots, and any\\n+  non-covered control flow fall back to the current flush-a... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n39: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778872801635,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d14d96100142g6IiyZOD428v\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"7bd3b6ba7b2b03399fa115816285708a3d623c16\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d144ee7001MwiCFzx0p1O3GF\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":73488,\"input\":448,\"output\":905,\"reasoning\":967,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":71168}},\"cost\":0}}\n40: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778872802642,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d14dd50001zE2V9E7ZS68S3f\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d14d992001ezX9ahgl4VJxte\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"snapshot\":\"7bd3b6ba7b2b03399fa115816285708a3d623c16\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n41: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778872805015,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d14e674001Z