4a9d4fafd016a0771e97ec4819892d989d89d756a0d\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}}}}\n46: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778872809984,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d14fa00001A4LdcipEtm1qwr\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"7bd3b6ba7b2b03399fa115816285708a3d623c16\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d14e950001UIIrMTGy5U1ZDu\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":74698,\"input\":1346,\"output\":78,\"reasoning\":58,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":73216}},\"cost\":0}}\n\n(End of file - total 46 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778872605562,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d11db79001HAJz4W4T500aey\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d11d71d001RVhp73FqMlEaz1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"snapshot\":\"7bd3b6ba7b2b03399fa115816285708a3d623c16\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778872620500,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d1214f3001ZM1yS0PRnrWj90\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d11d71d001RVhp73FqMlEaz1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Checking prior `bench` predictor experiments first so the hypothesis stays inside the negative lessons already learned.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778872620275,\"end\":1778872620499},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_073f20e474d88943016a07712c2b98819a844c4a3d33d890ea\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778872620531,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_YIh2yvBttlsrNWfskRx91roy\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":250},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.23%): Pulling DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the one-cycle EX ALU and handling them with a stall-on-use iterative unit can buy large Fmax gains because CoreMark's hot loop is dominated by MUL, load/store, and branch traffic, so rare divide stalls cost less than keeping a 32-bit divider on the common critical path.\\n2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, -14.32%): On this core's combinational IF/ID path, adding ID-stage BTFNT and always-taken JAL prediction pulled decode, immediate-target add, and next-PC select onto the fetch critical path, and the resulting Fmax loss outweighed any CoreMark loop-branch bubble savings.\\n3: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r2s0 (regression, +5.57%): After DIV/REM already moved to `rtl/div_unit.sv`, splitting `alu_op` into hot/cold classes and replacing one flat ALU result `case` with separate `hot_result`/`m_result` muxes plus an `op[4]` final select regressed, suggesting bench's real EX critical path is elsewhere and extra class-select structure can cost more Fmax than it saves.\\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (improvement, +10.45%): Backend-only buffering of aligned normal-RAM stores is a good lever on this RTL because CoreMark issues enough stack/list/matrix/state stores that turning `io_dmemReady=0` on STOREs from a whole-pipeline freeze into a one-deep deferred write raises IPC, as long as younger memory ops and end-visible markers stay fenced behind the pending slot... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778872620546,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_QigpccKvIzMYNXd4aiwXqfUH\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"predict|backedge|loop|btfnt|btb|stream|fetch queue|taken-target\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 17 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 2: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Iterative Cold Divider Off EX Path\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address generation, branch support, and\\\\nMUL. On a Tang Nano 20K, a full 32-bit divider is a strong candidate for\\\\nthe universal EX-stage critical path, yet CoreMark's timed loop is mostly\\\\nmultiply, load/store, and branch traffic and should pay little or no steady\\\\nstate penalty from slower divide instructions.\\\\n\\\\nThis makes divider extraction the highest-leverage micro-opt still missing\\\\nfrom the frozen bench fixture: it targets Fmax directly while preserving the\\\\nhot one-cycle behavior for the instructions that dominate CoreMark.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address generation, branch support, and\\\\nMUL. On a Tang Nano 20K, a full 32-bit divider is a strong candidate for\\\\nthe universal EX-stage critical path, yet CoreMark's timed loop is mostly\\\\nmultiply, load/store, and branch traffic and should pay little or no steady\\\\nstate penalty from slower divide instructions.\\\\n\\\\nThis makes divider extraction the highest-leverage micro-opt still missing\\\\nfrom the frozen bench fixture: it targets Fmax directly while preserving the\\\\nhot one-cycle behavior for th... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778872620623,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d12164d001w9BVwwO6XFy52w\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"7bd3b6ba7b2b03399fa115816285708a3d623c16\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d11d71d001RVhp73FqMlEaz1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":42361,\"input\":41667,\"output\":191,\"reasoning\":503,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778872621806,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d121aed001fEoS3L2PQ6IE3d\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d121685001hdcMtC3IKmhLe3\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"snapshot\":\"7bd3b6ba7b2b03399fa115816285708a3d623c16\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778872641416,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d1259da001HZNyXWljvo52ug\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d121685001hdcMtC3IKmhLe3\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Looking up the later `predictor` outcomes now; the branch-folding variants are the closest prior art to any remaining predictor idea.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778872637914,\"end\":1778872641414},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_02a6264dc2709701016a07713dcc7c819a9f8452d57272cd80\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778872641471,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_CFwvoRUd906y93WOoWGL9bPM\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"hyp-20260515-003-r5s2|hyp-20260515-003-r6s2|hyp-20260515-003-r9s2|hyp-20260515-003-r4s2|hyp-20260515-003-r3s2|hyp-20260515-003-r8s2|hyp-20260515-003-r2s2|hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 8 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 4: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 8, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778872641512,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_9WcTL0nXk9M7N8MpK4ag2crO\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"\\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\".*\\\"outcome\\\":|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-003-r5s2\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-003-r6s2\\\"\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 9 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 4: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 8, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire an ID-stage pred... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778872641623,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d126855001gxrtoc4vDjBx58\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"7bd3b6ba7b2b03399fa115816285708a3d623c16\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d121685001hdcMtC3IKmhLe3\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2ee2971ffex1LvOdi7zqPOdc\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":52899,\"input\":10382,\"o