{"type":"text","timestamp":1778877942659,"sessionID":"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut","part":{"id":"prt_e2d634889001ZhlyQ2tG8nFG5N","messageID":"msg_e2d62825a001zP2Wahke79beGg","sessionID":"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut","type":"text","text":"Writing the hypothesis YAML in `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/` with a backedge-only fold-buffer refinement that keeps the live fetch path sequential and uses accepted fetch history to seed the cached target instruction sooner.","time":{"start":1778877941897,"end":1778877942656},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0fa27143a9a211a9016a0785f5c390819aa89bdec502c8c9b3","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778877956978,"sessionID":"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_p3LPpg3GNwmEDiK5YbR9k7bu","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r13s2\n+title: \"Accepted-History Backedge Fold Slot\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Predictor work on `bench` has almost no safe frontend budget: ID redirects,\n+  BTB-style target lookup, and loop streaming all lost more Fmax than they\n+  gained IPC. The only predictor shape that stayed competitive was the\n+  one-slot backedge fold buffer because it kept `io_imemAddr` on the existing\n+  sequential path. Its remaining weakness is fill latency: the slot only\n+  becomes useful after the target instruction is fetched again\n+  architecturally, so the first observed taken backedge and any iStall-delayed\n+  refill still pay full bubbles.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Keep the single active backedge fold slot and the sequential `io_imemAddr`\n+  path, but train the slot from a tiny recent accepted-fetch history instead\n+  of waiting for a post-redirect refetch of the target word. When EX resolves\n+  a taken backward branch, search the last few architecturally accepted\n+  `(pc, instr)` pairs; if the target PC is present, snapshot that real\n+  instruction immediately into the fold slot and mark it usable for the next\n+  loop iteration. Fall back to the old delayed fill only on a history miss.\n+\n+  This stays inside the only predictor shape that has been timing-safe on\n+  `bench`: one lookup entry in IF, no extra target mux on the live fetch cone,\n+  and no multi-entry select logic. It directly attacks the remaining warm-up\n+  and refill misses for CoreMark's tight backedges while avoiding the unsafe\n+  \"injected side value with no accepted backing entry\" behavior called out by\n+  the last broken fold experiment.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add fold-prediction sideband fields and a compact recent-fetch history record type for a single-slot backedge fold predictor.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Keep the sequential PC path, record a tiny history of architecturally accepted fetch `(pc, instr)` pairs, and expose the active fold slot plus history data for training.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch fold-hit metadata alongside the instruction so EX can validate or repair folded backedge predictions without re-decoding predictor state.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Train taken backward branches from the accepted-fetch history, fall back to delayed fill on history miss, and keep EX as the architectural source of truth for redirect and trap behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the recent-fetch-history and fold-training signals between IF and EX while preserving the existing RVFI and bus contracts.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add regression tests for repeated taken backedges, history-seeded fold fill, and stall/flush interactions so no wrong-path retirement leaks through prediction.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r13s2\n+title: \"Accepted-History Backedge Fold Slot\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Predictor work on `bench` has almost no safe frontend budget: ID redirects,\n+  BTB-style target lookup, and loop streaming all lost more Fmax than they\n+  gained IPC. The only predictor shape that stayed competitive was the\n+  one-slot backedge fold buffer because it kept `io_imemAddr` on the existing\n+  sequential path. Its remaining weakness is fill latency: the slot only\n+  becomes useful after the target instruction is fetched again\n+  architecturally, so the first observed taken backedge and any iStall-delayed\n+  refill still pay full bubbles.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Keep the single active backedge fold slot and the sequential `io_imemAddr`\n+  path, but train the slot from a tiny recent accepted-fetch history instead\n+  of waiting for a post-redirect refetch of the target word. When EX resolves\n+  a taken backward branch, search the last few architecturally accepted\n+  `(pc, instr)` pairs; if the target PC is present, snapshot that real\n+  instruction immediately into the fold slot and mark it usable for the next\n+  loop iteration. Fall back to the old delayed fill only on a history miss.\n+\n+  This stays inside the only predictor shape that has been timing-safe on\n+  `bench`: one lookup entry in IF, no extra target mux on the live fetch cone,\n+  and no multi-entry select logic. It directly attacks the remaining warm-up\n+  and refill misses for CoreMark's tight backedges while avoiding the unsafe\n+  \"injected side value with no accepted backing entry\" behavior called out by\n+  the last broken fold experiment.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add fold-prediction sideband fields and a compact recent-fetch history record type for a single-slot backedge fold predictor.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Keep the sequential PC path, record a tiny history of architecturally accepted fetch `(pc, instr)` pairs, and expose the active fold slot plus history data for training.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch fold-hit metadata alongside the instruction so EX can validate or repair folded backedge predictions without re-decoding predictor state.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Train taken backward branches from the accepted-fetch history, fall back to delayed fill on history miss, and keep EX as the architectural source of truth for redirect and trap behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the recent-fetch-history and fold-training signals between IF and EX while preserving the existing RVFI and bus contracts.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add regression tests for repeated taken backedges, history-seeded fold fill, and stall/flush interactions so no wrong-path retirement leaks through prediction.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r13s2\n+title: \"Accepted-History Backedge Fold Slot\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Predictor work on `bench` has almost no safe frontend budget: ID redirects,\n+  BTB-style target lookup, and loop streaming all lost more Fmax than they\n+  gained IPC. The only predictor shape that stayed competitive was the\n+  one-slot backedge fold buffer because it kept `io_imemAddr` on the existing\n+  sequential path. Its remaining weakness is fill latency: the slot only\n+  becomes useful after the target instruction is fetched again\n+  architecturally, so the first observed taken backedge and any iStall-delayed\n+  refill still pay full bubbles.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Keep the single active backedge fold slot and the sequential `io_imemAddr`\n+  path, but train the slot from a tiny recent accepted-fetch history instead\n+  of waiting for a post-redirect refetch of the target word. When EX resolves\n+  a taken backward branch, search the last few architecturally accepted\n+  `(pc, instr)` pairs; if the target PC is present, snapshot that real\n+  instruction immediately into the fold slot and mark it usable for the next\n+  loop iteration. Fall back to the old delayed fill only on a history miss.\n+\n+  This stays inside the only predictor shape that has been timing-safe on\n+  `bench`: one lookup entry in IF, no extra target mux on the live fetch cone,\n+  and no multi-entry select logic. It directly attacks the remaining warm-up\n+  and refill misses for CoreMark's tight backedges while avoiding the unsafe\n+  \"injected side value with no accepted backing entry\" behavior called out by\n+  the last broken fold experiment.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add fold-prediction sideband fields and a compact recent-fetch history record type for a single-slot backedge fold predictor.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Keep the sequential PC path, record a tiny history of architecturally accepted fetch `(pc, instr)` pairs, and expose the active fold slot plus history data for training.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch fold-hit metadata alongside the instruction so EX can validate or repair folded backedge predictions without re-decoding predictor state.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Train taken backward branches from the accepted-fetch history, fall back to delayed fill on history miss, and keep EX as the architectural source of truth for redirect and trap behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the recent-fetch-history and fold-training signals between IF and EX while preserving the existing RVFI and bus contracts.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add regression tests for repeated taken backedges, history-seeded fold fill, and stall/flush interactions so no wrong-path retirement leaks through prediction.\"\n","additions":43,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778877956971,"end":1778877956977}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0fa27143a9a211a9016a0785f6762c819a801f166dba378cd3"}},"id":"prt_e2d634b83001kX5Znybz56IIE7","sessionID":"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut","messageID":"msg_e2d62825a001zP2Wahke79beGg"}}
