ite\":0,\"read\":76288}},\"cost\":0}}\n30: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778876236108,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d49414a001T3QdyQviic5OaG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d492b250017TfTjliOKzb4pp\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n31: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876262630,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"apply_patch\",\"callID\":\"call_KKgqgm307VedS6umDCMwTDZ8\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"patchText\":\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r12s2.yaml\\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r12s2\\n+title: \\\"Champion-Challenger Backedge Fold Buffer\\\"\\n+category: predictor\\n+motivation: |\\n+  The predictor history on `bench` is unusually narrow: almost every branch or\\n+  fetch predictor that added lookup, redirect, or target-selection work to the\\n+  live frontend path regressed badly, but the single-slot backedge fold buffer\\n+  matched the current best fitness exactly. That strongly suggests there is\\n+  still predictor headroom, but only inside the same timing-safe fold-and-\\n+  inject shape that leaves `io_imemAddr` on the existing sequential path.\\n+\\n+  The likely remaining loss is one-slot thrash. CoreMark rotates among several\\n+  hot counted loops, so a single fold slot can keep relearning a different\\n+  backedge and give away otherwise-predictable taken-branch bubbles.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Keep the fetch-time predictor lookup exactly one entry wide, but add a small\\n+  off-path challenger slot and repeat counter that are updated only from EX.\\n+  The active fold slot remains the only structure consulted in IF: same one tag\\n+  compare, same cached target instruction injection, same sequential\\n+  `io_imemAddr` path, and no new multi-entry select logic on the live fetch\\n+  cone.\\n+\\n+  When EX resolves a taken backward branch that does not match the active slot,\\n+  train it first into the challenger. Only if that challenger repeats does it\\n+  get promoted into the active fold slot. This attacks the likely one-slot\\n+  aliasing problem across CoreMark's list, matrix, and state loops without\\n+  repeating the two-entry fetch-l... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n32: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778876262790,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d49a984001d0hZahxzilMQGt\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d492b250017TfTjliOKzb4pp\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":94770,\"input\":1454,\"output\":775,\"reasoning\":381,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":92160}},\"cost\":0}}\n33: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778876264259,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d49af42001wK6sEuNC81eic3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d49a9d2001gSxKHPTDUXvLEV\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n34: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876267628,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_kt92oZ63MRjbXpBfwATWfrBq\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r12s2.yaml\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":200},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r12s2.yaml</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: id: hyp-20260515-003-r12s2\\n2: title: \\\"Champion-Challenger Backedge Fold Buffer\\\"\\n3: category: predictor\\n4: motivation: |\\n5:   The predictor history on `bench` is unusually narrow: almost every branch or\\n6:   fetch predictor that added lookup, redirect, or target-selection work to the\\n7:   live frontend path regressed badly, but the single-slot backedge fold buffer\\n8:   matched the current best fitness exactly. That strongly suggests there is\\n9:   still predictor headroom, but only inside the same timing-safe fold-and-\\n10:   inject shape that leaves `io_imemAddr` on the existing sequential path.\\n11: \\n12:   The likely remaining loss is one-slot thrash. CoreMark rotates among several\\n13:   hot counted loops, so a single fold slot can keep relearning a different\\n14:   backedge and give away otherwise-predictable taken-branch bubbles.\\n15: hypothesis: |\\n16:   Keep the fetch-time predictor lookup exactly one entry wide, but add a small\\n17:   off-path challenger slot and repeat counter that are updated only from EX.\\n18:   The active fold slot remains the only structure consulted in IF: same one tag\\n19:   compare, same cached target instruction injection, same sequential\\n20:   `io_imemAddr` path, and no new multi-entry select logic on the live fetch\\n21:   cone.\\n22: \\n23:   When EX resolves a taken backward branch that does not match the active slot,\\n24:   train it first int... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n35: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778876267861,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d49bd54001IJBAFvLEdhuDQi\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d49a9d2001gSxKHPTDUXvLEV\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":94907,\"input\":1628,\"output\":83,\"reasoning\":12,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":93184}},\"cost\":0}}\n36: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778876268928,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d49c17f001LS7DHlYVYybWZx\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d49bd80001FpuhL900ranOsC\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n37: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778876279933,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d49eac90011fXrlX5AUlHv8P\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d49bd80001FpuhL900ranOsC\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Wrote `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r12s2.yaml`.\\n\\nThe hypothesis is a `predictor` proposal: keep the fetch-time path at the timing-safe one-slot backedge fold lookup that already matched best fitness, and move extra intelligence into EX-time training with a shadow challenger slot plus promotion-on-repeat to reduce one-slot loop thrash without adding a two-entry fetch lookup.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778876279497,\"end\":1778876279932},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0b91c7c3a1135fcc016a077f7763e4819b8bf96dd056761347\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}}}}\n38: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778876280057,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d49ecf8001IaHY7KxWcfc677\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d49bd80001FpuhL900ranOsC\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":96148,\"input\":987,\"output\":96,\"reasoning\":345,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":94720}},\"cost\":0}}\n\n(End of file - total 38 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778876075389,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d46cd7c001zj4Hm1nFNdeEru\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d46c891001YeHATfYeXMf0Fz\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778876090242,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d4705eb0029PMifSGBiGRcUj\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d46c891001YeHATfYeXMf0Fz\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Reviewing prior predictor attempts and the current `bench` fetch/redirect structure first, then I’ll write a single-slot predictor hypothesis file scoped to `cores/bench/`.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778876089835,\"end\":1778876090242},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0d12a084aeda7da2016a077eb9bb10819aa8d2303c7380d411\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876090275,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_V8wuzkMf88oslqdXADZK4NMm\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":400},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.23%): Pulling DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the one-cycle EX ALU and handling them with a stall-on-use iterative unit can buy large Fmax gains because CoreMark's hot loop is dominated by MUL, load/store, and branch traffic, so rare divide stalls cost less than keeping a 32-bit divider on the common critical path.\\n2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, -14.32%): On this core's combinational IF/ID path, adding ID-stage BTFNT and always-taken JAL prediction pulled decode, immediate-target add, and next-PC select onto the fetch critical path, and the resulting Fmax loss outweighed any CoreMark loop-branch bubble savings.\\n3: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r2s0 (regression, +5.57%): After DIV/REM already moved to `rtl/div_unit.sv`, splitting `alu_op` into hot/cold classes and replacing one flat ALU result `case` with separate `hot_result`/`m_result` muxes plus an `op[4]` final select regressed, suggesting bench's real EX critical path is elsewhere and extra class-select structure can cost more Fmax than it saves.\\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (improvement, +10.45%): Backend-only buffering of aligned normal-RAM stores is a good lever on this RTL because CoreMark issues enough stack/list/matrix/state stores that turning `io_dmemReady=0` on STOREs from a whole-pipeline freeze into a one-deep deferred write raises IPC, as long as younger memory ops and end-visible markers stay fenced behind the pending slot... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876090283,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_AY9pCv5p0MOFTYEJnqrbuvlR\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"(?i)predict|btfnt|backedge|loop|jalr|ras|return|btb|branch\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 28 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 2: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Iterative Cold Divider Off EX Path\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address generation, branch support, and\\\\nMUL. On a Tang Nano 20K, a full 32-bit divider is a strong candidate for\\\\nthe universal EX-stage critical path, yet CoreMark's timed loop is mostly\\\\nmultiply, load/store, and branch traffic and should pay little or no steady\\\\nstate penalty from slower divide instructions.\\\\n\\\\nThis makes divider extracti