ritical path, yet CoreMark's timed loop is mostly\\\\nmultiply, load/store, and branch traffic and should pay little or no steady\\\\nstate penalty from slower divide instructions.\\\\n\\\\nThis makes divider extraction the highest-leverage micro-opt still missing\\\\nfrom the frozen bench fixture: it targets Fmax directly while preserving the\\\\nhot one-cycle behavior for the instructions that dominate CoreMark.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The frozen bench core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\\\ncombinational ALU path as ADD, address gen... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778876104684,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d473feb0016C819aPWaCFoP4\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d470824001hViLmYWg1ar31X\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":58706,\"input\":16186,\"output\":103,\"reasoning\":433,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":41984}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778876105928,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d4744c60011LVPCYMZBjzx1k\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d47400e002SPZIwJ84YjQPli\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778876108056,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_YvqmjnFMShVSmxUozEywnbj5\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\",\"offset\":29,\"limit\":20},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n29: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r10s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Canonical Decode Source Operands\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current load-use interlock keys off raw IF/ID bitfields, not the\\\\noperands a legal instruction will actually consume. That means single-source\\\\nor zero-source instructions can still alias an older load's `rd` through\\\\nunused immediate bits and burn a bubble. The `r4s0` failure showed why a\\\\ndirect hazard rewrite was unsafe: `bench` currently carries those raw source\\\\nfields into RVFI, so any safe relaxation has to start by canonicalizing the\\\\narchitectural source view.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current load-use interlock keys off raw IF/ID bitfields, not the\\\\noperands a legal instruction will actually consume. That means single-source\\\\nor zero-source instructions can still alias an older load's `rd` through\\\\nunused immediate bits and burn a bubble. The `r4s0` failure showed why a\\\\ndirect hazard rewrite was unsafe: `bench` currently carries those raw source\\\\nfields into RVFI, so any safe relaxation has to start by canonicalizing the\\\\narchitectural source view.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Teach decode which source operands are architecturally live for each\\\\nvalidated opcode/funct form, and canonicalize unused sources to `x0` before\\\\nthe regfile, hazard unit, and RVFI pipeline state ever see them. In\\\\npractice, OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, and EBREAK would stop\\\\nadve... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778876108177,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d474d90001TqiUwJErph6jpz\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"ab029c21c7961d7e2fcf0ec21f7ee2c2fc867074\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d47400e002SPZIwJ84YjQPli\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d2b93825ffeZHZpLmPPs3FrVQ\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\"