{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778879472904,"sessionID":"ses_1d2863275ffecU7AoS7MPyx9nI","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_l2UGZfUoM1jFDdjt6L4UYUsw","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.log","offset":1,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.log</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778877788766,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d60f25d001W4MLj38oacAMC3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d60edb6001WpF0soSOU2J5X7\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9014816a9bd5a694f41ab8505373ab685\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n2: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778877800204,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_sju8WuJZsLERUYJ0AVf7ASs0\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":400},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.23%): Pulling DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the one-cycle EX ALU and handling them with a stall-on-use iterative unit can buy large Fmax gains because CoreMark's hot loop is dominated by MUL, load/store, and branch traffic, so rare divide stalls cost less than keeping a 32-bit divider on the common critical path.\\n2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, -14.32%): On this core's combinational IF/ID path, adding ID-stage BTFNT and always-taken JAL prediction pulled decode, immediate-target add, and next-PC select onto the fetch critical path, and the resulting Fmax loss outweighed any CoreMark loop-branch bubble savings.\\n3: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r2s0 (regression, +5.57%): After DIV/REM already moved to `rtl/div_unit.sv`, splitting `alu_op` into hot/cold classes and replacing one flat ALU result `case` with separate `hot_result`/`m_result` muxes plus an `op[4]` final select regressed, suggesting bench's real EX critical path is elsewhere and extra class-select structure can cost more Fmax than it saves.\\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (improvement, +10.45%): Backend-only buffering of aligned normal-RAM stores is a good lever on this RTL because CoreMark issues enough stack/list/matrix/state stores that turning `io_dmemReady=0` on STOREs from a whole-pipeline freeze into a one-deep deferred write raises IPC, as long as younger memory ops and end-visible markers stay fenced behind the pending slot... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778877800218,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_bHNTZydXZQIHcr2lAOlpaL6u\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\"|backedge|predict|fold|loop buffer|stream\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 21 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 4: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 8, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire an ID-stage prediction path into IF and r... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n4: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778877800319,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d611f7e001JMNEatIxPgkv2x\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9014816a9bd5a694f41ab8505373ab685\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d60edb6001WpF0soSOU2J5X7\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":43111,\"input\":32780,\"output\":173,\"reasoning\":430,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":9728}},\"cost\":0}}\n5: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778877801500,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d61241b001Ax4WjdRciuH8Sz\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d611fb3001XwdEf7v5Cd92Bo\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9