ef _r(funct7, rs2, rs1, funct3, rd, opcode):\\n20:     return ((funct7 & 0x7F) << 25) | ((rs2 & 0x1F) << 20) | ((rs1 & 0x1F) << 15) \\\\\\n21:          | ((funct3 & 0x7) << 12) | ((rd & 0x1F) << 7) | (opcode & 0x7F)\\n22: \\n23: \\n24: def _i(imm, rs1, funct3, rd, opcode):\\n25:     return ((imm & 0xFFF) << 20) | ((rs1 & 0x1F) << 15) | ((funct3 & 0x7) << 12) \\\\\\n26:          | ((rd & 0x1F) << 7) | (opcode & 0x7F)\\n27: \\n28: \\n29: def _s(imm, rs2, rs1, funct3, opcode):\\n30:     imm_hi = (imm >> 5) & 0x7F\\n31:     imm_lo = imm & 0x1F\\n32:     return (imm_hi << 25) | ((rs2 & 0x1F) << 20) | ((rs1 & 0x1F) << 15) \\\\\\n33:          | ((funct3 & 0x7) << 12) | (imm_lo << 7) | (opcode & 0x7F)\\n34: \\n35: \\n36: def _b(imm, rs2, rs1, funct3, opcode):\\n37:     # imm is a 13-bit signed numb... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n27: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778877891120,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d62822f0012BzW0LrL8kNeRK\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9014816a9bd5a694f41ab8505373ab685\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d627280001DlyvM1vupTIYUW\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":79775,\"input\":2378,\"output\":67,\"reasoning\":18,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":77312}},\"cost\":0}}\n28: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778877892404,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d628733001p8C3GO5OLab5v6\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d62825a001zP2Wahke79beGg\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9014816a9bd5a694f41ab8505373ab685\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n29: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778877942659,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d634889001ZhlyQ2tG8nFG5N\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d62825a001zP2Wahke79beGg\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Writing the hypothesis YAML in `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/` with a backedge-only fold-buffer refinement that keeps the live fetch path sequential and uses accepted fetch history to seed the cached target instruction sooner.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778877941897,\"end\":1778877942656},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0fa27143a9a211a9016a0785f5c390819aa89bdec502c8c9b3\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n30: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778877956978,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"apply_patch\",\"callID\":\"call_p3LPpg3GNwmEDiK5YbR9k7bu\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"patchText\":\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml\\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r13s2\\n+title: \\\"Accepted-History Backedge Fold Slot\\\"\\n+category: predictor\\n+motivation: |\\n+  Predictor work on `bench` has almost no safe frontend budget: ID redirects,\\n+  BTB-style target lookup, and loop streaming all lost more Fmax than they\\n+  gained IPC. The only predictor shape that stayed competitive was the\\n+  one-slot backedge fold buffer because it kept `io_imemAddr` on the existing\\n+  sequential path. Its remaining weakness is fill latency: the slot only\\n+  becomes useful after the target instruction is fetched again\\n+  architecturally, so the first observed taken backedge and any iStall-delayed\\n+  refill still pay full bubbles.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Keep the single active backedge fold slot and the sequential `io_imemAddr`\\n+  path, but train the slot from a tiny recent accepted-fetch history instead\\n+  of waiting for a post-redirect refetch of the target word. When EX resolves\\n+  a taken backward branch, search the last few architecturally accepted\\n+  `(pc, instr)` pairs; if the target PC is present, snapshot that real\\n+  instruction immediately into the fold slot and mark it usable for the next\\n+  loop iteration. Fall back to the old delayed fill only on a history miss.\\n+\\n+  This stays inside the only predictor shape that has been timing-safe on\\n+  `bench`: one lookup entry in IF, no extra target mux on the live fetch cone,\\n+  and no multi-entry select logic. It directly attacks the remaining warm-up\\n+  and refill misses for CoreMark's tight backedges while avoiding the unsafe\\n+  \\\"injected side value with no accept... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n31: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778877957084,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d6383db001bLroQw5lba94uQ\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9014816a9bd5a694f41ab8505373ab685\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d62825a001zP2Wahke79beGg\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":88525,\"input\":5621,\"output\":849,\"reasoning\":2695,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":79360}},\"cost\":0}}\n32: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778877958261,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d638873001L27APoEFYJphQ4\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d6383ff001V0e5tLBnEj4TSy\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9014816a9bd5a694f41ab8505373ab685\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n33: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778877960639,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_do1vnEaLjX5xwOw1XadqMo0H\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":240},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: id: hyp-20260515-003-r13s2\\n2: title: \\\"Accepted-History Backedge Fold Slot\\\"\\n3: category: predictor\\n4: motivation: |\\n5:   Predictor work on `bench` has almost no safe frontend budget: ID redirects,\\n6:   BTB-style target lookup, and loop streaming all lost more Fmax than they\\n7:   gained IPC. The only predictor shape that stayed competitive was the\\n8:   one-slot backedge fold buffer because it kept `io_imemAddr` on the existing\\n9:   sequential path. Its remaining weakness is fill latency: the slot only\\n10:   becomes useful after the target instruction is fetched again\\n11:   architecturally, so the first observed taken backedge and any iStall-delayed\\n12:   refill still pay full bubbles.\\n13: hypothesis: |\\n14:   Keep the single active backedge fold slot and the sequential `io_imemAddr`\\n15:   path, but train the slot from a tiny recent accepted-fetch history instead\\n16:   of waiting for a post-redirect refetch of the target word. When EX resolves\\n17:   a taken backward branch, search the last few architecturally accepted\\n18:   `(pc, instr)` pairs; if the target PC is present, snapshot that real\\n19:   instruction immediately into the fold slot and mark it usable for the next\\n20:   loop iteration. Fall back to the old delayed fill only on a history miss.\\n21: \\n22:   This stays inside the only predictor shape that has been timing-safe on\\n23:   `bench`: one lookup entry in IF... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n34: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778877960779,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d63924a001qfGPhg8tRTCYw3\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9014816a9bd5a694f41ab8505373ab685\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d6383ff001V0e5tLBnEj4TSy\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":88664,\"input\":4087,\"output\":83,\"reasoning\":14,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":84480}},\"cost\":0}}\n35: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778877962099,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d63976f001WWl6MXejz2UqUd\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d639272001U993ldxmoOGs7V\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9014816a9bd5a694f41ab8505373ab685\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n36: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778877997793,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d6413c7001ptQ7Sp39lYbdHd\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d639272001U993ldxmoOGs7V\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Wrote `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.yaml`.\\n\\nHypothesis focus: keep the only timing-safe predictor shape seen so far on `bench` (single-slot backedge fold/inject), but improve it by seeding the cached target instruction from recent accepted fetch history instead of waiting for a later architectural refetch.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778877993927,\"end\":1778877997792},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0adf9a63b3b3a407016a078624c138819b8b8a01fce33c812f\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}}}}\n37: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778877998026,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d6423c90010GpE03efamKyEq\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9014816a9bd5a694f41ab8505373ab685\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d639272001U993ldxmoOGs7V\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":89621,\"input\":1420,\"output\":85,\"reasoning\":52,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":88064}},\"cost\":0}}\n\n(End of file - total 37 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778877788766,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2d60f25d001W4MLj38oacAMC3\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2d60edb6001WpF0soSOU2J5X7\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"snapshot\":\"245514b9014816a9bd5a694f41ab8505373ab685\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778877800204,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_sju8WuJZsLERUYJ0AVf7ASs0\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":400},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.23%): Pulling DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the one-cycle EX ALU and handling them with a stall-on-use iterative unit can buy large Fmax gains because CoreMark's hot loop is dominated by MUL, load/store, and branch traffic, so rare divide stalls cost less than keeping a 32-bit divider on the common critical path.\\n2: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, -14.32%): On this core's combinational IF/ID path, adding ID-stage BTFNT and always-taken JAL prediction pulled decode, immediate-target add, and next-PC select onto the fetch critical path, and the resulting Fmax loss outweighed any CoreMark loop-branch bubble savings.\\n3: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r2s0 (regression, +5.57%): After DIV/REM already moved to `rtl/div_unit.sv`, splitting `alu_op` into hot/cold classes and replacing one flat ALU result `case` with separate `hot_result`/`m_result` muxes plus an `op[4]` final select regressed, suggesting bench's real EX critical path is elsewhere and extra class-select structure can cost more Fmax than it saves.\\n4: - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (improvement, +10.45%): Backend-only buffering of aligned normal-RAM stores is a good lever on this RTL because CoreMark issues enough stack/list/matrix/state stores that turning `io_dmemReady=0` on STOREs from a whole-pipeline freeze into a one-deep deferred write raises IPC, as long as younger memory ops and end-visible markers stay fenced behind the pending slot... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778877800218,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d29f129effe6qj5AeaxhR0Fut\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_bHNTZydXZQIHcr2lAOlpaL6u\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\"|backedge|predict|fold|loop buffer|stream\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments\",\"include\":\"log.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 21 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 4: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expec