h, but add a tiny confidence counter and sticky replacement logic while preserving sequential `io_imemAddr` generation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify taken backward branches for training and emit saturating refresh/decay/replace updates instead of unconditionally overwriting the active fold slot.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the minimal fold-prediction sideband metadata needed to carry a folded-branch marker through the pipeline without changing the RVFI-visible architectural fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fold sideband through ID/EX so EX can distinguish predicted-folded branches from ordinary control flow when applying repair and training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the one-slot fold predictor update path between EX and IF while keeping the top-level memory and RVFI contract unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline tests that alternate hot and cold backedges to verify sticky replacement, correct redirect repair on loop exit, and strict RVFI PC/order behavior under stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep the single-slot fold/inject fetch path, but add a tiny confidence counter and sticky replacement logic while preserving sequential `io_imemAddr` generation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify taken backward branches for training and emit saturating refresh/decay/replace updates instead of unconditionally overwriting the active fold slot.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the minimal fold-prediction sideband metadata needed to carry a folded-branch marker through the pipeline without changing the RVFI-visible architectural fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fold sideband through ID/EX so EX can distinguish predicted-folded branches from ordinary control flow when applying repair and training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the one-slot fold predictor update path between EX and IF while keeping the top-level memory and RVFI contract unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline tests that alternate hot and cold backedges to verify sticky replacement, correct redirect repair on loop exit, and strict RVFI PC/order behavior under stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 179.15, \"delta_pct\": -59.96, \"vs_baseline\": -36.66, \"fmax_mhz\": 76.69, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4280712, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6165, \"ff\": 2424, \"seeds\": [76.69, 74.67, 77.3], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T21:53:06.206284Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r14s2 (regression, -59.96%): On `bench`, predictor headroom is not in smarter one-slot fold replacement either: keeping IF lookup one-entry wide but adding sticky `fold_slot_conf`/`fold_update_op` retention and `predicted_*` repair plumbing costs more Fmax than CoreMark recovers from reducing occasional backedge-slot thrash.\"}\n","metadata":{"output":"...\n\ns and direct `JAL`. The slot\\nrecords the control PC, resolved target PC, and the first target instruction\\nonce that target is fetched architecturally. On a later hit, `if_stage`\\nleaves `io_imemAddr` on the normal sequential path but tags the control\\ninstruction so the following cycle can inject the cached target instruction\\ninto IF/ID instead of a bubble or fallthrough word.\\n\\nEX remains the architectural source of truth. A correct folded hit repairs\\nthe fetch PC to `target + 4`, while loop-exit misses, stale slots, and any\\nnon-covered control flow fall back to the current flush-and-redirect path.\\nCompared with the prior backedge-only fold buffer, this adds very little new\\ntiming risk while broadening coverage to CoreMark's direct-call traffic,\\nwhich is the most plausible remaining predictor lever on this core.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add minimal fold metadata bits that travel with a predicted control instruction and its injected target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-slot control-flow fold entry keyed by control PC, cache the first target instruction after an architectural fetch, and inject it on later hits without changing the sequential `io_imemAddr` path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch fold-hit metadata with the control instruction so later stages can distinguish a normal redirect from a successful folded hit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the slot on taken backward branches and direct `JAL`, validate folded hits against the architectural next PC, and request `target + 4` repair only when the injected instruction was correct.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire fold-train, fold-hit, and repair signals across IF, ID, EX, and hazard control while preserving the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Refine flush behavior so a correct folded target survives branch resolution while stale or wrong folded injections are still killed.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add a pipeline test that warms the fold slot on repeated direct calls and taken backedges and checks RVFI-order-safe recovery on loop exit and stale-slot misses.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add minimal fold metadata bits that travel with a predicted control instruction and its injected target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-slot control-flow fold entry keyed by control PC, cache the first target instruction after an architectural fetch, and inject it on later hits without changing the sequential `io_imemAddr` path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch fold-hit metadata with the control instruction so later stages can distinguish a normal redirect from a successful folded hit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the slot on taken backward branches and direct `JAL`, validate folded hits against the architectural next PC, and request `target + 4` repair only when the injected instruction was correct.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire fold-train, fold-hit, and repair signals across IF, ID, EX, and hazard control while preserving the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Refine flush behavior so a correct folded target survives branch resolution while stale or wrong folded injections are still killed.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add a pipeline test that warms the fold slot on repeated direct calls and taken backedges and checks RVFI-order-safe recovery on loop exit and stale-slot misses.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 177.2, \"delta_pct\": -60.39, \"vs_baseline\": -37.35, \"fmax_mhz\": 74.78, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4220161, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6162, \"ff\": 2419, \"seeds\": [74.78, 75.15, 72.56], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T19:39:06.365345Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r10s2 (regression, -60.39%): On `bench`, even keeping `io_imemAddr` on the sequential path is not enough for fetch-side control folding, because carrying `fold_predicted`/`fold_target_pc` metadata, injecting cached target instructions into IF/ID, and adding EX/hazard repair control (`fold_match`, `redirect_flush`, `if_fold_inject`) costs more Fmax than CoreMark recovers from hiding direct-`JAL` and loop-backedge bubbles.\"}\n34:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r11s2\", \"title\": \"Two-Entry Backedge Fold Buffer\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The only predictor family that did not materially hurt `bench` was the\\nsingle-slot backedge fold buffer, which matched the current best fitness at\\n447.40 while keeping `io_imemAddr` on the existing sequential path. That\\nsuggests the remaining predictor headroom is not in more aggressive fetch\\nredirection, but in improving hit rate inside that same timing-safe\\nfold-and-inject shape.\\n\\nCoreMark rotates among several hot counted loops across the list, matrix,\\nand state kernels. A one-entry fold slot likely thrashes between those\\nbackedges and leaves repeatable taken-branch bubbles uncovered even though\\nthe underlying predictor mechanism appears Fmax-safe on this FPGA.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only predictor family that did not materially hurt `bench` was the\\nsingle-slot backedge fold buffer, which matched the current best fitness at\\n447.40 while keeping `io_imemAddr` on the existing sequential path. That\\nsuggests the remaining predictor headroom is not in more aggressive fetch\\nredirection, but in improving hit rate inside that same timing-safe\\nfold-and-inject shape.\\n\\nCoreMark rotates among several hot counted loops across the list, matrix,\\nand state kernels. A one-entry fold slot likely thrashes between those\\nbackedges and leaves repeatable taken-branch bubbles uncovered even though\\nthe underlying predictor mechanism appears Fmax-safe on this FPGA.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the one-slot backedge fold idea with a two-entry backedge-only fold\\nbuffer trained from EX. Each entry records a taken backward branch PC, its\\nresolved target PC, and the first target instruction once that target is\\nfetched architecturally. On a later hit, `if_stage` still keeps\\n`io_imemAddr` on the normal sequential path, but tags the in-flight branch\\nso the following cycle can inject the cached target instruction into IF/ID\\nand repair the fetch PC to `target + 4` only after the folded target has\\nentered the pipe.\\n\\nKeep the scope deliberately narrow: only taken backward conditional\\nbranches, no `JAL`, no `JALR`, no taken-target mux in the live fetch path,\\nand no multi-instruction stream mode. Compared with the timing-neutral\\none-entry fold buffer, the extra capacity should reduce aliasing across\\nCoreMark's hot loops while preserving the one predictor shape that has not\\nalready cost Fmax on this core.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the minimal fold-prediction metadata needed to carry a folded backedge through IF/ID and ID/EX to EX repair logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a two-entry backedge fold buffer that injects a cached target instruction on a branch-PC hit while leaving `io_imemAddr` on the existing sequential path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fold metadata alongside the branch so EX can distinguish folded hits from normal control flow without re-decoding predictor state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the two fold entries from resolved taken backward branches and generate the repair behavior for loop-exit or stale-entry misses.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire fold-buffer train, inject, and repair signals between IF and EX without changing the top-level IO contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline tests for repeated backedge fold hits, loop-exit recovery, and coexistence with random `io_imemReady` stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the minimal fold-prediction metadata needed to carry a folded backedge through IF/ID and ID/EX to EX repair logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a two-entry backedge fold buffer that injects a cached target instruction on a branch-PC hit while leaving `io_imemAddr` on the existing sequential path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fold metadata alongside the branch so EX can distinguish folded hits from normal control flow without re-decoding predictor state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the two fold entries from resolved taken backward branches and generate the repair behavior for loop-exit or stale-entry misses.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire fold-buffer train, inject, and repair signals between IF and EX without changing the top-level IO contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline tests for repeated backedge fold hits, loop-exit recovery, and coexistence with random `io_imemReady` stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 298.47, \"delta_pct\": -33.29, \"vs_baseline\": 5.53, \"fmax_mhz\": 125.17, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4193716, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6599, \"ff\": 2548, \"seeds\": [125.17, 118.22, 134.34], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T20:10:45.589148Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r11s2 (regression, -33.29%): On `bench`, predictor headroom is not in larger sequential-path fold buffers: a second backedge entry adds `if_stage` entry-select/target-instruction state and `fold_injecting`/EX repair plumbing, and that control cost outweighs the hit-rate gain from reducing CoreMark loop aliasing.\"}\n37:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r12s2\", \"title\": \"Champion-Challenger Backedge Fold Buffer\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The predictor history on `bench` is unusually narrow: almost every branch or\\nfetch predictor that added lookup, redirect, or target-selection work to the\\nlive frontend path regressed badly, but the single-slot backedge fold buffer\\nmatched the current best fitness exactly. That strongly suggests there is\\nstill predictor headroom, but only inside the same timing-safe fold-and-\\ninject shape that leaves `io_imemAddr` on the existing sequential path.\\n\\nThe likely remaining loss is one-slot thrash. CoreMark rotates among several\\nhot counted loops, so a single fold slot can keep relearning a different\\nbackedge and give away otherwise-predictable taken-branch bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The predictor history on `bench` is unusually narrow: almost every branch or\\nfetch predictor that added lookup, redirect, or target-selection work to the\\nlive frontend path regressed badly, but the single-slot backedge fold buffer\\nmatched the current best fitness exactly. That strongly suggests there is\\nstill predictor headroom, but only inside the same timing-safe fold-and-\\ninject shape that leaves `io_imemAddr` on the existing sequential path.\\n\\nThe likely remaining loss is one-slot thrash. CoreMark rotates among several\\nhot counted loops, so a single fold slot can keep relearning a different\\nbackedge and give away otherwise-predictable taken-branch bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the fetch-time predictor lookup exactly one entry wide, but add a small\\noff-path challenger slot and repeat counter that are updated only from EX.\\nThe active fold slot remains the only structure consulted in IF: same one tag\\ncompare, same cached target instruction injection, same sequential\\n`io_imemAddr` path, and no new multi-entry select logic on the live fetch\\ncone.\\n\\nWhen EX resolves a taken backward branch that does not match the active slot,\\ntrain it first into the challenger. Only if that challenger repeats does it\\nget promoted into the active fold slot. This attacks the likely one-slot\\naliasing problem across CoreMark's list, matrix, and state loops without\\nrepeating the two-entry fetch-lookup regression. In effect, hit-rate\\nimprovement moves into EX-time training policy while IF timing stays at the\\none-slot fold-buffer complexity that already proved safe.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add minimal fold-predictor sideband fields so a folded branch can carry active-slot metadata from IF through EX without changing RVFI-visible state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep a single active backedge fold lookup on the fetch path, inject the cached target instruction on active hits, and maintain a shadow challenger record that is never consulted in the live PC path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fold sideband alongside the decoded instruction so EX can distinguish active-slot predictions from ordinary sequential fetches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train taken backward branches into active and challenger slots, bump challenger confidence on repeats, and promote only repeated challengers into the active fold slot while keeping EX as the architectural source of truth for redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor training, promotion, and fold sideband signals between IF and EX without changing the top-level nret=1 contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add minimal fold-predictor sideband fields so a folded branch can carry active-slot metadata from IF through EX without changing RVFI-visible state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep a single active backedge fold lookup on the fetch path, inject the cached target instruction on active hits, and maintain a shadow challenger record that is never consulted in the live PC path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fold sideband alongside the decoded instruction so EX can distinguish active-slot predictions from ordinary sequential fetches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train taken backward branches into active and challenger slots, bump challenger confidence on repeats, and promote only repeated challengers into the active fold slot while keeping EX as the architectural source of truth for redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor training, promotion, and fold sideband signals between IF and EX without changing the top-level nret=1 contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r12s2 (broken, n/a): On `bench`, backedge fold injection cannot safely split `redirect` from `flush_redirect` on the combinational IF/ID path unless the cached target instruction sits in a real accepted entry, because advancing the PC to `target+4` while the target word is still only an injected side value makes stalls/flushes correctness-critical and can drop control flow.\"}\n40:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r13s2\", \"title\": \"Accepted-History Backedge Fold Slot\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Predictor work on `bench` has almost no safe frontend budget: ID redirects,\\nBTB-style target lookup, and loop streaming all lost more Fmax than they\\ngained IPC. The only predictor shape that stayed competitive was the\\none-slot backedge fold buffer because it kept `io_imemAddr` on the existing\\nsequential path. Its remaining weakness is fill latency: the slot only\\nbecomes useful after the target instruction is fetched again\\narchitecturally, so the first observed taken backedge and any iStall-delayed\\nrefill still pay full bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Predictor work on `bench` has almost no safe frontend budget: ID redirects,\\nBTB-style target lookup, and loop streaming all lost more Fmax than they\\ngained IPC. The only predictor shape that stayed competitive was the\\none-slot backedge fold buffer because it kept `io_imemAddr` on the existing\\nsequential path. Its remaining weakness is fill latency: the slot only\\nbecomes useful after the target instruction is fetched again\\narchitecturally, so the first observed taken backedge and any iStall-delayed\\nrefill still pay full bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the single active backedge fold slot and the sequential `io_imemAddr`\\npath, but train the slot from a tiny recent accepted-fetch history instead\\nof waiting for a post-redirect refetch of the target word. When EX resolves\\na taken backward branch, search the last few architecturally accepted\\n`(pc, instr)` pairs; if the target PC is present, snapshot that real\\ninstruction immediately into the fold slot and mark it usable for the next\\nloop iteration. Fall back to the old delayed fill only on a history miss.\\n\\nThis stays inside the only predictor shape that has been timing-safe on\\n`bench`: one lookup entry in IF, no extra target mux on the live fetch cone,\\nand no multi-entry select logic. It directly attacks the remaining warm-up\\nand refill misses for CoreMark's tight backedges while avoiding the unsafe\\n\\\"injected side value with no accepted backing entry\\\" behavior called out by\\nthe last broken fold experiment.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add fold-prediction sideband fields and a compact recent-fetch history record type for a single-slot backedge fold predictor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep the sequential PC path, record a tiny history of architecturally accepted fetch `(pc, instr)` pairs, and expose the active fold slot plus history data for training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch fold-hit metadata alongside the instruction so EX can validate or repair folded backedge predictions without re-decoding predictor state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train taken backward branches from the accepted-fetch history, fall back to delayed fill on history miss, and keep EX as the architectural source of truth for redirect and trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the recent-fetch-history and fold-training signals between IF and EX while preserving the existing RVFI and bus contracts.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add regression tests for repeated taken backedges, history-seeded fold fill, and stall/flush interactions so no wrong-path retirement leaks through prediction.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add fold-prediction sideband fields and a compact recent-fetch history record type for a single-slot backedge fold predictor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep the sequential PC path, record a tiny history of architecturally accepted fetch `(pc, instr)` pairs, and expose the active fold slot plus history data for training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch fold-hit metadata alongside the instruction so EX can validate or repair folded backedge predictions without re-decoding predictor state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train taken backward branches from the accepted-fetch history, fall back to delayed fill on history miss, and keep EX as the architectural source of truth for r