hesis\": \"Keep the fetch-time predictor lookup exactly one entry wide and preserve the\\nexisting fold-buffer shape: one backedge slot, one tag compare, sequential\\n`io_imemAddr`, and target-instruction injection only after a proven taken\\nbackward branch has been trained. Do not add a second lookup entry, earlier\\ntarget fill, or any new redirect mux on the live fetch cone.\\n\\nInstead, change only the EX-time replacement policy. Give the active fold\\nslot a tiny saturating confidence counter. Matching taken backedges refresh\\nthe slot and raise confidence; a different taken backedge does not evict the\\nactive slot immediately, but first decays that confidence and only replaces\\nthe slot once the current entry has gone cold. This should reduce one-slot\\nthrash across CoreMark's multiple kernels while staying well inside the only\\npredictor shape that has not hurt Fmax on this core.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep the single-slot fold/inject fetch path, but add a tiny confidence counter and sticky replacement logic while preserving sequential `io_imemAddr` generation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify taken backward branches for training and emit saturating refresh/decay/replace updates instead of unconditionally overwriting the active fold slot.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the minimal fold-prediction sideband metadata needed to carry a folded-branch marker through the pipeline without changing the RVFI-visible architectural fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fold sideband through ID/EX so EX can distinguish predicted-folded branches from ordinary control flow when applying repair and training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the one-slot fold predictor update path between EX and IF while keeping the top-level memory and RVFI contract unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline tests that alternate hot and cold backedges to verify sticky replacement, correct redirect repair on loop exit, and strict RVFI PC/order behavior under stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep the single-slot fold/inject fetch path, but add a tiny confidence counter and sticky replacement logic while preserving sequential `io_imemAddr` generation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify taken backward branches for training and emit saturating refresh/decay/replace updates instead of unconditionally overwriting the active fold slot.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the minimal fold-prediction sideband metadata needed to carry a folded-branch marker through the pipeline without changing the RVFI-visible architectural fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the fold sideband through ID/EX so EX can distinguish predicted-folded branches from ordinary control flow when applying repair and training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the one-slot fold predictor update path between EX and IF while keeping the top-level memory and RVFI contract unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline tests that alternate hot and cold backedges to verify sticky replacement, correct redirect repair on loop exit, and strict RVFI PC/order behavior under stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 179.15, \"delta_pct\": -59.96, \"vs_baseline\": -36.66, \"fmax_mhz\": 76.69, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4280712, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6165, \"ff\": 2424, \"seeds\": [76.69, 74.67, 77.3], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T21:53:06.206284Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r14s2 (regression, -59.96%): On `bench`, predictor headroom is not in smarter one-slot fold replacement either: keeping IF lookup one-entry wide but adding sticky `fold_slot_conf`/`fold_update_op` retention and `predicted_*` repair plumbing costs more Fmax than CoreMark recovers from reducing occasional backedge-slot thrash.\"}\n","exit":0,"description":"Show later predictor experiment entries","truncated":false},"title":"Show later predictor experiment entries","time":{"start":1778882265948,"end":1778882265951}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0c63beade09a0b26016a0796d9b7bc81989d608623f1a25322"}},"id":"prt_e2da542ee001HHojaDl76WY3Bo","sessionID":"ses_1d25b7dd1ffePyQ2UXCo1NepoO","messageID":"msg_e2da4f5fd001RwJ8vgR5U0Knvm"}}
