{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778882437151,"sessionID":"ses_1d25b7dd1ffePyQ2UXCo1NepoO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_1kRFbcs1JjntcXSUwArXGGzk","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r15s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r15s2\n+title: \"Redirect-Hit Target Word Cache\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Predictor work on `bench` has mostly failed when it touched the live\n+  `pc -> next_pc` cone or carried fold-repair metadata through IF/ID/EX.\n+  The core still burns a guaranteed bubble after every taken redirect,\n+  though, because `if_stage` forces NOP on the redirect cycle even when the\n+  target word is hot and was fetched before. The most promising remaining\n+  predictor angle is therefore one that only does work after EX has already\n+  made the architectural redirect decision.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a one-entry redirect-target word cache that is trained from real,\n+  architecturally accepted target fetches and consulted only when EX already\n+  asserts `redirect`. On a cache hit, `if_stage` injects the cached target\n+  instruction into IF/ID on that same redirect cycle and advances the PC to\n+  `redirect_target + 4`; on a miss, the core keeps the existing\n+  bubble-and-refetch behavior.\n+\n+  This is intentionally narrower than the failed fold and BTB-style ideas.\n+  There is no predictor lookup on ordinary fetches, no predicted-next-PC\n+  metadata carried through the pipeline, and no mispredict recovery path\n+  beyond the existing EX redirect. A small invalidation path for stores that\n+  hit the cached word keeps self-modifying cases safe while repeated\n+  CoreMark backedges and calls can reclaim one taken-control bubble and\n+  some redirect-time iStall exposure with much less Fmax risk.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: low\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a one-entry redirect-target cache that fills from accepted target fetches and, on a repeated redirect hit, injects the cached target instruction while keeping the normal sequential fetch path unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire ID-stage accept/hold information and store-word invalidation signals into `if_stage` so redirect-hit injection only happens when the target instruction will really be latched.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Expose a narrow invalidation event for stores that touch the cached target word, including deferred-store cases, so redirect injection never uses stale instruction data.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add pipeline tests for repeated taken redirects, redirect-hit injection under `io_imemReady=0`, and same-word store invalidation so RVFI order and PC sequencing remain correct.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r15s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r15s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r15s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r15s2.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r15s2\n+title: \"Redirect-Hit Target Word Cache\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Predictor work on `bench` has mostly failed when it touched the live\n+  `pc -> next_pc` cone or carried fold-repair metadata through IF/ID/EX.\n+  The core still burns a guaranteed bubble after every taken redirect,\n+  th