{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778835313061,"sessionID":"ses_1d529263affeANfCjt74fFVOMY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_7KOWL9phMC6KedBJBbiiKOjM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\n+title: \"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire an ID-stage prediction path into IF and route EX-stage mispredict recovery into hazard control.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Update the PC from a predicted-taken branch or JAL in ID while keeping EX recovery as the highest-priority redirect.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute a static backward-taken/forward-not-taken decision and early BRANCH/JAL target for speculative fetch.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Recompute the real branch or jump outcome and request a flush only when the static prediction was wrong.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Turn redirect flushing into mispredict-only recovery so correct predictions do not inject bubbles.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add coverage for predicted-taken control flow and recovery from a deliberately wrong static branch prediction.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\n+title: \"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire an ID-stage prediction path into IF and route EX-stage mispredict recovery into hazard control.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Update the PC from a predicted-taken branch or JAL in ID while keeping EX recovery as the highest-priority redirect.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute a static backward-taken/forward-not-taken decision and early BRANCH/JAL target for speculative fetch.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Recompute the real branch or jump outcome and request a flush only when the static prediction was wrong.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Turn redirect flushing into mispredict-only recovery so correct predictions do not inject bubbles.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add coverage for predicted-taken control flow and recovery from a deliberately wrong static branch prediction.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\n+title: \"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire an ID-stage prediction path into IF and route EX-stage mispredict recovery into hazard control.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Update the PC from a predicted-taken branch or JAL in ID while keeping EX recovery as the highest-priority redirect.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compute a static backward-taken/forward-not-taken decision and early BRANCH/JAL target for speculative fetch.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Recompute the real branch or jump outcome and request a flush only when the static prediction was wrong.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Turn redirect flushing into mispredict-only recovery so correct predictions do not inject bubbles.\"\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n+    description: \"Add coverage for predicted-taken control flow and recovery from a deliberately wrong static branch prediction.\"\n","additions":23,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778835313056,"end":1778835313060}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0625d47cf673c96f016a06df675698819ab7847f2f8e6c4085"}},"id":"prt_e2ad8ac01001c5sgRIfkZtOzlc","sessionID":"ses_1d529263affeANfCjt74fFVO