{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778835317725,"sessionID":"ses_1d529263affeANfCjt74fFVOMY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_mTiJ2bMLS2ptRY0zR2p0SyNU","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\n2: title: \"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\"\n3: category: predictor\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\n6: hypothesis: |\n7:   Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\n8: expected_impact:\n9:   fitness_delta_pct: 8\n10:   confidence: medium\n11: changes:\n12:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n13:     description: \"Wire an ID-stage prediction path into IF and route EX-stage mispredict recovery into hazard control.\"\n14:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n15:     description: \"Update the PC from a predicted-taken branch or JAL in ID while keeping EX recovery as the highest-priority redirect.\"\n16:   - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n17:     description: \"Compute a static backward-taken/forward-not-taken decision and early BRANCH/JAL target for speculative fetch.\"\n18:   - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n19:     description: \"Recompute the real branch or jump outcome and request a flush only when the static prediction was wrong.\"\n20:   - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n21:     description: \"Turn redirect flushing into mispredict-only recovery so correct predictions do not inject bubbles.\"\n22:   - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n23:     description: \"Add coverage for predicted-taken control flow and recovery from a deliberately wrong static branch prediction.\"\n\n(End of file - total 23 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Static BTFNT branch predictor with ID redirect\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current bench core resolves every branch and jump in EX and flushes on every taken redirect. CoreMark is loop-heavy, so repeatedly paying that taken-branch penalty burns IPC. LUT headroom is tight, which makes a low-state predictor more attractive than a larger dynamic structure.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a decode-stage backward-taken/forward-not-taken predictor for conditional branches and always predict JAL taken, driving a speculative next PC from ID into IF. EX remains the architectural source of truth for branch direction and target, but only flushes and recovers on a mispredict. This should remove most loop-backedge and JAL bubbles in CoreMark while staying much lighter than a tagged BTB/BHT, limiting Fmax and LUT risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire an ID-stage prediction path into IF and route EX-stage mispredict recovery into hazard control.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Update the PC from a predicted-taken branch or JAL in ID while keeping EX recovery as the highest-priority redirect.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute a static backward-taken/forward-not-taken decision and early BRANCH/JAL target for speculative fetch.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recompute the real branch or jump outcome and request a flush only when the static prediction was wrong.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r1s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778835317719,"end":1778835317724}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_082c7a20422242a8016a06df755f148198b2726891292489c9"}},"id":"prt_e2ad8e335001c3LjNMS6ZNCa2D","sessionID":"ses_1d529263affeANfCjt74fFVOMY","messageID":"msg_e2ad8d2e80012J2njrhOyw2xbV"}}
