{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778836924880,"sessionID":"ses_1d5111418ffeMqrGFIyxKLZkLg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Q3sfs2SZjB3AnaXsHkV9oJtS","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-001-r2s0\n2: title: \"RTL-only hot/cold ALU opcode split\"\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The current best bench result already removed DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU from the\n6:   hot one-cycle EX path, but `rtl/alu.sv` still uses a dense ALU-op encoding\n7:   and one broad result case covering common RV32I work, multiply results, and\n8:   dummy divide-class outputs. That leaves the always-hot ADD/address/compare/\n9:   shift path sharing decode and mux structure with cold M-extension cases.\n10: \n11:   A sibling-core experiment on `cores/v1` showed that this specific RTL-only\n12:   reshaping can improve fitness, while more aggressive multiplier rewrites and\n13:   source-qualified hazard logic either regressed or broke. That makes the ALU\n14:   mux shape the best-supported remaining `micro_opt` angle for the frozen\n15:   bench fixture.\n16: hypothesis: |\n17:   Re-encode the ALU operation constants so bit 4 cleanly marks RV32M\n18:   operations, with MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU/DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU grouped as a cold\n19:   `op[4]=1` class while the common RV32I/simple operations stay in the hot\n20:   `op[4]=0` class. Then refactor `rtl/alu.sv` into two local result muxes:\n21:   a simple-result mux for ADD/SUB/logic/compare/shift/LUI and an M-result mux\n22:   for multiply plus the existing placeholder divide outputs used when the real\n23:   divider lives in `rtl/div_unit.sv`.\n24: \n25:   This keeps the pipeline, RVFI contract, divider protocol, and CoreMark\n26:   cycle behavior unchanged while giving synthesis a shallower common EX result\n27:   select on the instructions that dominate CoreMark. The expected gain is\n28:   mainly Fmax, not IPC, which fits the post-divider state of `cores/bench`.\n29: expected_impact:\n30:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n31:   confidence: medium\n32: changes:\n33:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n34:     description: \"Re-encode ALU op localparams so RV32M ops occupy a cold `op[4]=1` class without changing architectural meaning.\"\n35:   - file: rtl/alu.sv\n36:     description: \"Split the broad ALU result case into separate hot RV32I and cold RV32M result muxes, selecting the final output with the new hot/cold opcode bit.\"\n\n(End of file - total 36 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-001-r2s0\ntitle: \"RTL-only hot/cold ALU opcode split\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current best bench result already removed DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU from the\n  hot one-cycle EX path, but `rtl/alu.sv` still uses a dense ALU-op encoding\n  and one broad result case covering common RV32I work, multiply results, and\n  dummy divide-class outputs. That leaves the always-hot ADD/address/compare/\n  shift path sharing decode and mux structure with cold M-extension cases.\n\n  A sibling-core experiment on `cores/v1` showed that this specific RTL-only\n  reshaping can improve fitness, while more aggressive multiplier rewrites and\n  source-qualified hazard logic either regressed or broke. That makes the ALU\n  mux shape the best-supported remaining `micro_opt` angle for the frozen\n  bench fixture.\nhypothesis: |\n  Re-encode the ALU operation constants so bit 4 cleanly marks RV32M\n  operations, with MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU/DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU grouped as a cold\n  `op[4]=1` class while the common RV32I/simple operations stay in the hot\n  `op[4]=0` class. Then refactor `rtl/alu.sv` into two local result muxes:","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r2s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778836924867,"end":1778836924878}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_000cce70edee657b016a06e5bc89648199acc1af1ec84d9b02"}},"id":"prt_e2af168fa001PsdnyXFLRoNTeF","sessionID":"ses_1d5111418ffeMqrGFIyxKLZkLg","messageID":"msg_e2af1572f00124TfCJmqiynDrv"}}
