{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778862642164,"sessionID":"ses_1d38f39a0ffeX2wiAJx0ZaPdZq","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_6m9E4WiVBdfEjNrUkffVd0VM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r6s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r6s2\n+title: \"Single-Slot Backedge Branch Fold Buffer\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Every predictor attempt on `bench` that touched the frontend `pc -> next_pc`\n+  cone regressed: ID-stage BTFNT added decode and target-generation delay, and\n+  even tiny taken-target caches still paid too much tag-compare and target-mux\n+  cost in IF. But CoreMark remains dominated by tight taken loop backedges, so\n+  always waiting for EX to redirect still leaves repeatable control bubbles on\n+  the table.\n+\n+  The best remaining predictor angle is therefore one that predicts only the\n+  hottest already-seen backedge while leaving `io_imemAddr` generation on its\n+  current simple sequential path.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a one-entry EX-trained branch-fold buffer for taken backward conditional\n+  branches. When EX resolves a taken backedge, record the branch PC and target\n+  PC, then capture the target instruction the next time that target is fetched\n+  architecturally. On a later hit for the same branch PC, keep the normal\n+  sequential fetch address path, but tag the branch as predicted-taken and\n+  inject the cached target instruction/PC into IF->ID on the following cycle\n+  instead of the wrong-path fallthrough word.\n+\n+  EX remains the architectural source of truth. A correct prediction repairs\n+  the fetch PC to `target + 4` after the folded target has already entered the\n+  pipe, while a loop-exit miss or stale slot falls back to the existing flush\n+  and redirect behavior. This tries to recover one taken-branch bubble in the\n+  CoreMark hot loops without reintroducing the Fmax loss from putting target\n+  selection directly on the fetch-address critical path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: low\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add the minimal fold-prediction metadata that must travel with an in-flight branch and a folded target instruction.\" \n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire fold-buffer train, hit, and repair signals between IF, EX, and hazard control without changing the top-level IO contract.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Implement a one-entry backedge fold buffer that caches branch PC, target PC, and target instruction, and injects the cached target into IF->ID while leaving `io_imemAddr` on the normal sequential path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the fold-hit metadata alongside the branch so EX can tell whether the younger target instruction was injected speculatively.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Train the buffer from resolved taken backward branches and convert redirect handling into fold success, stale-slot repair, or loop-exit mispredict recovery.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Adjust flush logic so a correctly folded target survives branch resolution while wrong-path or stale folded instructions are still killed safely.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r6s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r6s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r6s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-