vel with an in-flight branch and a folded target instruction.\" \n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire fold-buffer train, hit, and repair signals between IF, EX, and hazard control without changing the top-level IO contract.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Implement a one-entry backedge fold buffer that caches branch PC, target PC, and target instruction, and injects the cached target into IF->ID while leaving `io_imemAddr` on the normal sequential path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the fold-hit metadata alongside the branch so EX can tell whether the younger target instruction was injected speculatively.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Train the buffer from resolved taken backward branches and convert redirect handling into fold success, stale-slot repair, or loop-exit mispredict recovery.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Adjust flush logic so a correctly folded target survives branch resolution while wrong-path or stale folded instructions are still killed safely.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r6s2.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r6s2.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r6s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r6s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r6s2.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r6s2\n+title: \"Single-Slot Backedge Branch Fold Buffer\"\n+category: predictor\n+moti