{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778869476755,"sessionID":"ses_1d32164c8ffeUUlKe8QCUYu3PB","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_OpYNDcmyEg1Lw4VCjhtHQkO7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r8s2\n+title: \"One-Entry Short-Loop Stream Predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Every prior `bench` predictor that touched the live fetch `pc -> next_pc`\n+  decision regressed, which says the remaining predictor win cannot be another\n+  per-fetch target compare or ID-stage redirect. CoreMark is still dominated by\n+  tiny hot counted loops under random `io_imemReady` stalls, so the best\n+  remaining opportunity is to amortize predictor cost across several loop-body\n+  instructions instead of paying it every taken branch.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a one-entry EX-trained short-loop stream buffer for small taken backward\n+  conditional branches. When EX resolves a taken backedge whose target-to-branch\n+  span is small (for example `<= 4` instructions), capture the loop start PC,\n+  branch PC, and the sequential instructions in that window into a registered\n+  buffer. On a later hit at the loop entry, IF enters a local stream mode and\n+  sources the buffered instructions for the predicted-taken iterations instead of\n+  re-fetching them from imem one by one.\n+\n+  This keeps EX as the architectural source of truth and avoids the proven bad\n+  path of same-cycle frontend target generation. Compared with the earlier\n+  single-branch predictors, it can hide both the taken-backedge bubble and\n+  random imem stall bubbles across the whole buffered loop body, so one entry\n+  may repay its control cost better than another fetch-path BTB or fold slot.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: low\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add minimal pipeline metadata for loop-stream provenance and buffered-instruction position.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Implement the one-entry short-loop instruction buffer, loop-entry hit detection, and local stream-mode instruction source selection without changing the top-level IO contract.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch loop-stream metadata alongside PC and instruction so downstream stages can validate or recover predictions precisely.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Train the buffer from resolved taken backward branches, verify streamed iterations against architectural control flow, and request recovery on loop exit or mismatch.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire predictor train, stream-hit, and recovery signals between IF, ID, EX, and the existing redirect path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Treat loop-stream recovery like a redirect and ensure stalls flush or cancel speculative buffered issue cleanly.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r8s2\n+title: \"One-Entry Short-Loop Stream Predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Every prior `bench` predictor that touched the live fetch `pc -> next_pc`\n+  decision regressed, which says the rem