{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778871084020,"sessionID":"ses_1d308243bffeiqTNPiFD1doV7T","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_YDLdi235SfrnUzFF3ojq9PkX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r9s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r9s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-001-r9s0\n2: title: \"Shared RV32M Multiply Datapath\"\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The current `bench` core already found its two big wins by removing costly\n6:   control and divider work from the always-hot paths, while later fetch-side\n7:   predictors and MEM-side queue refinements mostly regressed or failed\n8:   placement. One localized datapath cost still stands out in `rtl/alu.sv`:\n9:   the real build computes three separate 64-bit products (`mul_ss`, `mul_uu`,\n10:   `mul_su`) just to serve the four MUL-family instructions.\n11: \n12:   CoreMark does use multiply in hot code, so turning MUL into a multi-cycle\n13:   path would likely hurt IPC. A better micro-opt is to keep one-cycle RV32M\n14:   latency but remove redundant multiplier hardware and mux fanout from the EX\n15:   datapath.\n16: hypothesis: |\n17:   Replace the three parallel MUL-family product trees in `rtl/alu.sv` with a\n18:   single shared sign-configurable multiplier. Use one 33x33 extended product\n19:   whose extra sign bits are selected from the opcode so the same result can\n20:   produce `MUL`, `MULH`, `MULHU`, and `MULHSU`: low 32 bits for `MUL`, high\n21:   32 bits for the three high-half variants, with the existing ALTOPS branch\n22:   left unchanged.\n23: \n24:   This keeps the pipeline, hazards, RVFI retirement behavior, and CoreMark\n25:   cycle count unchanged while reducing redundant DSP/LUT usage and routing\n26:   pressure inside the hot EX datapath. Relative to prior failed micro-opts,\n27:   it does not add frontend prediction, store-slot control, or late-source\n28:   bookkeeping; it is a narrow Fmax-focused cleanup with lower correctness\n29:   surface area than another hazard relaxation.\n30: expected_impact:\n31:   fitness_delta_pct: 6\n32:   confidence: medium\n33: changes:\n34:   - file: rtl/alu.sv\n35:     description: \"Replace the current `mul_ss`/`mul_uu`/`mul_su` triple-product implementation with one shared sign-configurable multiplier and select the correct low or high half per RV32M op while preserving the existing ALTOPS cases.\"\n36:   - file: test/test_alu.py\n37:     description: \"Strengthen MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU coverage with signedness-focused edge vectors so the shared multiplier rewrite is pinned to exact RV32M bit results.\"\n\n(End of file - total 37 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-001-r9s0\ntitle: \"Shared RV32M Multiply Datapath\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current `bench` core already found its two big wins by removing costly\n  control and divider work from the always-hot paths, while later fetch-side\n  predictors and MEM-side queue refinements mostly regressed or failed\n  placement. One localized datapath cost still stands out in `rtl/alu.sv`:\n  the real build computes three separate 64-bit products (`mul_ss`, `mul_uu`,\n  `mul_su`) just to serve the four MUL-family instructions.\n\n  CoreMark does use multiply in hot code, so turning MUL into a multi-cycle\n  path would likely hurt IPC. A better micro-opt is to keep one-cycle RV32M\n  latency but remove redundant multiplier hardware and mux fanout from the EX\n  datapath.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the three parallel MUL-family product trees in `rtl/alu.sv` with a\n  single shared sign-configurable multiplier. Use one 33x33 extended product\n  whose extra sign bits are selected from the opcode so the same result can\n  produce `MUL`, `MULH`, `MULHU`, and `MULHSU`: low 32 bits for `MUL`, high","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r9s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778871084016,"end":1778871084020}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0681f0a9cdcfbdf7016a076b2b7f58819abc2453177a32e57c"}},"id":"prt_e2cfaa256001608sfPXCUHomLl","sessionID":"ses_1d308243bffeiqTNPiFD1doV7T","messageID":"msg_e2cfa92f9001QMaHmEnDpv5FFZ"}}
